	chapter_group.0B67406B7FAC80B7.title: "Collections"
	chapter_group.1F9C8D54B077CFBC.title: "Tips"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "The Route"
	quest.003FD72ED518BE70.quest_desc: [
		"You’ll notice each wire has its own &eMax Amperage&r — that’s the amount of amps a cable can safely carry before burning."
		"To know how many amps will flow through a cable, you must consider two things:"
		""
		"- A Generator or Battery outputs a specific amount of Amps:"
		"Battery Buffers will output as many amps as they have batteries inside."
		"Every single-block generator outputs &e1A&r."
		"For multiblock generators, it depends on the &aDynamo Energy Hatch&r — the value is shown in its tooltip."
		""
		"Amperage output is also based on what is needed: each machine connected to a power line will request amps to fill its internal buffer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Let’s look at an example:"
		"You have &e6 machines&r connected to an &e8x Battery Buffer&r filled with 8 batteries."
		"The buffer will try to send &e1A&r to each machine — that’s &e6A&r total."
		"The amps are delivered in order: the closest machines get power first, and the furthest ones last."
		"If your cables only support &c4A&r, they’ll &cBURN&r. You’ll need &a8A cables&r in this case."
		""
		"&bTip:&r The first machine in the line might need a cable that handles &e8A&r,"
		"but the last machine may only need &e1A&r, as it’s only receiving what’s left."
		"&c⚠ Be careful:&r adding another machine at the end could cause the cable to burn if it exceeds the limit."
	]
	quest.003FD72ED518BE70.quest_subtitle: "It burns?"
	quest.003FD72ED518BE70.title: "Managing Amp"
	quest.0065A82458288853.quest_desc: [
		"A brass plate on a copper block. Like a Create steam engine it sits on a heated, watered fluid-tank boiler, and vents the steam into the balloon above: another way to lift."
	]
	quest.0065A82458288853.quest_subtitle: "Optional"
	quest.0065A82458288853.title: "Steam Lift"
	quest.00695D396C7FED88.quest_desc: [
		"Refine the bloom on the anvil. In this pack every iron ingot, plate and rod is TFC wrought iron."
	]
	quest.00695D396C7FED88.quest_subtitle: "Iron means wrought iron"
	quest.00695D396C7FED88.title: "Wrought Iron"
	quest.00BAF81D5528D7A2.quest_desc: [
		"Lead is used in &7LV&r+ to make soldering alloy and battery alloy."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here, so lead is a byproduct of TFC native silver: macerating or washing crushed silver ore gives lead dust."
	]
	quest.00BAF81D5528D7A2.quest_subtitle: "Element #82"
	quest.00BAF81D5528D7A2.title: "Lead"
	quest.012DC6D84EA3796D.quest_desc: [
		"Make this machine when you feel like it's time you invested into Batteries."
	]
	quest.012DC6D84EA3796D.quest_subtitle: "This machine does nothing exciting"
	quest.012DC6D84EA3796D.title: "Basic Canner"
	quest.015E23526315B229.quest_desc: [
		"Purified sphalerite and purified galena, with sulfuric acid in a mixer, give indium concentrate; an EV chemical reactor with aluminium turns the concentrate into indium dust. Galena only comes from the vents."
		""
		"Indium makes indium gallium phosphide, and the IV circuits and wafers that use it."
	]
	quest.015E23526315B229.quest_subtitle: "Zinc and lead, together"
	quest.015E23526315B229.title: "Indium"
	quest.01660AE825F50880.quest_desc: [
		"Neodymium makes the magnetic rods of &5EV&r and &9IV&r electric motors."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aCassiterite&r gives &aMonazite&r as its &3Ore Washer&r by-product. An &3Electrolyzer&r splits monazite dust into rare earth and phosphate, and a &3Centrifuge&r separates rare earth into small piles of cadmium, neodymium, samarium, cerium, yttrium and lanthanum."
	]
	quest.01660AE825F50880.quest_subtitle: "Element #60"
	quest.01660AE825F50880.title: "Neodymium"
	quest.01A6CA9A337188A3.quest_desc: [
		"Unfortunately, this is only an &lEmpty&r Spray Can, which you have to fill with Dye before using."
		""
		"Any (or almost any) GregTech tile entity (machine, pipe, cable...) can be &6painted&r to one of the 16 colors of your choosing. This is great for screenshots, or to separate different setups for convenience in a Multiplayer base. They also help with distinguishing between pipelines and cables."
		""
		"Holding the &aSpray Can&r in the offhand will automatically paint any block you place."
		""
		"While this may not be immediately useful in &6LV&r, you can also paint Input and Output Buses and Hatches in matching colors to effectively \"group\" them together, ensuring recipe ingredients are kept separated if you're trying to use a single multiblock to do multiple recipes."
	]
	quest.01A6CA9A337188A3.quest_subtitle: "Time for server tag wars"
	quest.01A6CA9A337188A3.title: "Spray Can"
	quest.01F0503DA2852C96.quest_desc: [
		"Electricity comes from boiler steam: feed an LV steam turbine from your boilers and cable it to your machines."
		""
		"The turbine turns &d2 mB of steam into 1 EU&r: 64 mB a tick for 32 EU/t. Steam isn't energy-dense, so plan on plenty of boilers and wide pipes."
		""
		"When single boilers can't keep up, a &6Large Bronze Boiler&r (LV circuits, tin cables and a bronze firebox casing) burns solid fuels, lava or creosote."
	]
	quest.01F0503DA2852C96.quest_subtitle: "Electricity"
	quest.01F0503DA2852C96.title: "Steam Turbine"
	quest.02A40DBFA00DFDA7.quest_desc: [
		"A deployer is a mechanical hand: it uses whatever it holds on the block or item in front of it. Create's sequenced assembly runs on deployers; that's how precision mechanisms and train tracks are made."
		""
		"While you could get by with a single deployer, we &3really&r don't recommend it. Setting up a line of deployers along a belt will save heaps of time and sanity."
		""
		"Airship envelopes also cost fewer brass nuggets when a deployer makes them."
	]
	quest.02A40DBFA00DFDA7.quest_subtitle: "Primitive Assembly Line"
	quest.02A40DBFA00DFDA7.title: "Deployers"
	quest.02A8A31D3FC17775.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Pyrolyse Oven&r is an electric equivalent to the &3Coke Oven&r. It turns logs into &9Charcoal&r and coal into &9Coke&r with a &9Creosote&r byproduct just as before, but with other circuits it gives other &6Organic Byproducts&r, the most useful of these being &aWood Tar&r."
		""
		"It also turns &aBio Chaff&r into &aBiomass&r, which is more pertinent for your progression right now."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The byproducts can be distilled into an array of organic resources, with &odifferent&r byproducts giving &odifferent&r ratios of &odifferent&r chemicals."
		""
		"Take a peek at the &9Distillery&r Quest to get to grips with the power of distillation..."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Some recipes accept &bNitrogen&r to run faster. This isn't quite worth pursuing right now."
		""
		"Its basic recipes need &d64 EU/t&r, which a single &7LV&r Energy Hatch supplies. &3Cupronickel Coils&r are fine while you get used to it, but they run it 25 percent slower than &bKanthal&r, and every coil after Kanthal makes it faster."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9&lNote:&r&l The plant path is one way to &9&lEthylene&r&l, which you need for your first plastic on the way to &6HV&r&l. The other path involves Oil.&r"
		""
		"The Pyrolyse Oven remains &doptional&r. However, it is very rewarding to build one, either for Power or for its Byproducts, and a tree farm keeps it fed."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In GT5u, the structure for the Pyrolyse Oven was infamously a giant box with only 9 coils inside. Players usually spent several minutes debugging what was wrong due to the lack of a preview."
	]
	quest.02A8A31D3FC17775.quest_subtitle: "Thermal Decomposition"
	quest.02A8A31D3FC17775.title: "Pyrolyse Oven"
	quest.03AA7F3789D020D9.quest_desc: [
		"You're going to want to use the &3LCR&r recipe for your first &aEpichlorohydrin&r."
		""
		"This recipe requires &aPropene&r, which means that &dOil Processing&r and &dFuel Cracking&r are now necessary ventures. We're truly sorry if you've been dragging your heels!"
		""
		"It's quite important that you make your first &3Distillation Tower&r before progressing to the right."
		""
		"Last of all, if you haven't noticed, you can loop the &dSalt Water&r byproduct to bootstrap the &dSodium Hydroxide&r."
	]
	quest.03AA7F3789D020D9.title: "Epichlorohydrin"
	quest.03C6FC1FF3C91355.quest_desc: [
		"Combine Crushed Ore with a GregTech hammer in a crafting grid to turn it into Impure Dust (TFC's hammers don't work for this). The macerator does the same, with a chance at a byproduct dust on top."
		""
		"Impure dust smelts into the same ingot as the crushed ore, but it can also be washed into clean dust (next quest). This may all be slow and tedious for now, but you'll soon unlock ways to do this faster and automatically!"
	]
	quest.03C6FC1FF3C91355.quest_subtitle: "Smash it with a hammer"
	quest.03C6FC1FF3C91355.title: "Early Ore Processing - Part 2"
	quest.03EA517012CF9B66.quest_desc: [
		"The macerator can sometimes yield different byproducts from your Purified ores than other routes, but these are still locked to &6HV&r like every other macerator byproduct."
	]
	quest.03EA517012CF9B66.quest_subtitle: "(again)"
	quest.03EA517012CF9B66.title: "The Macerator"
	quest.0444B1B9CCF2B737.quest_desc: [
		"Doping is the process of intentionally introducing impurities into semiconductors to alter their properties."
		""
		"&7Polysilicon&r can be doped with small amounts of &ePhosphorus&r to make a better &eSilicon Boule&r."
		""
		"Phosphorus-doped Silicon Boules typically yield &68 times&r more wafers than their non-doped counterparts. However, they are not strictly needed until &5EV&r, where they'll be used in more complex wafers."
		""
		"&9Note&r: Cutting Phosphorus Boules and engraving their Wafers require a &dCleanroom&r."
	]
	quest.0444B1B9CCF2B737.quest_subtitle: "That's dope, bro!"
	quest.0444B1B9CCF2B737.title: "Phosphorus Boules"
	quest.04462F0277710661.title: "Stone Age"
	quest.044A421FAF3D844D.quest_desc: [
		"Osmium comes at the end of the platinum line: TFC &aTetrahedrite&r's purified ore gives &aPlatinum Group Sludge&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r, and its later separation steps (follow EMI from the sludge) leave osmium."
	]
	quest.044A421FAF3D844D.quest_subtitle: "Element #76"
	quest.044A421FAF3D844D.title: "Osmium"
	quest.0465DCAC9F21A02A.quest_desc: [
		"The crucible sits on top of a charcoal forge (any heat source below works). It has 9 slots, holds 4000 mB of metal and shows your alloy ratios as you go. It keeps its contents when broken, and it also collects pig iron when placed below a blast furnace."
		""
		"Keep in mind that the crucible WILL try to alloy everything inside it - it does not keep metals separate like a TC Smeltery - so it's a good idea to keep it clean when you aren't using it."
	]
	quest.0465DCAC9F21A02A.quest_subtitle: "Melt metals like a pro"
	quest.0465DCAC9F21A02A.title: "Crucible"
	quest.050720D08A515699.quest_desc: [
		"&dSmall Vessels&r have 4 inventory slots while &6Large Vessels&r have 9! The &dSmall Vessel&r is not just for item storage: you can also melt ores and alloy basic metals in it."
		"The &6Large Vessel&r is a block, and once &3sealed&r it is great for preserving food."
		""
		"&l&9Tip:&r&o Food in a Small Vessel or a sealed Large Vessel gets the Preserved trait and lasts longer, and it won't attract the rats that raid food left in chests."
	]
	quest.050720D08A515699.quest_subtitle: "Clay can be quite useful"
	quest.050720D08A515699.title: "Large and Small Vessels"
	quest.052208FD56BA7EBB.quest_desc: [
		"Vanadium Steel (Vanadium, Chromium and Steel, mixed and then smelted in the EBF) is required in small quantities in progression: the &bMV&r Cutter's buzzsaw blade and the Fluid Drilling Rig's gears are made of it."
		""
		"It's also &6nearly four times as durable&r as Steel when used in GregTech tools."
	]
	quest.052208FD56BA7EBB.quest_subtitle: "Steel Your Heart"
	quest.052208FD56BA7EBB.title: "Steel Alloys"
	quest.0560BE2B9092FD80.quest_desc: [
		"Once you have leather, you will be able to get your first true armor. It isn't great, but it will provide that extra protection you may need. "
		""
		"They also give you a slight resistance to &6Slashing&r damage."
	]
	quest.0560BE2B9092FD80.quest_subtitle: "Clothes at last"
	quest.0560BE2B9092FD80.title: "Leather Armor"
	quest.057B715A2C3D0340.quest_desc: [
		"The &cGas Turbine&r works exactly like the other &6generators&r, but burns gases."
		""
		"At &7LV&r that means &7Methane&r: a Centrifuge gets 60 mB from every rubber log, along with sticky resin you need anyway. It won't power a factory alone, but a rubber tree farm keeps it going."
	]
	quest.057B715A2C3D0340.quest_subtitle: "For petrochemical enthusiasts"
	quest.057B715A2C3D0340.title: "The Gas Turbine"
	quest.05FC80F849E5E5F2.quest_desc: [
		"To get your grubby hands on some Titanium, &aRutile&r must first be reduced to &aTitanium Tetrachloride&r with Carbon and Chlorine in an &3HV Chemical Reactor&r, then reduced again in an &3EBF&r with &dMagnesium&r to finally arrive at Titanium. The ingots come out hot, so they need the &3Vacuum Freezer&r."
		""
		"The &dCarbon&r, &dChlorine&r, &dOxygen&r, and &dMagnesium&r can all be recovered: electrolyze the &dCarbon Monoxide&r back into Carbon and Oxygen, and react the &dMagnesium Chloride&r with Sodium in a Chemical Reactor for Magnesium and Salt, which electrolyzes back into Sodium and Chlorine. With that loop running, &athe only material&r that you'll need to provide for Titanium is &dRutile&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aTitanium Tetrachloride&r also acts as a catalyst in the &3Large Chemical Reactor&r's polymer recipes. A touch of &aTiCl₄&r can increase the polymer yield to &6133%%&r. Naturally, this is completely optional."
	]
	quest.05FC80F849E5E5F2.quest_subtitle: "Is it titanium yet?"
	quest.05FC80F849E5E5F2.title: "Almost Titanium²"
	quest.0601C96611FFB82E.quest_desc: [
		"Sulfur is used from the steam age on to vulcanize rubber, and in &7LV&r+ to make sulfuric acid."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC sulfur and pyrite ores, and as a byproduct of cinnabar, gypsum and sphalerite: electrolyzing sphalerite dust gives zinc and sulfur."
	]
	quest.0601C96611FFB82E.quest_subtitle: "Element #16"
	quest.0601C96611FFB82E.title: "Sulfur"
	quest.0635D73869211D86.quest_desc: [
		"Kaolin clay is found at high altitudes, in plateaus, old mountains, rolling hills and highlands, where the temperature is at least 18 °C and rainfall at least 300 mm. Blood lilies grow on it, so look out for them."
		""
		"TFC: Real World's climate follows the real Earth, so think warm, wet uplands, mostly in the tropics and subtropics. From a temperate start that is a long expedition: bring plenty of food and water, a boat if there's sea in the way, and storage for bringing home as much kaolin as you can."
	]
	quest.0635D73869211D86.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to the Jungle"
	quest.0635D73869211D86.title: "Kaolin Source: Overworld"
	quest.06858E14C61E1D7B.quest_desc: [
		"Have you heard about Overclocking, but don't really understand what it is? Let's take some time to explain it."
		""
		"We should start with the basics:"
		"&dLV&r represents a maximum of 32 EU/t — sometimes less, but never more."
		"&dMV&r goes up to 128 EU/t."
		"&dHV&r reaches 512 EU/t."
		"Basically, every tier is a 4x increase in power usage."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"What happens when you run a lower-tier recipe in a higher-tier machine? That's what we call &eOverclocking&r!"
		""
		"An &dMV&r recipe (33–128 EU/t) run in an &dHV&r machine will both: 1) Use 4x more energy, and 2) Be 2x faster."
		""
		"The same MV recipe in an &dEV&r machine? 16x the energy cost, but only 4x faster."
		""
		"As you can see, it's more power efficient to use multiple machines rather than overclocking a single one."
		"But let's be real: in most setups, you'll prefer overclocking to building a ton of the same machines."
		""
		"Still, it's good to know this early on, when energy is tight."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There's a special kind of overclocking exclusive to just a few multiblocks: &ePerfect Overclocking&r."
		"Here, instead of 4x energy for 2x speed, you get &a4x energy&r for &a4x speed&r! This makes it just as efficient as running multiple machines."
		""
		"The ones you'll meet:"
		"- Large Chemical Reactor, always"
		"- Electric Blast Furnace, when its coils run hot enough (see the Blast Overclocking quest)"
	]
	quest.06858E14C61E1D7B.quest_subtitle: "Basic upgrade mechanic"
	quest.06858E14C61E1D7B.title: "Overclock"
	quest.06941934630BB12E.quest_desc: [
		"Most grasses you find in the overworld can be harvested for Straw when broken with a Knife or Hoe. Straw has a number of uses for crafting, but you'll want at least 8 to create a Pit Kiln."
		""
		"Straw can also be crafted into Thatch, a simple building block that players and mobs pass right through, and two thatch blocks make a Thatch Bed."
	]
	quest.06941934630BB12E.quest_subtitle: "You can also use a Hoe if you want"
	quest.06941934630BB12E.title: "Gather Straw"
	quest.06C99D4DA23732A7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Face Mask&r will protect you from &cinhaling dangerous dust&r. It's &aeasy to craft&r, just paper and string, and worth wearing whenever you handle a powder with an inhalation hazard."
	]
	quest.06C99D4DA23732A7.title: "Face Mask"
	quest.06D9D74614BC03F5.quest_desc: [
		"Runs GregTech's alloy recipes on steam: red alloy from one copper and four redstone (grind cinnabar or cryolite in a TFC quern), rubber from raw rubber and sulfur."
		""
		"It also makes &6Bronze&r and &6Brass&r the effortless way: three copper and one tin or zinc, as ingots or dusts, give four ingots. No vessel, no watching temperatures."
		""
		"It's a steam-hungry machine. If you find yourself running out of steam, give a machine a &alove-tap&r with a &dSoft Mallet&r to pause it."
	]
	quest.06D9D74614BC03F5.quest_subtitle: "Red alloy and rubber"
	quest.06D9D74614BC03F5.title: "Steam Alloy Smelter"
	quest.074BBCBE5E87C0BB.quest_desc: [
		"While looking at &bEMI&r, you've probably noticed that your &dMacerator&r lists more &boutputs&r than what you're actually getting."
		""
		"GregTech doesn't communicate this very well, but these extra slots are only available in &6HV&r. Once you make it to that tier, the &6HV&r macerator becomes incredibly powerful, giving a huge amount of bonus byproducts when it grinds crushed and purified ores."
		""
		"TFC ore pieces have no byproducts at the first crush, in any machine."
	]
	quest.074BBCBE5E87C0BB.quest_subtitle: "I can get even more from my ores!"
	quest.074BBCBE5E87C0BB.title: "Crushing with byproducts"
	quest.077E55E82DC9119B.quest_desc: [
		"The &5EV Circuit Assembler&r won’t be of much use until you have a steady supply of &bNano CPU Wafers&r. Still, it will allow you to craft microprocessor circuits much faster and eventually give you access to your first &dLuV Circuits&r, which will be useful once you have an &1IV Assembler&r."
	]
	quest.077E55E82DC9119B.quest_subtitle: "Less useful than the Assembler for now"
	quest.077E55E82DC9119B.title: "The &5EV&r Circuit Assembler"
	quest.07C43A80E60B9C55.quest_desc: [
		"You may have realized that most &eMultiblocks&r require a &6Maintenance Hatch&r. Until &6HV&r, where you can get an &aAutomatic Maintenance Hatch&r, you can use this item to fix the hatch without needing to use all of your maintenance tools."
		""
		"It can be really useful if you don't want to invest in an &aAuto Maintenance Hatch&r yet, or if you're simply &cnot there yet&r."
	]
	quest.07C43A80E60B9C55.quest_subtitle: "If you can't fix it with this, use more of it!"
	quest.07C43A80E60B9C55.title: "Duct Tape"
	quest.07C81F40FBB9407D.quest_desc: [
		"Knap clay into a small vessel and ingot molds, then fire them in a pit kiln (straw and logs over the pottery, lit)."
		""
		"The vessel holds up to four items like a small bag (food inside keeps longer), but more importantly it's your first tool for working with metals: fill it with ore, fire it in a pit kiln to &lmelt&r the metal, then use it to pour into a mold. Its tooltip tells you what the ores inside will melt into, which is especially useful for alloys."
		""
		"Alloys need specific percentages of each metal. Copper is great right away, but you could make your very first metal tools from bronze instead."
	]
	quest.07C81F40FBB9407D.quest_subtitle: "A fired small vessel"
	quest.07C81F40FBB9407D.title: "Pottery"
	quest.07FEB5D83B2D0768.quest_desc: [
		"Heat kaolin clay to get kaolinite powder. You can use a forge to heat it, but cooking big batches in pit kilns may be faster."
		""
		"Grind graphite in a quern for graphite powder."
		""
		"Finally, combine 4 graphite powder, 4 kaolinite powder and 1 clay ball to make fire clay."
	]
	quest.07FEB5D83B2D0768.quest_subtitle: "At last"
	quest.07FEB5D83B2D0768.title: "Fire Clay"
	quest.080872DBA7A3B160.quest_desc: [
		"Hydrogen is used in countless GregTech chemical reactions, starting in &7LV&r with hydrochloric acid."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r in infinite amounts by electrolyzing water, or salt water (the sea will do), which also gives chlorine."
		""
		"Deuterium and tritium are for collectors: centrifuge hydrogen into deuterium (&7LV&r) and deuterium into tritium (&bMV&r)."
	]
	quest.080872DBA7A3B160.quest_subtitle: "Element #1"
	quest.080872DBA7A3B160.title: "Hydrogen"
	quest.082D50B32B4F3E6D.quest_desc: [
		"&a4A&r of &bMV&r energy transmission may be appealing, but you probably don't need these at this point. The option is always there if you need it."
	]
	quest.082D50B32B4F3E6D.title: "MV Superconductors"
	quest.0841E0F3E7DA1785.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Large Chemical Reactor (LCR)&r is a multiblock &3Chemical Reactor&r with more input/output slots. Its Teflon casings allow it to process extra recipes."
		""
		"The &3LCR&r can perform some exclusive reactions which allow you to combine multiple normal &3Chemical Reactor&r steps into a &6single step&r. Examples below:"
		""
		"&9-&r &aNitrogen Dioxide&r (for Nitric Acid and Dinitrogen Tetroxide)"
		"&9-&r &aSulfuric Acid&r"
		"&9-&r &aPhenol&r"
		"&9-&r &aEpichlorohydrin&r (you need it for Epoxy!)"
		"&9-&r &aEpoxy&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are also &3LCR&r exclusive recipes. For example, &dRadon&r can only be made in the LCR right now."
		""
		"All &dOverclocks&r in the &3LCR&r are &6100%% efficient&r (known as Perfect overclocks); each overclock will &5quadruple the speed&r, as opposed to doubling it."
		""
		"The &3LCR&r has yet another &6advantage&r. You can use &32 Energy Hatches&r to allow it to run recipes of the &5next tier&r, similar to the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Tip:&r Given the amount of LCRs you may end up using, why not try utilising &dwallsharing&r to its full potential?"
		""
		"You could share one 2A (standard) &3Energy Hatch&r between 2 LCRs."
		""
		"You might want to share &3Input/Output Hatches&r, but make sure each LCR is running the correct recipe."
		""
		"Keep in mind Maintenance hatches are not sharable."
	]
	quest.0841E0F3E7DA1785.title: "Large Chemical Reactor"
	quest.085716E91923B183.quest_desc: [
		"Work pig iron on the anvil into high-carbon steel and then steel, or refine pig iron with charcoal or coke in GregTech's primitive blast furnace."
	]
	quest.085716E91923B183.quest_subtitle: "Only from pig iron"
	quest.085716E91923B183.title: "Steel"
	quest.08B0EE2E85E999E2.quest_desc: [
		"Silver is used in the bronze age for TFC's sterling silver, and in GregTech for electrum and the silver cables of &6HV&r motors."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC native silver."
	]
	quest.08B0EE2E85E999E2.quest_subtitle: "Element #47"
	quest.08B0EE2E85E999E2.title: "Silver"
	quest.08BF36E8C1A5F640.quest_desc: [
		"A wooden shield, made from lumber and glue, will protect you somewhat from most damage sources you point it at."
		""
		"It's cheap, and it shows. Metal shields come once you can work an anvil."
	]
	quest.08BF36E8C1A5F640.quest_subtitle: "Skeletons hurt, like a lot"
	quest.08BF36E8C1A5F640.title: "Wooden Shield"
	quest.08C7DA782BA13103.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Cleanroom&r is a hollow multiblock free of contaminants. Going forward, most new &acircuit-related recipes&r, as well as some unique blocks like &3Fusion Casings&r, will need to be run in machines inside a Cleanroom."
		""
		"Creating it will put your &aPolyethylene&r automation to the test for all the &dPlascrete&r and/or &dCleanroom Glass&r you will make."
		""
		"We'll start you off with a 5x5x5 Cleanroom, but you should upgrade its size when you start feeling cramped."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Cleanroom comes from GregTech 5, but as is often the case, the GT5 implementation is much more punishing. The recipes would run without regard to cleanliness, but had a %% chance of completion equal to the cleanliness of the Cleanroom. This caused a lot of accidental voiding."
		""
		"&oFurthermore, if the Cleanroom had a maintenance issue, the cleanliness would cap out at 90%%, which means 10%% of items would be voided."
		""
		"&oThe GTCEu Cleanroom will &6never void&f recipe outputs."
	]
	quest.08C7DA782BA13103.quest_subtitle: "They put me in a room... a clean room"
	quest.08C7DA782BA13103.title: "The Cleanroom"
	quest.091978749669983D.quest_desc: [
		"The Integrated Logic Circuit is an alternate &7LV &aCircuit&r, which is easier to mass-produce, and can be upgraded to &bMV&r (and then &6HV&r)."
		""
		"&9Note:&r This is not a strict upgrade to the cost of Circuits - you would need to get to the next Tier for that. It is still an important upgrade, and is required to get to &6HV circuits&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The circuit progression in GTCEu is mostly based on GT5u's progression. It has been rebalanced to not be as painful. &lSpecifically&r&o this circuit tier, which was a trap!"
	]
	quest.091978749669983D.quest_subtitle: "You have unlocked a new tier of Circuits!"
	quest.091978749669983D.title: "More LV Circuits"
	quest.0921EDF6053EBE28.quest_desc: [
		"Most ores don't need any fancy bathing setups, and running them through an &dOre Washer&r will suffice: about a third of a byproduct per ore."
		""
		"If you use the &bOre Washer&r, make sure to use &9Distilled Water&r to double the speed of the recipe."
		""
		"Don't have one yet? You can right-click a cauldron of water with crushed ore to purify it, though this won't get you any byproducts."
	]
	quest.0921EDF6053EBE28.quest_subtitle: "The standard option for most ores"
	quest.0921EDF6053EBE28.title: "Bathe them in Water"
	quest.0923233DF1EDA4AC.quest_desc: [
		"&aSoldering Alloy&r is used solely as a &9Fluid&r, and in circuit recipes it's a &dcheaper&r stand-in for molten Tin: half as much per circuit."
		""
		"The choice is yours. Save more materials? Make Soldering Alloy. Spend less time crafting materials? Tin is the way to go."
		""
		"Mix 6 tin, 3 lead and 1 antimony dust in a Mixer, then melt the dust in an Extractor. Ignore the Alloy Blast Smelter recipes in EMI!"
	]
	quest.0923233DF1EDA4AC.quest_subtitle: "I got soul but I'm not a solder"
	quest.0923233DF1EDA4AC.title: "Soldering Alloy"
	quest.09439275D6F76A0F.quest_desc: [
		"Before we start, here's some important information if you're aiming to make Ethylene:"
		""
		"Taking the &aOil&r route will require &oat least&r a &3LV Distillery&r."
		""
		"With the &aBiomass&r route, you will &lneed&r a &3MV Distillery&r."
		""
		"Get &eeither&r to complete this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Got all that? &6Alright&r! Let's discuss a complex topic: &9Distillation&r. We'll try to help you understand how and why the &aEMI&r recipes are the way they are, so stick with us."
		""
		"Nearly all the &3Distillery&r recipes are duplicates from the &3Distillation Tower&r, except that they only have one Fluid output, and void everything else."
		""
		"In other words, you could argue the &3Distillery&r is an &dinferior&r &3Distillation Tower&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This doesn't mean that the &3Distillery&r is the worse of the two. It is unlocked earlier, and it is &dsmaller&r, &dcheaper&r, and &dmore energy efficient&r per recipe."
		""
		"Hell, in many cases, you won't even mind losing the other Fluids."
		""
		"&3Distilleries&r are an essential component for power generation, whether you pick &aDiesel&r or &aBenzene&r."
		""
		"You'll probably want many of them at as low-tier as possible to avoid the energy losses from Overclocking."
	]
	quest.09439275D6F76A0F.quest_subtitle: "The Illusion of Free Choice"
	quest.09439275D6F76A0F.title: "Distillery"
	quest.094BA6B5628B036B.quest_desc: [
		"Candles are a better light source than torches: a candle burns for 240 in-game hours (ten days) before it needs relighting, a torch for 72."
		""
		"Seal string in a barrel of tallow to make them (cook blubber in a pot of water for tallow), and dye them in a barrel if you like."
	]
	quest.094BA6B5628B036B.quest_subtitle: "Cozy..."
	quest.094BA6B5628B036B.title: "Candles"
	quest.0959F5B3F2214E58.title: "Iron Age"
	quest.0974FECB148B5E92.quest_desc: [
		"Let's talk about the &dElectronic Components&r from &dGregTech&r. They are a &ccore part&r of the mod's progression and are used to make &aall circuits&r in the game."
		""
		"Most components have &amultiple recipes&r. Depending on the &9materials&r you choose, you can achieve &ebetter yields&r. We encourage you to browse through &aEMI&r and decide which ones fit your situation best."
		""
		"These components can be crafted in &clarge stacks&r—you'll need &ea lot&r of them for your future circuits!"
		""
		"For the &dTransistor&r, you’ll specifically need &5Silicon Ingots&r... but by now, you should be &cvery familiar&r with &chandling hot stuff&r, right?"
	]
	quest.0974FECB148B5E92.quest_subtitle: "A core piece of GT progression system"
	quest.0974FECB148B5E92.title: "Electronic Components"
	quest.098AC1425224A51C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6RTM Coils&r can reach an impressive &e4,500K&r, unlocking access to &dTantalum Carbide&r (4,120K), a key material for your progression: you'll need it to craft the &5Alloy Blast Smelter&r. They will also greatly speed up the recipes in your EBF."
		""
		"Each coil takes RTM wire, Vanadium Steel foil and molten Nichrome, so your Nichrome production pays off again."
	]
	quest.098AC1425224A51C.quest_subtitle: "How hot can it get?"
	quest.098AC1425224A51C.title: "How hot can it get?"
	quest.09B8C65CB61591CE.quest_desc: [
		"Silicon is used to make silicone rubber and, in the electric blast furnace with a pinch of gallium arsenide, the silicon boules that wafers and chips are cut from."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: centrifuge flint dust into silicon dioxide, then electrolyze it."
	]
	quest.09B8C65CB61591CE.quest_subtitle: "Element #14"
	quest.09B8C65CB61591CE.title: "Silicon"
	quest.0A2195935D229EB0.quest_desc: [
		"You know what to do with this by now, but this is a good time to give you a heads up that now is the time to scale up your factory if you haven't already done so."
		""
		"Automate the crafting of new machines and components to keep your factory running at tip-top shape, because if you don't, the rest of EV is going to hit you like a brick wall."
		""
		"Don't wait to find out the hard way!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"At the very least, here's what we recommend before pushing further into EV:"
		""
		"&9-&r Passive production of Rubber, Polyethylene, Oxygen, Hydrogen, Nitrogen, and Chlorine"
		"&9-&r At least two general-purpose EBFs, and a few LCRs"
		"&9-&r Automated production of a circuit of every tier and most of the common crafting components like motors, pumps, plates, and wires"
		"&9-&r A dedicated ore processing setup"
		"&9-&r A couple EV amps worth of power generation (see the below quests)"
		""
		"You can do it, you've made it this far already!"
	]
	quest.0A2195935D229EB0.quest_subtitle: "Last step before some Extreme power generation!"
	quest.0A2195935D229EB0.title: "EV Assembler"
	quest.0A26B6F81DEA43C8.quest_desc: [
		"By shearing some friendly &2wool-producing&r livestock (or scraping a sheepskin hide), you can spin the resulting wool into &dWool Yarn&r with a &3Spindle&r. Working 16 yarn in a &3Loom&r gives you &dWool Cloth.&r"
		""
		"Besides rolling glass in &bGlassworking&r, it's used for beds and on the sewing table."
		""
		"Wool is considered a &bHigh Quality Cloth.&r"
	]
	quest.0A26B6F81DEA43C8.quest_subtitle: "Baaa..."
	quest.0A26B6F81DEA43C8.title: "Wool Cloth"
	quest.0ABCBED4780E3070.quest_desc: [
		"By clicking the &6Circuit Configuration Slot&r in machines, you can create a &bghost Programmed Circuit&r. "
		""
		"This is a fake circuit that allows you to select a given configuration for recipes! There's no need to spend your circuits crafting &bProgrammed Circuits&r anymore."
		""
		"&dElectric Machines&r and &dItem Input Buses&r will have a Ghost Circuit Slot."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This feature is originally from GTNH."
	]
	quest.0ABCBED4780E3070.quest_subtitle: "Don't want to spend your circuits to select recipes?"
	quest.0ABCBED4780E3070.title: "Programmed Circuits"
	quest.0B1098D3533FA722.quest_desc: [
		"Just like in regular Minecraft, &dLamps&r can be hung from the ceiling with the help of chains or placed on top of blocks. They're smithed on an anvil, finished with &dLamp Glass&r, and filled with a bucket of liquid fuel such as &6Olive Oil&r or &6Tallow&r."
		""
		"Lava keeps burning &4indefinitely&r, but only a Blue Steel or Red Steel lamp can hold it. Lamps keep their fuel when broken."
	]
	quest.0B1098D3533FA722.quest_subtitle: "These are pretty."
	quest.0B1098D3533FA722.title: "Lamps"
	quest.0B18E2D3F5CD9725.quest_desc: [
		"&lOutside of Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Oh boy, what can't this machine do? Decomposition recipes to separate dust types, separating air, do your taxes, and many others..."
		""
		"The list is too long! Let's just say &cyou need the Centrifuge&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFor Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"This takes &aImpure Dust&r or &aPurified Dust&r and turns them into clean Dust, plus an added tiny Dust &6Byproduct&r. This is outside of the optimal chain for Byproducts, but this is also the cheapest Ore Processing machine of the presented array to run and to setup on a small scale."
	]
	quest.0B18E2D3F5CD9725.quest_subtitle: "It does the opposite of the Mixer"
	quest.0B18E2D3F5CD9725.title: "Basic Centrifuge"
	quest.0B974C29AB2F667C.quest_desc: [
		"New Cutting Machine? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New Lens? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New Power Circuit? &a✓&r"
		""
		"New Coil for Energy Hatch? &a✓&r"
		""
		"The &aMPIC&r Wafer is a Phosphorus Wafer engraved with a &6Brown&r lens; cutting it takes an &5EV&r Cutter."
	]
	quest.0B974C29AB2F667C.title: "Power Integrated Circuit"
	quest.0B98DB7D47E4C852.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike their vanilla counterparts, Barrels here are used as Liquid Storage. Barrels are capable of storing a total of 10 Buckets of fluid, allowing for relatively simple storage of fluids."
		""
		"You can also combine these fluids with other items, to create things like Leather, Glue, Mortar and more."
	]
	quest.0B98DB7D47E4C852.quest_subtitle: "Stephano?"
	quest.0B98DB7D47E4C852.title: "Barrels"
	quest.0B9BC1D2BC2C9322.quest_desc: [
		"Weak steel is one half of black steel. Alloy it in a crucible from 2 parts steel, 1 part nickel and 1 part black bronze."
		""
		"The exact ranges are 50-70% steel, 15-25% nickel and 15-25% black bronze; EMI shows them on molten weak steel."
	]
	quest.0B9BC1D2BC2C9322.quest_subtitle: "Hope you like math"
	quest.0B9BC1D2BC2C9322.title: "Weak Steel Ingredients"
	quest.0C3BDFB496BDE961.quest_desc: [
		"&4Red Alloy&r is an alloy of Copper and Redstone, prized in the GregTech universe for its conductivity. Make it in the Alloy Smelter: one copper and four redstone. A TFC quern grinds cinnabar or cryolite into redstone."
		""
		"Press it into a plate and slit the plate into wires with Create's saw. Your first circuits need red alloy cable."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This material originally comes from RedPower - what a throwback!"
	]
	quest.0C3BDFB496BDE961.quest_subtitle: "A completely fictional alloy"
	quest.0C3BDFB496BDE961.title: "Red Alloy"
	quest.0C3F12BBF127206D.quest_desc: [
		"You now have two ways to mine automatically! Both of them are very slow, so it's a good idea to set them up, keep their chunks loaded (Create: Power Loader's chunk loaders) and go do something else instead of sitting and waiting."
		""
		"The &3Mechanical Drill&r needs a contraption to move it, breaking all stone along the way. You can also attach it to the front of a train or minecart to dig tunnels."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The &3Steam Miner&r, on the other hand, only breaks ore blocks (TFC's ores count) and replaces them with cobblestone, leaving the rest of the ground intact. It mines ores in a small radius, so it has to be moved less often than a drill, but it's also a lot slower."
	]
	quest.0C3F12BBF127206D.quest_subtitle: "Let the machines swing the pickaxe"
	quest.0C3F12BBF127206D.title: "Automatic Mining"
	quest.0C7E965D4E868A3F.quest_desc: [
		"&6HV&r doesn't unlock any new weapons, but it does come with an important piece of equipment: GregTech's &6NanoMuscle™ Suite&r (see Tips: Tools)."
	]
	quest.0C7E965D4E868A3F.title: "&6HV&r"
	quest.0D701D3F51BCC0AF.quest_desc: [
		"&aBatteries&r can be put into the energy slot at the bottom middle of machine GUIs, or in a &3Battery Buffer&r."
		""
		"When inside your inventory, they can be sneak-right-clicked to allow the batteries to &dcharge&r your EU items."
		""
		"&7LV&r, &bMV&r, and &6HV&r Batteries come in three forms: &dLithium&r has the best capacity, followed by &dCadmium&r, then &dSodium&r. A Canner fills a Battery Hull with two dusts."
		""
		"In this pack &dSodium&r is the easy one: electrolyze &asalt&r from TFC halite. &dCadmium&r comes from bathing crushed tetrahedrite in sodium persulfate, and &dLithium&r waits for &bMV&r."
		""
		"Get &eany&r &aBattery&r to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.0D701D3F51BCC0AF.quest_subtitle: "Batteries for storing energy!"
	quest.0D701D3F51BCC0AF.title: "Batteries!"
	quest.0D71EEE3AFA68254.quest_desc: [
		"Glass bottles are a sturdier way to carry water: a silica glass bottle holds 500 mB, five drinks, and the other glasses a little less. However, blowing glass bottles won't be possible until you can shape Brass: a bottle is blown on a blowpipe, pinched with Jacks (two welded brass rods) and cut with a Gem Saw (a brass rod and gem powder)."
		""
		"Check the field guide's Glassworking pages for glass batches and the blowpipe."
	]
	quest.0D71EEE3AFA68254.quest_subtitle: "Not as cool as a leather flask"
	quest.0D71EEE3AFA68254.title: "Glass Bottles"
	quest.0D94A9A938A6BC36.quest_desc: [
		"The Brewery can be used to make &aLubricant&r from &aRedstone&r and &aCreosote&r/&aOil&r. Lubricant has some niche uses, namely being used in the &3Cutter&r to significantly reduce the duration of its recipes."
		""
		"The Brewery is a very, very slow machine, but it requires almost no power to run its recipes. Building &2many Breweries&r will help you obtain enough Biomass on your quest for plastic."
		""
		"&9Note:&r The Brewery unlocks the Biomass path towards &9Ethylene&r. The same can be done in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r. The other path involves Oil.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o You could make your own Brewery if you want to build up a company and start selling Booze... in GregTech 6.&r"
	]
	quest.0D94A9A938A6BC36.quest_subtitle: "*hic*... *hic*"
	quest.0D94A9A938A6BC36.title: "Local Brewery selling Booze"
	quest.0E0EEA17CD70C458.quest_desc: [
		"All machines typically have one &7Front Face&r, and one &9Output Face&r."
		""
		"The &7Front Face&r should be obvious."
		"The &9Output Face&r is the face with a dot or hole on it. By default, this is at the back of the machine as you place it."
		""
		"Machines can &aauto-output&r through their output face. To enable auto-output, click the appropriate button in the GUI. Fluid and item auto-outputs are toggled separately. Further control over auto-outputs can be achieved with &dFilters&r and &dCovers&r, which are explained in the &dCover Behavior&r quest found in this chapter."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Right-clicking a machine with a &5Wrench&r changes the output side, and shift-right-clicking changes the front side. Keep in mind that the front side &ccannot&r also be the output side! "
		""
		"By default, items and fluids cannot be inserted through the output side, but this can be toggled with a &5Screwdriver&r. Either right-click the output face directly, or shift-right-click on the grid corresponding to the side of the output."
	]
	quest.0E0EEA17CD70C458.quest_subtitle: "Let's learn."
	quest.0E0EEA17CD70C458.title: "Machine Auto-Output Behaviour"
	quest.0E5DA1024FCEB1CE.quest_desc: [
		"Chlorine is used in &7LV&r+ to make hydrochloric acid, and in many later chemical chains."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r in infinite amounts by electrolyzing salt water (the sea is salt water), or from salt and rock salt dust (TFC halite and sylvite)."
	]
	quest.0E5DA1024FCEB1CE.quest_subtitle: "Element #17"
	quest.0E5DA1024FCEB1CE.title: "Chlorine"
	quest.0E6EA3DD94A0B6B0.quest_desc: [
		"The only things you can really do with refined ore are crush it into dust or smelt it."
	]
	quest.0E6EA3DD94A0B6B0.title: "Refined Ore"
	quest.0E7FD27DA1141DE3.quest_desc: [
		"The &dChemical Bath&r is a versatile machine, mainly used to dye materials and to get extra resources out of ores, but until you build a &bVacuum Freezer&r it is also how you cool your hot ingots. Cooling takes 120 EU/t, so you need the &bMV&r Chemical Bath."
	]
	quest.0E7FD27DA1141DE3.quest_subtitle: "Why can't we just cool these in a lake?"
	quest.0E7FD27DA1141DE3.title: "Chemical Bath"
	quest.0EA1CFB62F855B98.quest_desc: [
		"The &eLarge Bronze Boiler&r is a multiblock that makes far more &bSteam&r than the small boilers. It burns solid fuels or liquid ones such as creosote, and takes a while to heat up."
		""
		"Its controller takes LV circuits. Press the EMI 'Uses' key (U) on the controller to see the structure."
		""
		"Like every boiler, keep water flowing in before it gets hot, or it will &cEXPLODE&r."
	]
	quest.0EA1CFB62F855B98.quest_subtitle: "Mass producing Steam"
	quest.0EA1CFB62F855B98.title: "Large Bronze Boiler"
	quest.0F32780099526FC4.quest_desc: [
		"Fluorine is used for hydrofluoric acid, and from it polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE)."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &bMV&r by electrolyzing topaz dust (from TFC topaz), or biotite dust, which the centrifuge separates from stone dust."
	]
	quest.0F32780099526FC4.quest_subtitle: "Element #9"
	quest.0F32780099526FC4.title: "Fluorine"
	quest.0FA2318EDDC6EC90.quest_desc: [
		"Nitric Acid's fumes are extremely toxic! It's also a very potent oxidizer."
		""
		"&aNitric Acid&r is used in:"
		""
		"&9-&r Cetane-Boosted Diesel, a better Diesel fuel that you'll get to soon."
		"&9-&r The optional gem slurry chains."
		"&9-&r The Platinum Group Sludge chain."
		"&9-&r Polybenzimidazole (try saying that ten times fast!) in &1IV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are two main ways to make &aNitric Acid&r - &othe &agood&f way and the &4bad&f ways!&r"
		""
		"Therefore, we'll point you towards the best method:"
		""
		"Get a &3Large Chemical Reactor&r and use it to make &aNitrogen Dioxide&r. From there, react it in a regular &3Chemical Reactor&r with more &dOxygen&r and &dWater&r and you got yourself some &aNitric Acid&r!"
		""
		"This requires a lot of &dOxygen&r, so make sure your electrolysis keeps up. Notice that this is Hydrogen free!"
	]
	quest.0FA2318EDDC6EC90.quest_subtitle: "This won't eat your skin"
	quest.0FA2318EDDC6EC90.title: "Nitric Acid"
	quest.0FD922EE3AD4BDD0.quest_desc: [
		"You know the drill at this point. &6Tungstensteel&r will be your main material for &1IV&r, and you can expect to need a very large quantity of it: Tungsten and Steel dust in your &5EV&r Mixer, then the EBF at 3,000K. Make sure you have a dedicated &6Tungsten line&r running to sustain your production before moving further."
	]
	quest.0FD922EE3AD4BDD0.quest_subtitle: "The main material of IV"
	quest.0FD922EE3AD4BDD0.title: "Tungstensteel"
	quest.0FE3395E6B2219DA.quest_desc: [
		"This prospector boasts a &6higher range&r than its &7LV&r counterpart."
		""
		"Sneak right-clicking with the Prospector in your hand will change its mode to &6Fluid Vein Mode&r. This will instead display the base &dyield&r of the bedrock Fluid veins below you, along with how full they are."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Reminder:&r The yield of a &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r is directly proportional to the \"fullness\" of the vein. When low enough, the output will default to a yield that can be defined in the CEu config."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r When the fullness drops below 30%% (alright, rough estimate), you should consider moving to another vein for the sake of power-to-yield efficiency. Aiming for the &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig&r in &5EV&r may interest you, as not only does it significantly boost the output, but it also reduces the rate at which it drains the vein!"
	]
	quest.0FE3395E6B2219DA.title: "HV Prospector"
	quest.10448D4511718EED.quest_desc: [
		"While stone and obsidian are relatively simple and primitive materials, they're what you're stuck with until you learn how to work with metals. Some other useful tools include the Javelin, which can be thrown like a vanilla Trident, the Hammer, which you'll need for flux and anvils, and the Hoe, which allows you to farm."
	]
	quest.10448D4511718EED.quest_subtitle: "Turns out hitting stones together is quite useful"
	quest.10448D4511718EED.title: "Primitive Tools"
	quest.104F2FD3B0D01DAA.quest_desc: [
		"There are &amany ways&r to get your hands on &dHydrogen&r—and it will often be a &abyproduct&r of other chemical reactions."
		""
		"In &dPetrochem&r, you’ll produce a lot of &dMethane&r, which can be &aelectrolyzed&r into &dHydrogen&r. You could also electrolyze &9Water&r, but we recommend going for &9Seawater&r instead, as it gives more useful byproducts."
		""
		"Later on, the &ebest method&r will be reacting &9Water&r with &dMethane&r directly—but that’s &6HV-gated&r and will start off &erather slow&r."
	]
	quest.104F2FD3B0D01DAA.quest_subtitle: "You know about Hydrogen right?"
	quest.104F2FD3B0D01DAA.title: "Hydrogen Gas"
	quest.10AEBA6BC88ED1F3.quest_desc: [
		"Rhodium is used to make rhodium-plated palladium, the base material of &dLuV&r."
		""
		"It comes from the platinum line (see ruthenium): electrolyze the rhodium sulfate split from inert metal mixture (&5EV&r)."
	]
	quest.10AEBA6BC88ED1F3.quest_subtitle: "Element #45"
	quest.10AEBA6BC88ED1F3.title: "Rhodium"
	quest.10C6E7F8807D43D1.quest_desc: [
		"The various single-block generators only go up to HV, so from here on, you'll have to use multiblocks to generate more power. Two of the best options at EV are the &dLarge Gas Turbine&r and &dLarge Combustion Engine&r, so head over to the power chapter to learn more about them."
	]
	quest.10C6E7F8807D43D1.title: "Extreme Power Generation"
	quest.113579E5D7E23CC0.quest_desc: [
		"Almost everything you can wear can have an armor trim applied, TFC's metal armor included. Check the &a#minecraft:trimmable_armor&r tag to see what you can apply trims to, and the &a#minecraft:trim_materials&r tag for your color options: TFC's gems, silver, sterling silver, gold, rose gold and bismuth."
		""
		"Smithing templates are sewn on a &6Sewing Table&r, then applied at a &6Smithing Table&r. Trims are purely cosmetic."
	]
	quest.113579E5D7E23CC0.quest_subtitle: "Add some flair to your fit"
	quest.113579E5D7E23CC0.title: "Armor Trims"
	quest.11472E726E00A598.quest_desc: [
		"How to spend all this energy?"
		""
		"Use your machines! Sounds simple, right?"
		"Well... not exactly. There are many small details worth learning."
		""
		"Basic Machines:"
		"- These machines are simple."
		"- They can request up to &a2A&r each."
		"- If you input a higher tier of energy... &4💥 they explode&r."
		""
		"GregTech Multiblocks:"
		"Now things get interesting. Multiblocks offer more flexibility and power — &eif&r you understand how they work."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Standard Mechanics:"
		"- If a multiblock can accept two Energy Hatches (most of them), this allows you to use higher-tier recipes than the machine's base tier."
		""
		"Example:"
		"If you're building an Electric Blast Furnace and you install two &7LV&r Energy Hatches, it will be able to process &bMV&r-tier EBF recipes."
		""
		"This is one of the key benefits of multiblocks over single-block machines — to upgrade them to the next tier, you only have to swap out their energy hatches instead of replacing the whole machine."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Some multiblocks only accept one Energy Hatch, but that doesn't limit them to 2 amps! From &5EV&r on there are 4A and 16A Energy Hatches."
		""
		"More amps on a single hatch let the machine &bOverclock&r recipes, but not run higher-tier recipes. That limitation is intentional, to keep multiblocks from skipping GregTech's tier progression."
		""
		"So remember: More amps on a single hatch means faster processing, but two hatches are required to unlock higher-tier recipes."
	]
	quest.11472E726E00A598.quest_subtitle: "Oh you will spend energy"
	quest.11472E726E00A598.title: "Spending Energy"
	quest.11EC1AB24A424C40.quest_desc: [
		"Knives are most useful for crafting, but they can be a weapon in a pinch. They deal &9Piercing&r damage, which Zombies are weak to."
		""
		"For more information on &cDamage Types&r consult the &3Field Guide&r."
	]
	quest.11EC1AB24A424C40.quest_subtitle: "Stabby stabby"
	quest.11EC1AB24A424C40.title: "Knives"
	quest.123D7767539A9B44.quest_desc: [
		"Large water wheels give four times a small wheel's stress capacity per RPM, but still need flowing water from a river. Wrap a water wheel in eight more planks to make one."
	]
	quest.123D7767539A9B44.quest_subtitle: "Larger, stronger, more expensive"
	quest.123D7767539A9B44.title: "Large Water Wheels"
	quest.1305572189D97712.quest_desc: [
		"Even at its lowest power (Cupronickel coils and &7LV&r Voltage), the &dMulti Smelter&r smelts 32 items at once, far beyond any furnace you've built."
		""
		"If that wasn't already enough to convince you, standard &aoverclocks&r apply with sufficient voltage."
		""
		"And even better: higher tier &3Coils&r increase the number of items it can smelt in &dparallel&r!"
		""
		"As everywhere in this pack, iron that is smelted comes out as cast iron."
	]
	quest.1305572189D97712.quest_subtitle: "Possibly the most powerful furnace you've seen"
	quest.1305572189D97712.title: "Ultimate Smelter"
	quest.1347FDA5072CDAA7.quest_desc: [
		"The &3MV Cutter&r is required to cut &7Silicon Boules&r into wafers for &aLaser Engraving&r, and the engraved wafers into chips. Its saw is a &bVanadium Steel&r buzzsaw blade."
		""
		"We recommend you supply this machine with a steady stream of &dLubricant&r to cut down on the processing time."
		""
		"Lubricant can be &3brewed&r from &cRedstone&r and &dCreosote&r, &eSeed Oil&r or &eOil&r."
	]
	quest.1347FDA5072CDAA7.quest_subtitle: "Upgrades, people, upgrades!"
	quest.1347FDA5072CDAA7.title: "Advanced Cutter"
	quest.138251FC5C8DD73E.quest_desc: [
		"Cooking raw meat is an important step for getting protein: cooked meat keeps much longer than raw meat."
		""
		"The simplest way to cook meat is in a Fire Pit (see the Fire quest): put it in the firepit's heating slot."
	]
	quest.138251FC5C8DD73E.quest_subtitle: "You don't want to die from eating raw meat, do you?"
	quest.138251FC5C8DD73E.title: "Basic Cooking"
	quest.13BE6FB3D56F1F93.quest_desc: [
		"On the deep ocean floor, nodules lie loose on the mud in broad fields around small cores of nodule bed. Pick a loose one up by hand, or sweep the bed blocks with a shovel: each gives raw pyrolusite (manganese), now and then cobaltite."
		""
		"Macerate it for crushed pyrolusite, wash it, spin it in a thermal centrifuge and macerate the refined ore: the dust comes with a little niobium. Manganese arrives with the macerator too (step 19), so stainless steel does not wait for anything else."
	]
	quest.13BE6FB3D56F1F93.quest_subtitle: "Broad and thin"
	quest.13BE6FB3D56F1F93.title: "Manganese Nodules"
	quest.13CD47440020B7C8.quest_desc: [
		"Gallium is used to make gallium arsenide for silicon boules and diodes."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r as a byproduct of processing TFC sphalerite, or by electrolyzing sphalerite dust."
	]
	quest.13CD47440020B7C8.quest_subtitle: "Element #31"
	quest.13CD47440020B7C8.title: "Gallium"
	quest.149221361E259C6B.quest_desc: [
		"A brass sheet on a stripped log (TFC logs count). Propellers, smart machines and airships build on it."
	]
	quest.149221361E259C6B.quest_subtitle: "Precision machinery"
	quest.149221361E259C6B.title: "Brass Casing"
	quest.14BC11A8925C8230.quest_desc: [
		"At the cost of 4x the drilling Power, the &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig&r gains &616x the output&r in Fluid."
		""
		"The depletion of veins is also halved. This means you will get a total of &632x&r as much Oil (or whatever fluid) from a bedrock fluid vein until depletion!"
		""
		"Even when depleted, you can still use this and be firmly power positive."
		""
		"One single &3Advanced Fluid Drilling Rig&r should be enough to supply Power for a base up to &dLuV&r... and possibly beyond!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"As a &9reminder&r, since this last appeared in &bMV&r:"
		""
		"&9-&r &aLight Oil&r can be used for &dLPG&r and &dMethane&r to run in &3Large Gas Turbines&r."
		""
		"&9-&r &aOil&r can be used for &dDiesel&r and &dCetane-Boosted Diesel&r to run in &3Large Combustion Engines&r."
	]
	quest.14BC11A8925C8230.quest_subtitle: "Extreme is an apt descriptor"
	quest.14BC11A8925C8230.title: "Extreme Fluid Drilling"
	quest.150A550D8C7F2163.quest_desc: [
		"For all your other Purified Ores that don't need special treatment, it's best to run them through the &dThermal Centrifuge&r. This machine can produce byproducts at a reliable rate, without needing any other ingredients. It's quite slow, however, so we suggest making several."
	]
	quest.150A550D8C7F2163.quest_subtitle: "The go-to for most purified ores"
	quest.150A550D8C7F2163.title: "The Thermal Centrifuge"
	quest.15604562C26BB8B7.quest_desc: [
		"A big part of progression in GregTech revolves around gaining access to new materials that you'll use to upgrade your machines or unlock advanced components."
		""
		"One such material you'll encounter is &bCupronickel&r — the beginning of a long journey."
		"This material is used to build your first &6Electric Blast Furnace&r, an essential step in your industrial growth."
		""
		"Luckily, this first step is fairly simple: an Alloy Smelter turns one copper and one nickel (from TFC garnierite) into two cupronickel. So even if the coils ask for &b128 Cupronickel&r, don't worry — it's easier than it looks!&r"
		""
		"Later on, their counterparts will become much more complex, so enjoy the simplicity while it lasts!"
	]
	quest.15604562C26BB8B7.quest_subtitle: "It's an alloy"
	quest.15604562C26BB8B7.title: "Cupronickel Ingots"
	quest.15AF91786A007021.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dusts&r are the final form of almost every ore."
		""
		"From here, you can smelt it in a steam furnace or with Create's fan, send it to &estorage&r, or even start using it right away! Iron dusts smelt into TFC cast iron. Some dusts will require one last step before they become truly useful."
		""
		"Remember to keep your &6ore processing line&r in top shape! You'll want to keep expanding and upgrading it as you progress, so you can spend less time mining and more time gregging."
	]
	quest.15AF91786A007021.quest_subtitle: "Or is it?"
	quest.15AF91786A007021.title: "Your final dust"
	quest.15BDF7BE4A90BFE0.quest_desc: [
		"You've built new &6chemistry lines&r, manufactured advanced &balloys&r, and mastered the &aCleanroom&r. We hope you enjoyed the ride, because now things get even more complex, with powerful new machines and demanding processes ahead."
		""
		"In the &5EV Chapter&r, your main objective will be to craft your very first &1IV&r Circuits and the &1IV&r Machine Hull."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Along the way, several key challenges await you:"
		""
		"• Process &eTungsten&r and turn it into &6Tungstensteel&r, the main material of &1IV&r."
		""
		"• Upgrade your EBF to &6RTM Coils&r, which open Tantalum Carbide and your first &6Alloy Blast Smelter&r."
		""
		"• Set up &aEpoxy&r production for the boards of your &bNano&r Circuits."
		""
		"Good luck, this is where GregTech begins to show its true depth!"
	]
	quest.15BDF7BE4A90BFE0.quest_subtitle: "Tungsten, Epoxy and your first IV circuits"
	quest.15BDF7BE4A90BFE0.title: "This is Extreme Voltage"
	quest.161F2A1961D57E50.quest_desc: [
		"Storing your energy is one of the most fundamental pillars of the power system in GregTech."
		""
		"Why is that? Simply because even the strongest generators won't keep up when you start a big craft."
		""
		"GregTech provides several ways to store large amounts of EU. These storages act as a buffer between your energy production and the machines that drain it during long operations."
		""
		"Whether you're running an Electric Blast Furnace or a whole HV-EV crafting chain, you'll want that backup of energy to keep everything stable."
		""
		"Don't underestimate the power of a good battery — it may just be the thing that saves your base from a blackout during critical moments."
	]
	quest.161F2A1961D57E50.quest_subtitle: "Gotta put all that juice somewhere"
	quest.161F2A1961D57E50.title: "Storing Energy"
	quest.167A094CD8F158C2.quest_desc: [
		"Nickel goes into TFC's black steel, and in GregTech into invar (the electric blast furnace's casings), cupronickel (its first coils), nichrome, stainless steel and many other alloys."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC garnierite."
	]
	quest.167A094CD8F158C2.quest_subtitle: "Element #28"
	quest.167A094CD8F158C2.title: "Nickel"
	quest.1682B45C9E28D8AA.quest_desc: [
		"In addition to alloying metals together, the Alloy Smelter can also use &3Casting Molds&r to shape materials."
		""
		"Molds start as an &aEmpty Mold&r: four steel plates with a hammer and a file. A hammer then shapes it into the mold you want. You'll need the &aBall&r mold for glass tubes; the &aPlate&r mold makes glass plates."
		""
		"Be sure to make &aCasting Molds&r - don't make &cExtruder Molds&r, as they're used in a different machine."
	]
	quest.1682B45C9E28D8AA.quest_subtitle: "Reduce the amount of malding by molding"
	quest.1682B45C9E28D8AA.title: "Molding"
	quest.175CB60182CF29B9.quest_desc: [
		"TFC worlds have no vanilla kelp, so belts, the spout, funnels, tunnels and pulleys take leather, burlap cloth or dried kelp."
	]
	quest.175CB60182CF29B9.quest_subtitle: "Leather or burlap"
	quest.175CB60182CF29B9.title: "Belts"
	quest.17A31BE2D2FF7FA8.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Schematicannon&r is an automatic building machine: it places blocks from attached containers according to a schematic, firing gunpowder as it goes. Use it to bring over buildings made in a creative world, or to copy and paste parts of your own structures."
		""
		"Draw schematics with Create's schematic and quill, and write them out at a schematic table."
	]
	quest.17A31BE2D2FF7FA8.quest_subtitle: "Automatic building"
	quest.17A31BE2D2FF7FA8.title: "Schematicannon"
	quest.17AB09C31FC6A067.quest_desc: [
		"To make any sort of &dGlass&r, you'll need a &3glassblowing&r setup."
		""
		"It starts with a &aBlowpipe&r: knap one from clay and fire it into a &aCeramic Blowpipe&r (brittle, it can break), or work a sturdier one from a &6Brass Rod&r on an anvil. Add a &aGlass Batch&r, heat it to &4Faint Red&r, and work it."
		""
		"&dGlass Panes&r and &dBlocks&r are poured onto &6Brass Plated Blocks&r: a flat table of them for panes, a basin for blocks. Check out the &2Field Guide&r for the details."
	]
	quest.17AB09C31FC6A067.quest_subtitle: "Realistic Glassworking!"
	quest.17AB09C31FC6A067.title: "Glassblowing"
	quest.17B268615FD2D56D.quest_desc: [
		"Nitrogen is used in &7LV&r+ for countless chemical reactions and to speed up the EBF and pyrolyse oven."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r in infinite amounts by centrifuging air from a gas collector."
	]
	quest.17B268615FD2D56D.quest_subtitle: "Element #7"
	quest.17B268615FD2D56D.title: "Nitrogen"
	quest.17D1FCED8C753DAF.quest_desc: [
		"Andesite casing (andesite alloy applied to a stripped log; TFC logs count) is the basis of most of Create's simple machines: gearboxes, the millstone, the press, the fan, the saw and more. Check EMI for everything you can build with it."
		""
		"New to Create? There are many tutorials online about different kinds of contraptions you can build, and most of them work here too."
	]
	quest.17D1FCED8C753DAF.quest_subtitle: "Primitive Machine Hull?"
	quest.17D1FCED8C753DAF.title: "Metal Casings"
	quest.1836C89E2D474639.quest_desc: [
		"Here's what TFC's ores give in a Sodium Persulfate bath:"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Sphalerite&r: &dZinc&r"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Tetrahedrite&r: &dCadmium&r"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Limonite&r: &dCobalt Oxide&r"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Malachite&r: &dZincite&r"
	]
	quest.1836C89E2D474639.quest_subtitle: "A useful time saver"
	quest.1836C89E2D474639.title: "Sodium Persulfate bathing examples"
	quest.18559C584D4D2089.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Chemical Reactor&r unlocks a ton of new recipes. Ah, who doesn't love the ever-growing demand on more advanced Chemistry?"
		""
		"&9Note:&r We've actually unlocked a ton of new content by reaching &6HV&r. However, not every processing line or item is crucial right now. It'd make the &6HV&r chapter far too dense if we included everything!"
		""
		"You could still check out the &5EV&r Chapter if you want to push yourself."
	]
	quest.18559C584D4D2089.title: "High Voltage Chemistry"
	quest.18891BC3AA9170CF.quest_desc: [
		"The Lathe is an important machine to help shape metals. It turns &6one Bolt into one Screw&r, where crafting by hand takes two bolts per screw."
		""
		"It also turns an ingot into a rod plus two small piles of dust, which you can smelt back, so nothing is lost."
	]
	quest.18891BC3AA9170CF.quest_subtitle: "Get rid of your archaic tech"
	quest.18891BC3AA9170CF.title: "Basic Lathe"
	quest.1889CF43A33440C0.quest_desc: [
		"Fills a balloon with hot air. It runs on redstone and burns no fuel. Brass plates, wrought iron plates and any coal or charcoal."
	]
	quest.1889CF43A33440C0.quest_subtitle: "Lift"
	quest.1889CF43A33440C0.title: "Hot-Air Burner"
	quest.18B082A954A67CBD.quest_desc: [
		"Bathing certain ores in &dMercury&r can give some other useful byproducts. Not all ores can be processed this way, but the ones that can will get a &670 percent&r chance of a byproduct, compared to the &633 percent&r of the &bOre Washer&r."
		""
		"&dMercury&r can be easily obtained by centrifuging TFC &cCinnabar&r dust (or &cRedstone&r)."
		""
		"The quest below gives the crushed ores worth bathing in Mercury."
	]
	quest.18B082A954A67CBD.quest_subtitle: "Don't stick your finger in it"
	quest.18B082A954A67CBD.title: "Bathe them in Mercury"
	quest.18C1F48C2B1DF94D.quest_desc: [
		"Cerium has few uses in GregTech; it is here for the set."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aCassiterite&r gives &aMonazite&r as its &3Ore Washer&r by-product. An &3Electrolyzer&r splits monazite dust into rare earth and phosphate, and a &3Centrifuge&r separates rare earth into small piles of cadmium, neodymium, samarium, cerium, yttrium and lanthanum."
	]
	quest.18C1F48C2B1DF94D.quest_subtitle: "Element #58"
	quest.18C1F48C2B1DF94D.title: "Cerium"
	quest.18E4DF305DFBB933.quest_desc: [
		"&lOutside of Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"The Chemical Bath soaks items in fluids: planks in creosote become treated wood, wood pulp in water becomes paper, and it can dye and bleach various items and blocks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFor Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Some &aCrushed Ores&r have alternate routes to &aPurified Ore&r: a bath in &aMercury&r or &aSodium Persulfate&r. This step isn't really important, unless you really want that special &6Byproduct&r."
	]
	quest.18E4DF305DFBB933.quest_subtitle: "The Chemical Bath bathes..."
	quest.18E4DF305DFBB933.title: "Basic Chemical Bath"
	quest.193640A1B80EB4C3.quest_desc: [
		"To begin making your Saw, put at least 100 mB of ore of your desired metal in a Vessel (ten small ore pieces). Afterwards, place the Vessel in a Pit Kiln and light it on fire."
		""
		"Once the Pit Kiln burns out, take your vessel while the metal is still molten and use it to open the Casting interface. Simply place the fired Saw Blade Mold in its slot and watch it fill with your very first Saw Blade. Afterwards, combine your Saw Blade with a Stick and you'll create your Saw!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"While the easiest metal to work with is Copper, you can try your hand at the process of alloying. This quest accepts a saw of Copper or any of the three bronzes."
		""
		"&lBismuth Bronze&r: Copper (50-65%), Zinc (20-30%) and Bismuth (10-20%)."
		""
		"&lBronze&r: Copper (88-92%) and Tin (8-12%). The most average of the bronzes."
		""
		"&lBlack Bronze&r: Copper (50-70%), Silver (10-25%) and Gold (10-25%). Considerably more expensive."
	]
	quest.193640A1B80EB4C3.quest_subtitle: "Time for your first metal tool"
	quest.193640A1B80EB4C3.title: "Metallic Saw"
	quest.194A04058BBC0B1A.quest_desc: [
		"TFC's blast furnace turns iron ore, charcoal and flux into pig iron. GregTech's electric blast furnace is later built from one."
		""
		"Craft it from a crucible and eight wrought iron double sheets, then build its chimney on top from reinforced fire bricks (a fire bricks block and a wrought iron or steel sheet): eight per layer, up to five layers, each layer holding four more ore. Put a bellows on one side, a tuyere in its interface, and a crucible right below it to catch the molten pig iron."
		""
		"Drop in equal numbers of iron ore and flux, plus charcoal: it burns only charcoal (coke is for GregTech's primitive blast furnace). Light it, keep it fuelled, and work the bellows once it's as hot as charcoal gets. The field guide has the full build."
	]
	quest.194A04058BBC0B1A.quest_subtitle: "Pig iron"
	quest.194A04058BBC0B1A.title: "Blast Furnace"
	quest.1952386A42CCD531.quest_desc: [
		"Thirst is the blue bar by your hunger bar. You can and will die of dehydration if you don't keep it filled! The easiest way to have a drink is from fresh water in the wild: right-click a lake or river with an empty hand."
		""
		"Tick this off once you've had a drink of fresh water. You don't have to worry about purifying water here, though Salt Water will just make you more thirsty."
	]
	quest.1952386A42CCD531.quest_subtitle: "Remember to drink water!"
	quest.1952386A42CCD531.title: "Thirsty?"
	quest.19C743189F6D0D1E.quest_desc: [
		"Potassium is a plant nutrient. It is used in &6HV&r to make ender pearl dust, and with sodium it makes sodium-potassium, which &6HV&r+ energy hatches are made with."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r by electrolyzing rock salt dust (from TFC sylvite) and as a byproduct of processing TFC saltpeter."
	]
	quest.19C743189F6D0D1E.quest_subtitle: "Element #19"
	quest.19C743189F6D0D1E.title: "Potassium"
	quest.19F0503A32E6F671.quest_desc: [
		"Platinum is a high-tier GregTech metal: platinum cables and uranium triplatinum, the &5EV&r superconductor."
		""
		"It comes from GregTech's platinum line: a chemical reactor turns purified TFC tetrahedrite ore and nitric acid into platinum group sludge, and centrifuging the sludge with aqua regia (&6HV&r) gives raw platinum dust, which an electrolyzer splits into platinum."
	]
	quest.19F0503A32E6F671.quest_subtitle: "Element #78"
	quest.19F0503A32E6F671.title: "Platinum"
	quest.1A7D1D59EE94B474.quest_desc: [
		"Iodine has little use in GregTech (potassium iodide); it is here for the set."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &6HV&r: a chemical reactor makes it from a dried kelp block, hydrogen and hydrogen peroxide. Craft the block from nine TFC dried kelp or dried seaweed (dry fresh seaweed by a fire)."
	]
	quest.1A7D1D59EE94B474.quest_subtitle: "Element #53"
	quest.1A7D1D59EE94B474.title: "Iodine"
	quest.1AAA28B8C34007A2.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Rotation Speed Controller&r can simplify all of your cogwheel spaghetti into a single block, letting you adjust RPM in a simple, compact way. These will be useful later when you have more machines to balance your stress units between!"
	]
	quest.1AAA28B8C34007A2.quest_subtitle: "No more manual gear ratios!"
	quest.1AAA28B8C34007A2.title: "Rotation Speed Controller"
	quest.1AD111C96EB2B0F4.quest_desc: [
		"&aNOR Memory Chips&r go into the Nano Processor Computer, your second kind of &1IV&r Circuit."
		""
		"Engrave a Phosphorus Wafer with a &dPink&r lens in an &6HV&r Laser Engraver, then cut it into chips, both inside your Cleanroom."
	]
	quest.1AD111C96EB2B0F4.title: "NOR Memory"
	quest.1B4103562A9C617E.quest_desc: [
		"As always, we highly encourage you to use a &bBattery Buffer&r, so even if you use more &6energy&r than you produce, you won't run out of it right away, and you will be able to get the energy back while your machines aren't running."
	]
	quest.1B4103562A9C617E.quest_subtitle: "Energy management"
	quest.1B4103562A9C617E.title: "MV Battery Buffer"
	quest.1B850FA897BE6912.quest_desc: [
		"In the early game, you have a few simple storage options:"
		""
		"&lChest&r: Chests are cheap and easy to craft from lumber and have 18 slots. They hold items up to Large in size; Very Large items such as logs don't fit."
		""
		"&lCrate&r: A Crate stores a single kind of item, but up to 36 stacks of it."
		""
		"&lLarge Vessels&r: The cheapest to craft, only requiring clay, with nine slots. Sealed, they're ideal for food preservation. Available in a wide variety of colors too!"
		""
		"Baskets, shelves and tool racks round things out (see the field guide's Storage page). Keep food in sealed vessels: food left in chests can attract rats."
	]
	quest.1B850FA897BE6912.quest_subtitle: "Time to stop carrying all your junk in vessels"
	quest.1B850FA897BE6912.title: "Early Storage Options"
	quest.1BAADD5400F302BB.quest_desc: [
		"Tantalum is used to make tantalum capacitors and SMD resistors."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here. Centrifuge lava (&bMV&r) for a little tantalite, then electrolyze the tantalite for tantalum and manganese."
	]
	quest.1BAADD5400F302BB.quest_subtitle: "Element #73"
	quest.1BAADD5400F302BB.title: "Tantalum"
	quest.1BEEDB28C0DD1FD3.quest_desc: [
		"Your first &eNano Circuits&r! They need &bNano CPU Chips&r and the SMD components you've been making, all in the &5EV&r Circuit Assembler inside your Cleanroom."
		""
		"At first, &eNano Circuits&r will feel quite expensive, but once your Nano CPU production is fully passive, they will turn into one of your cheapest ones!"
	]
	quest.1BEEDB28C0DD1FD3.quest_subtitle: "It doesn't &olook&r that much smaller..."
	quest.1BEEDB28C0DD1FD3.title: "It doesn't &olook&r that much smaller..."
	quest.1C16C78A27F7378C.quest_desc: [
		"It's quite the investment to own a &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r, but it is &oby far&r the most prominent &6source of Oil&r."
		""
		"It pumps fluids from underneath Bedrock itself. Note that the fluids aren't actually there, instead being simulated."
		""
		"Fluid veins are stored within &cchunk-aligned regions&r. Each vein has a different fluid, but they are mostly types of Oil."
		""
		"You can't prospect for fluid veins &oyet&r: the &6HV&r prospector has a fluid mode."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Each vein generates with a different base yield. When drained, fluid veins slowly deplete, and their yield drops until it reaches the vein's depletion yield. At that point, you should move the Rig to a different vein."
		""
		"Higher tier Rigs massively increase the yield (see the multiplier in their tooltip) while depleting the vein more slowly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lWhat you can find in the &2Overworld&r&l:&r"
		""
		"&9Oil:&r richer in &aLight Oil Residue&r, the most appreciated variant."
		"&9Light Oil:&r richer in &aRefinery Gas&r, usable for power."
		"&9Heavy Oil:&r richer in &aHeavy Oil Residue&r, which has more niche uses, notably Toluene."
		"&9Raw Oil:&r richer in &aNaphtha&r, the best source of the early-game oil products."
		"&9Natural Gas:&r grants &aRefinery Gas&r with no distillation required."
		"&9Salt Water:&r grants &aSodium Hydroxide&r and &aChlorine&r, useful later."
		""
		"When starting out, you may have to tap randomly until you find something you like. Remember that whatever you pump could also fuel your Fluid Rig."
	]
	quest.1C16C78A27F7378C.quest_subtitle: "Fluid Drilling Rigs in CEu!"
	quest.1C16C78A27F7378C.title: "Fluid Drilling Rigs"
	quest.1C718DA55BE73FB2.quest_desc: [
		"Samarium makes samarium-iron-arsenic oxide and magnetic samarium."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aCassiterite&r gives &aMonazite&r as its &3Ore Washer&r by-product. An &3Electrolyzer&r splits monazite dust into rare earth and phosphate, and a &3Centrifuge&r separates rare earth into small piles of cadmium, neodymium, samarium, cerium, yttrium and lanthanum."
	]
	quest.1C718DA55BE73FB2.quest_subtitle: "Element #62"
	quest.1C718DA55BE73FB2.title: "Samarium"
	quest.1D65B1624ED9051B.quest_desc: [
		"&aDiesel&r is an &dOil-based &9Combustion Fuel&r."
		""
		"Mix &aLight Oil Residue&r and &aHeavy Oil Residue&r at &65:1&r in an &bMV&r &3Mixer&r. From &dOil&r or &dRaw Oil&r that means several Distilleries making Light Oil Residue for every one making Heavy Oil Residue."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You can cut the amount of &dOil&r required &6drastically&r by distilling &dHeavy Oil&r for the &aHeavy Oil Residue&r specifically: it gives far more of it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In general, it is better to prioritize placing down more machines (&dparallelisation&r) over overclocking the recipes. That way, you end up losing less energy processing the resources."
		""
		"&aDiesel&r is burned in a &3Combustion Generator&r. It can be further refined to &6Cetane-Boosted Diesel&r in &6HV&r. Compared to the other power sources, it is generally more efficient, but a more demanding processing line. If you take the &eOil&r route for &aPolyethylene&r, this can work great with existing infrastructure. Ultimately, the power source you want to use is your choice."
	]
	quest.1D65B1624ED9051B.quest_subtitle: "Mother, how is diesel made?"
	quest.1D65B1624ED9051B.title: "The Church of Diesel"
	quest.1D7F91FACA33E551.quest_desc: [
		"Combine your new Saw with a Log in your crafting grid to create Lumber. 4 Lumber can then be crafted into Planks..."
		""
		" and once you have 4 planks, its time to make your very first Workbench."
	]
	quest.1D7F91FACA33E551.quest_subtitle: "3x3 crafting is within your grasp"
	quest.1D7F91FACA33E551.title: "Time for the Workbench"
	quest.1D8F9A3BCF306583.quest_desc: [
		"Be careful what you carry! GregTech marks some materials &cHazardous&r on their tooltip (hold Shift for the details), and carrying them builds up a &6Medical Condition&r with nasty effects, up to and including &cdeath&r."
		""
		"If a debuff suddenly appears, get that item out of your inventory and into a chest!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You will eventually need to work with some of these materials, so you have ways to deal with them."
		""
		"The best way is to avoid getting any conditions in the first place: GregTech's Face Mask and Rubber Gloves protect against some hazards (their tooltips list which). Many conditions fade on their own, but some are &epermanent&r; GregTech's Paracetamol and RadAway pills, made much later, are its medicine."
	]
	quest.1D8F9A3BCF306583.quest_subtitle: "Don't eat the Asbestos"
	quest.1D8F9A3BCF306583.title: "Medical Conditions"
	quest.1E1EE320E78FF5A1.quest_desc: [
		"A new world starts in early summer (June), with each month lasting 8 days. Seasons will change, and with them the temperature and rainfall, which affect crops, fruit trees, bushes and whether snow and ice form."
		""
		"The Calendar and Climate tabs of your inventory show the date, the season, and your location's average and current temperature and rainfall. This world is a real-scale Earth, so its climate is the climate of the real place you're standing in: pick your farm site accordingly."
	]
	quest.1E1EE320E78FF5A1.quest_subtitle: "The weather for today? Pain."
	quest.1E1EE320E78FF5A1.title: "Weather"
	quest.1E4555A7AE8262F5.title: "Bronze Age"
	quest.1EAAC6402699B554.quest_desc: [
		"With the new version of &5Gregtech&r, a &chazard system&r has been introduced. By holding &dShift&r while hovering over &cHazardous Materials&r, you can see how they might affect you."
		""
		"We strongly advise using proper &6protective equipment&r to keep your &corgans intact&r."
	]
	quest.1EAAC6402699B554.quest_subtitle: "Choking Hazard, Ages 3+"
	quest.1EAAC6402699B554.title: "Hazardous Materials"
	quest.1F550EAB25A17073.quest_desc: [
		"You now have access to two &3new Maintenance Hatches&r. "
		""
		"The &3Automatic Maintenance Hatch&r is pretty simple - it eliminates the need for Maintenance, &6forever&r."
		""
		"The &3Configurable Maintenance Hatch&r is more interesting. You can configure it to cut off &a10%% duration&r on recipes, at the cost of making Maintenance happen three times as fast. That is &d16 real hours&r of activity. Additionally, you can use it on Multiblock Generators to increase the duration of the recipe, which indirectly increases their fuel efficiency by 10%%!"
		""
		"&9Reminder:&r You can put Tape in the maintenance Hatch to automatically fix problems."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Automatic Maintenance Hatch texture and mechanic comes from TecTech, an addon mod originally made for GregTech: New Horizons."
	]
	quest.1F550EAB25A17073.quest_subtitle: "I have become maintenance, eater of tape"
	quest.1F550EAB25A17073.title: "Advanced Maintenance"
	quest.1F6D4A7FD8AED990.quest_desc: [
		"&3Item Pipes&r are a simple yet effective way to move items around &dinstantly&r, but with throughput limits. Higher tier pipes provide ridiculously large throughput - a rare sight in modded Minecraft!"
		""
		"Item Pipes &9do not pull&r: they push any item inserted into them to connected inventories, prioritizing &9the closest inventory&r. Restrictive pipes are the last choice."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For now, feed them with Create funnels, &6Chutes&r and &6Hoppers&r; in LV, Conveyor Modules, Output Buses and machine Auto-Outputs join in."
		""
		"&9Note:&r pipes connect only to the block they were placed against. To open more connections, use your &5Wrench&r."
		""
		"Get &eany&r of the suggested Item Pipes to complete this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Oooooh, YEAH! Item Pipes were in GregTech 5, and for whatever reason they weren't kept for GTCE, so you had to use other mods to transport items. Who does that!? We hope you enjoy Item Pipes being back in GregTech!"
	]
	quest.1F6D4A7FD8AED990.quest_subtitle: "Not as cool as Item Conduits"
	quest.1F6D4A7FD8AED990.title: "Item Pipes"
	quest.1FB8988A3629E12E.quest_desc: [
		"Along the mid-ocean ridge's axis, a field of sulfide chimneys stands on a mound about every thirty kilometres. They glow faintly and puff dark water from the tip. A pickaxe gives raw chalcopyrite, pyrite, sphalerite and galena."
		""
		"Arc vents are white smokers: anhydrite, some zinc sulfide and, once in a while, pollucite (caesium)."
		""
		"The ridge is far from the coast: ocean floor 3,000 blocks across, with the axis a thin band in the middle. Magma rock and rising bubbles mark it."
	]
	quest.1FB8988A3629E12E.quest_subtitle: "Black smokers on the ridge"
	quest.1FB8988A3629E12E.title: "A Vent Field"
	quest.1FEA76E5FEB963DD.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Rubber Gloves&r will obviously protect you from &cskin contact hazards&r. Two &7Rubber Plates&r on the crafting grid is all they take."
	]
	quest.1FEA76E5FEB963DD.title: "Rubber Gloves"
	quest.2006CA886B1141B8.quest_desc: [
		"Cobalt is used in &7LV&r to make cobalt brass (brass, aluminium and cobalt in the mixer), whose buzzsaw blade goes into the &7LV&r cutter, and later in various alloys."
		""
		"It can be obtained as a byproduct of processing TFC native copper: macerating or washing crushed copper ore."
	]
	quest.2006CA886B1141B8.quest_subtitle: "Element #27"
	quest.2006CA886B1141B8.title: "Cobalt"
	quest.203136B9BD051792.quest_desc: [
		"Rocks can be \"Knapped\", which is the process of shaping a basic material into a usable form by smacking them together. Rock Knapping requires at least two rocks: hold them and right-click the air to open the Knapping interface. You can then \"chip off\" pieces of your rock to create a stone tool head. All the shapes for different tools can be found in EMI and the Field Guide."
		""
		"The two most important tools for the beginning of your journey are a Stone Knife and a Stone Axe, so try knapping those tool heads."
	]
	quest.203136B9BD051792.quest_subtitle: "Just like the olden days of the Paleolithic"
	quest.203136B9BD051792.title: "Knapping"
	quest.20333D881D8BE863.quest_desc: [
		"&dChlorine&r is a core component of your chemical toolkit. You’ll need &da lot of it&r for various reactions and crafting steps—the first one being &dHydrochloric Acid&r."
		""
		"There are many ways to obtain &dChlorine&r, but the main source is &dsalt&r. It’s basically everywhere, so you won’t struggle to find it."
		""
		"We recommend &aelectrolyzing seawater&r as an early method, but keep in mind—it’s &eslow&r."
	]
	quest.20333D881D8BE863.quest_subtitle: "Salty Gas"
	quest.20333D881D8BE863.title: "Chlorine Gas"
	quest.20AB26816E6BDB6B.quest_desc: [
		"Knap a Jug out of clay and fire it in a Pit Kiln. A Ceramic Jug is the earliest liquid container you can craft, but it only holds 100 mB, so you'll need to refill it after every drink: right-click water with it, then hold right-click to drink."
		""
		"The Jug is relatively fragile and has a small chance to break when you drink from it! You can also blow into it to make it whistle."
	]
	quest.20AB26816E6BDB6B.quest_subtitle: "Relatively easy water"
	quest.20AB26816E6BDB6B.title: "Ceramic Jug"
	quest.214FE96C0C15902B.quest_desc: [
		"You can now &3centrifuge&r &aSticky Resin&r, which will give you &aGlue&r in fluid form, plus raw rubber and the occasional Plantball."
		""
		"Give yourself a headstart and get on producing Glue. You can use it to make &6cheaper Resistors&r, as well as &6cheaper Circuit Boards&r in the &3Assembler&r."
	]
	quest.214FE96C0C15902B.quest_subtitle: "What a sticky situation"
	quest.214FE96C0C15902B.title: "Glued"
	quest.21B45E517A0921FC.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the organic &dEthylene&r path! The goal here is to produce &dEthanol&r and react it with &dSulfuric Acid&r to make &dEthylene&r."
		""
		"To get &dEthanol&r, you'll need to distill it from &aBiomass&r, so let's look at the ways to produce that biomass."
		""
		"The first method is simple: put &asaplings&r (TFC's count) into a &dBrewery&r with water. The downside? &eIt's slow&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The second method yields much better results. Macerate &bPlant Balls&r into &aBio Chaff&r."
		""
		"&bPlant Balls&r can be obtained by:"
		"-Compressing &asaplings&r (one sapling makes one plant ball)"
		"-Centrifuging &9rubber logs&r or &9sticky resin&r"
		""
		"Finally, process your &aBio Chaff&r with water in a &dBrewery&r, or go for a &dPyrolyse Oven&r for &e66 percent more&r biomass."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o You may recognise Plantballs from IndustrialCraft2! In IC2 Experimental, there was this rather... obscure way to turn Biomass into Biogas for power, which sadly required too much investment to be really worth it."
	]
	quest.21B45E517A0921FC.quest_subtitle: "Plants aren't industrial enough!"
	quest.21B45E517A0921FC.title: "Biomass"
	quest.21E9C3AB3603B368.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Chemical Reactor&r will be required for &la lot&r of recipes."
		""
		"Let's give it a spin: it makes &6Rubber three times cheaper&r than the alloy smelter. 9 raw rubber and 1 sulfur give 1296 mB of molten Rubber, nine ingots' worth, where the alloy smelter takes 3 raw rubber per ingot. Molten Rubber has to go into another machine, though."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Here are some &aother machines&r you might want to aim for:"
		""
		"A &3Fluid Solidifier&r is useful to solidify your Rubber directly into &aRubber Sheets&r. You'll want these moving forward."
		""
		"You could then make use of an &3Assembler&r to use your molten Rubber for &aCables&r. This isn't important for Tin Cables, but better cables will &eneed&r to be made in the Assembler."
	]
	quest.21E9C3AB3603B368.quest_subtitle: "Chemistry for dummies"
	quest.21E9C3AB3603B368.title: "Basic Chemical Reactor"
	quest.224BC4703FE4BD42.quest_desc: [
		"As with any good tech mod, &5GregTech&r comes with a wide variety of &6tools&r you can use. To operate them, you'll need to &acharge them with energy&r — and there are several ways to do that: place the tool in a &6Battery Buffer&r, in an &denergy slot&r of a machine, or even better, use a &eTurbo Charger&r."
		""
		"Just remember: you can only charge an item using a power source of &7equal&r or &ahigher tier&r. &cLower-tier sources&r won’t work on higher-tier tools — but don’t worry, &cnothing should explode&r. Probably."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Most &5GregTech&r power tools are crafted from a material's &6Tool Head&r (a Drill Head, a Chainsaw Head...) and a &6Power Unit&r. Try using &aEMI&r to explore what you can do with them — just remember two important things:"
		""
		"- The &ePower Unit's tier&r (LV, MV, HV...) sets the tool's tier and the &6size of its battery&r."
		"- The &cmaterial&r of the head decides how good the tool itself is."
	]
	quest.224BC4703FE4BD42.quest_subtitle: "Men only want one thing and it's f&kuck&ring disgusting"
	quest.224BC4703FE4BD42.title: "Power Tools"
	quest.22B7A03791E961C1.quest_desc: [
		"Ore veins generate differently than what you might be used to - you can't just wander into a random cave. Instead, look for small pieces of ore lying on the surface among the loose rocks and sticks."
		""
		"Can't find anything that melts into Copper (native copper, malachite or tetrahedrite)? Try looking in another rock type -- different ores spawn in different rocks. The field guide's ores section tells you where each one is found."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"These small pieces are indicators: a larger vein of the same ore lies somewhere nearby, probably underground and close to the surface. You don't have a pickaxe yet, so take note of the place where you found the ore! It'll be very useful later on."
		""
		"Each piece is worth 10 mB of metal (an ingot is 100 mB), so collect as many as you can, but make sure you make a note of where you found them!"
	]
	quest.22B7A03791E961C1.quest_subtitle: "Your first metal is already available if you look for it."
	quest.22B7A03791E961C1.title: "Pebbles with ore?"
	quest.22E35FC12304838C.quest_desc: [
		"Bismuth is used in the bronze age to make bismuth bronze."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC bismuthinite; GregTech's macerator grinds it straight into bismuth dust."
	]
	quest.22E35FC12304838C.quest_subtitle: "Element #83"
	quest.22E35FC12304838C.title: "Bismuth"
	quest.22F653B8888E16CC.quest_desc: [
		"This is it—the &6HV Machine Hull&r! Congratulations on reaching this major milestone."
		""
		"You had to manage &dchemicals&r, upgrade your &dEBF&r, mix a &cnew alloy&r, and learn about &aWafers&r and the &aLaser Engraver&r. We hope your &aunderstanding of GregTech&r is growing stronger every day."
		""
		"From now on, &ecomplexity will increase&r at each tier, but you’ll also gain access to &anew machines&r that will ease earlier processes and introduce &9interesting new mechanics&r."
		""
		"Even though you’ve just unlocked the &6HV Chapter&r, remember that this marks only &atwo&r of the &bMV Chapter&r’s main milestones."
		""
		"If you haven’t unlocked the &6Second HV Circuit&r yet, we highly encourage you to do so before moving forward."
		""
		"Otherwise, &aWelcome to HV!&r"
	]
	quest.22F653B8888E16CC.quest_subtitle: "That's your fourth machine hull! This is progression"
	quest.22F653B8888E16CC.title: "The HV Machine Hull"
	quest.22F7F6CFF45D44B7.quest_desc: [
		"The Gas Collector collects Air that can then be centrifuged into &aOxygen&r and &aNitrogen&r."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5 players remember when they had to use a Compressor with IC2 cells to get Compressed Air... here, cell chemistry is no more."
	]
	quest.22F7F6CFF45D44B7.quest_subtitle: "It'll take your breath away"
	quest.22F7F6CFF45D44B7.title: "Basic Gas Collector"
	quest.232B30864EA11BB6.quest_desc: [
		"GregTech comes with its own tools to help solve ore processing logistics."
		""
		"The &6Robot Arm&r can move precise numbers of items into a machine. The &6Tag Filter&r can filter items by tag, such as '&5*purified_ores*&r' to match all Purified Ores."
		""
		"The &4Smart Filter&r can filter items depending on their &6recipe&r. For example, if you use it with a robot arm on an electrolyzer, and set the robot arm to supply exact, it will only move your dusts into the electrolyzer once it has as many inputs as the recipe requires!"
	]
	quest.232B30864EA11BB6.quest_subtitle: "Providing answers to its own problems"
	quest.232B30864EA11BB6.title: "Ore processing with GregTech's own tools"
	quest.2354D80A310ED7CB.quest_desc: [
		"You could waste &o&eprecious years of your life&r in EMI looking for the most optimal Oxygen recipe, given the many ways to obtain it. Various minerals will produce it when electrolyzed."
		""
		"If only the quest book had more information!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Surprise! The best source according to us (!) is &acentrifuging Air&r after making a &dGas Collector&r, which you might not be able to make just yet. This recipe also gives &aNitrogen&r, which is handy as it can speed up certain &3Electric Blast Furnace&r recipes."
		""
		"The second best source according to us (!) is &aelectrolyzing Silicon Dioxide&r, which also gives you silicon. EMI shows where to get Silicon Dioxide."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The third best source according to us (!) is &aelectrolyzing Water&r. It's slow and costly, so it suits &1Hydrogen&r production better. &4Don't use this method as your main source of Oxygen&r."
		""
		"The fourth best source according to us (!) is &ato not void&r it, EVER! Any Oxygen obtained from any source is worth something and should be stored in Tanks."
	]
	quest.2354D80A310ED7CB.quest_subtitle: "Achtually, it's Dioxygen..."
	quest.2354D80A310ED7CB.title: "Breath of Fresh Oxygen"
	quest.23825C07601E4DD7.quest_desc: [
		"Most of GregTech's LV recipes go through the assembler."
		""
		"It's &cexpensive&r (two robot arms and two conveyor modules), but it pays back fast with better recipes:"
		"&9-&r &6Vacuum Tubes&r: two per craft, three with molten red alloy and four with annealed copper wire too, instead of one by hand"
		"&9-&r &6Resistors&r: two per craft with glue, four with annealed copper fine wire"
		"&9-&r &6Circuit Boards&r: four copper foils and glue instead of eight copper wires"
	]
	quest.23825C07601E4DD7.quest_subtitle: "GregTech's workhorse"
	quest.23825C07601E4DD7.title: "Assembler"
	quest.23972FD3A008121D.quest_desc: [
		"Cells are an alternative form of Fluid storage. All Cell types with the same type and amount of Fluid inside them &6stack&r. They can be automatically filled with a &3Canning Machine&r."
		""
		"The basic Fluid Cells hold &done bucket&r of Fluid, while the Steel Cells hold eight buckets."
		""
		"Not sold on them yet? Unlike drums and buckets, cells &asafely contain&r their contents, preventing you from getting burnt, frozen, or floating. They're also significantly cheaper!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Universal Cells hold up to &done bucket&r, but also can store &9fractions&r of Buckets. They're particularly ideal if you want to store leftover Fluid without crafting a whole Drum. "
		""
		"Cells made from higher tier materials can hold even more fluid, but &9Drums&r and &9Super Tanks&r can hold even more."
		""
		"Like Drums, Cells can be placed into a crafting grid to clear their contents."
	]
	quest.23972FD3A008121D.quest_subtitle: "You can see inside, unlike those drums..."
	quest.23972FD3A008121D.title: "Better bucket"
	quest.2399E4EF4131F58E.quest_desc: [
		"GregTech's LV motors are built around two Create shafts, with copper wire and a magnetic iron rod."
		""
		"The full recipe: two Create shafts, four copper wires, two tin cables and a magnetic iron (or steel) rod. Magnetize the rod with redstone by hand, or for free in a Polarizer. Make plenty: the first LV machines take up to four motors each, and every pump and piston hides one (conveyors two)."
		""
		"&2EMI is your friend&r: the recipe tree button at the bottom right of a recipe breaks it down into everything it needs, and can add a shopping list to your favourites."
	]
	quest.2399E4EF4131F58E.quest_subtitle: "Around a Create shaft"
	quest.2399E4EF4131F58E.title: "LV Motor"
	quest.23B41740510DCA4B.quest_desc: [
		"Molds allow you to make copper and bronze versions of most weapons, including three new types: Swords, Scythes, and Maces."
		""
		"Swords: These well rounded weapons deal &6Slashing&r damage."
		""
		"Scythes: They also deal &6Slashing&r damage."
		""
		"Maces: Heavy weapons that deal &2Crushing&r damage, a Skeleton's worst nightmare."
	]
	quest.23B41740510DCA4B.quest_subtitle: "The power of metal"
	quest.23B41740510DCA4B.title: "Molded Weapons"
	quest.23D84898362C0D7C.quest_desc: [
		"With the Steel Anvil, you'll be able to work Steel Ingots into different forms."
		""
		"Steel tools and equipment have a significant boost over their bronze and wrought iron counterparts, so they're worth making if your existing ones are about to break. You'll be needing to create a lot of alloys soon, so some new mining equipment would be a wise investment."
	]
	quest.23D84898362C0D7C.quest_subtitle: "A huge leap from wrought iron"
	quest.23D84898362C0D7C.title: "T4 Anvil: Steel"
	quest.244DFE17A8DDAF4A.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack andesite alloy takes TFC &6andesite, basalt, dacite, rhyolite or diorite&r (raw or cobble) plus zinc or bronze nuggets."
		""
		"Craft an ingot into nine nuggets."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFinding the rock&r"
		""
		"Loose rocks on the ground are the rock right under the soil, so they show what you're standing on."
		""
		"&6Volcanic regions&r (around volcanoes, volcanic islands and rifts) are mostly andesite, basalt, dacite or rhyolite. On ordinary land about one rock area in six has one of them on top; each area is about 1,000 blocks across. Mountain ranges never do, but some have diorite on top."
		""
		"&6Diorite dikes&r are everywhere: upright pipes of diorite about 30 blocks across and a few hundred blocks apart, usually topping out a few blocks under the soil. Look for speckled grey-white rock in cliffs, riverbanks, ravines and cave walls, or where loose rocks don't match the rock you dig into."
	]
	quest.244DFE17A8DDAF4A.quest_subtitle: "Create starts here"
	quest.244DFE17A8DDAF4A.title: "Andesite Alloy"
	quest.251B952BB2E8EBBE.quest_desc: [
		"Turns a build into a moving physics contraption: carts, boats and airships. Ground vehicles need no brass."
	]
	quest.251B952BB2E8EBBE.quest_subtitle: "Builds that move"
	quest.251B952BB2E8EBBE.title: "Physics Assembler"
	quest.253E1462DF747E17.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Alloy Blast Smelter&r is a very special multiblock. It works similarly to the &6EBF&r, with better coils allowing for Perfect Overclocking (see the power chapter), and it can process most EBF alloys straight from their element dusts &a25%% faster&r. Note that it outputs molten fluids instead of hot ingots!"
		""
		"One key feature of the &6ABS&r is its ability to craft the alloys needed for &6Large Multiblock Machines&r. Essentially, every basic machine like the Macerator or the Distillery has its own multiblock, offering extensive customization options such as multiple Input/Output Buses/Hatches or even adding a Parallel Hatch."
	]
	quest.253E1462DF747E17.quest_subtitle: "We love this heater"
	quest.253E1462DF747E17.title: "We love this heater"
	quest.258F8EDB171D5CDC.quest_desc: [
		"EMI might look a little overwhelming here, so we'll go through the best path for Sulfuric Acid here."
		""
		"Making &eSulfuric Acid&r is a three step process. It is used in many important reactions, so you should automate its production ASAP."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To automate it, you will need &3three LV Chemical Reactors&r. We would recommend building a dedicated setup somewhere with &3a single LV Generator&r to power all three machines. You can then spaghetti your pipes to handle input and output."
		""
		"&9-&r Step 1: React &aSulfur&r (crush TFC sulfur or pyrite) with &bOxygen&r to form &aSulfur Dioxide&r."
		"&9-&r Step 2: React &aSulfur Dioxide&r with more &bOxygen&r to form &aSulfur Trioxide&r."
		"&9-&r Step 3: React &aSulfur Trioxide&r with &bWater&r to form &eSulfuric Acid&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5's Chemical Reactor only had one Fluid slot. To circumvent that, they would do &dcell chemistry&f. The way you would automate Sulfuric Acid was by having one cell travel from machine to machine and then loop back to its starting position. A somewhat fun and interesting automation challenge, but also a chore!"
	]
	quest.258F8EDB171D5CDC.quest_subtitle: "...what he thought was H2O was H2SO4!"
	quest.258F8EDB171D5CDC.title: "Sulfuric Acid"
	quest.25AF0DF88BA3E529.quest_desc: [
		"Our warmest congratulations on making it here."
		""
		"The way you should obtain &aEthylene&r was described in the previous Quest, depending on the route you chose."
		""
		"&aEthylene&r will shortly be used in polymer production. It's also useful in a few other reactions."
	]
	quest.25AF0DF88BA3E529.quest_subtitle: "One of many hydrocarbons"
	quest.25AF0DF88BA3E529.title: "Ethylene"
	quest.25B0BF87328E2546.quest_desc: [
		"&8ULV&r Circuits stand in for Vacuum Tubes: every &7LV&r Electronic Circuit made in the Circuit Assembler takes two. One Simple SoC becomes 8 &aNAND Chips&r on a Phenolic board, or 12 on a Plastic board, which makes this the cheapest ULV circuit by far."
	]
	quest.25B0BF87328E2546.title: "Best ULV circuits!"
	quest.25B7ECAFDADE0A45.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations! With your Workbench you've officially entered the Peak of the Stone Age. With it you'll be able to craft a multitude of new things with the items you've gathered so far. In this pack TFC workbenches also count as crafting tables wherever a recipe asks for one."
		""
		"Now comes your main goal of the Primitive Age: proper metalworking with the Copper Anvil."
		""
		"Sidenote: While you could gather enough materials to make 14 ingots of bronze right now, you won't be able to turn them into a bronze anvil without crafting the copper one first, sorry! At least anvils are recyclable: an anvil melts back into all 14 ingots' worth of metal."
	]
	quest.25B7ECAFDADE0A45.quest_subtitle: "This... is a Crafting Table"
	quest.25B7ECAFDADE0A45.title: "Workbench"
	quest.26928A83F63777A9.quest_desc: [
		"Shafts from andesite alloy, cogwheels from shafts and planks. TFC workbenches count as crafting tables everywhere."
		""
		"Large cogwheels (a shaft or cogwheel with more planks) mesh with small ones to double or halve the speed: gear your machines up or down as they need."
	]
	quest.26928A83F63777A9.quest_subtitle: "Moving parts"
	quest.26928A83F63777A9.title: "Shafts and Cogwheels"
	quest.26CB1992A45CFEF6.quest_desc: [
		"Alloy copper (88-92%) with tin from cassiterite (8-12%) in a vessel. Bismuth bronze and black bronze work too."
	]
	quest.26CB1992A45CFEF6.quest_subtitle: "Copper and tin"
	quest.26CB1992A45CFEF6.title: "Bronze"
	quest.270F428D177E3320.quest_desc: [
		"Oh good lord, 128 ingots for 16 coils, that's a lot of &cKanthal&r... And what the heck is this &chot ingot&r thing?"
		""
		"Kanthal comes out of the EBF as a &cHot Ingot&r, and unlike hot metal in &aTerraFirmaCraft&r, &cit doesn't cool down on its own&r! You'll need to actively &acool it&r down."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To do that, place hot ingots into a &dChemical Bath&r with &9Water&r, or even better, &9Distilled Water&r for a faster cooling time."
		""
		"We highly recommend you &aautomate&r this process: use &apipes&r to send them directly from your &dEBF&r to your &dChemical Bath&r."
		""
		"You can also set up an &aItem Tag Filter&r to help with sorting the hot ingots &7#c:hot_ingots&r."
	]
	quest.270F428D177E3320.quest_subtitle: "This one is hot"
	quest.270F428D177E3320.title: "Kanthal"
	quest.2718A3ECD4BDF513.quest_desc: [
		"Chainsaws are a power tool you might craft for faster tree felling, but they also make for good melee weapons!"
	]
	quest.2718A3ECD4BDF513.quest_subtitle: "Hockey mask not included"
	quest.2718A3ECD4BDF513.title: "Chainsaws"
	quest.2762BE4E551907EA.quest_desc: [
		"The advanced chestplate is &oalmost&r as good as creative-mode flight."
		""
		"It's amazing for whizzing around your base, with its only downside being that it drains its internal battery fairly quickly."
		""
		"Keep a couple extra batteries on you, then they can charge up the suit by enabling Discharge mode on them with &aSneak-Right-Click&r."
	]
	quest.2762BE4E551907EA.quest_subtitle: "FREEEE BIIIIIIRD"
	quest.2762BE4E551907EA.title: "Advanced NanoMuscle™ Chestplate"
	quest.27A6BBDBA788F4CD.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, right-click a Cauldron of water with Impure or Purified Dust to wash it into clean Dust, your ore's final form. A cauldron takes seven wrought iron plates; later the ore washer and the centrifuge do this in bulk, with byproducts."
		""
		"Clean dust smelts into an ingot, and many GregTech recipes take it directly."
	]
	quest.27A6BBDBA788F4CD.quest_subtitle: "Wash that dirty dust"
	quest.27A6BBDBA788F4CD.title: "Early Ore Processing - Part 3"
	quest.27A80F0C09BF21BA.quest_desc: [
		"HV Macerators now output byproducts! If you don't have a dedicated ore processing setup yet, now is definitely the time to build one."
	]
	quest.27A80F0C09BF21BA.title: "&6HV&r Ore Processing"
	quest.27D4B8BC08AA1F81.quest_desc: [
		"No river nearby? A windmill turns anywhere it has room. Build at least eight sails (wool, sticks and andesite alloy) onto a windmill bearing and right-click the bearing to start it; every eight more sails add speed."
	]
	quest.27D4B8BC08AA1F81.quest_subtitle: "Pairs well with tulips"
	quest.27D4B8BC08AA1F81.title: "Windmills"
	quest.27F1083F6FFE9CDF.quest_desc: [
		"Going forward, Silicon will be essential for anything involving electronics, so it's definitely something you're going to want a reliable setup for."
		""
		"To obtain &5Silicon&r, we'll suggest &ctwo main methods&r so you have clear directions. As always, it's up to you to figure out what's &abest for your situation&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"First method: electrolyzing minerals. &aClay Dust&r (macerated clay) gives Silicon along with Aluminium, Sodium and Lithium, and so do &9Emerald&r and the &9Garnets&r from Ruby processing. Centrifuging &cRedstone&r also yields a little."
		""
		"Second method: although slower early on, making Silicon out of cobblestone becomes the &ebest method&r later. Plus, it generates &9Oxygen&r as a bonus!"
		""
		"The idea is simple: electrolyze &aSilicon Dioxide Dust&r into Oxygen and Silicon. You get Silicon Dioxide Dust by centrifuging &9Flint Dust&r, and a &3Sifter&r turns gravel (hammered or milled from cobblestone) into plenty of Flint."
		""
		"This setup can become &afully passive&r easily. Try using EMI's &aRecipe Tree&r to plan your builds; it really helps!"
	]
	quest.27F1083F6FFE9CDF.quest_subtitle: "Sillycon"
	quest.27F1083F6FFE9CDF.title: "Silicon Dust"
	quest.27F634389AA42D40.quest_desc: [
		"Just like regular clay, fire clay can be knapped into things that you'll then need to fire (1399 °C). Most importantly, it makes the crucible and fire bricks."
		""
		"Fire ingot molds break only 1 time in 100, against 1 in 10 for a clay ingot mold."
		""
		"You can also make a mold table and casting channels: connect mold tables to a crucible with channels to cast into several molds at once. Use the channel next to the crucible to start pouring, or give it a redstone pulse."
	]
	quest.27F634389AA42D40.quest_subtitle: "Extremely Heat Resistant Clay"
	quest.27F634389AA42D40.title: "Fire Clay products"
	quest.28203C51BE80D3C4.quest_desc: [
		"Palladium is used to make rhodium-plated palladium, the base material of &dLuV&r."
		""
		"It comes from GregTech's platinum line: a chemical reactor turns purified TFC tetrahedrite ore and nitric acid into platinum group sludge, and centrifuging the sludge with aqua regia (&6HV&r) gives raw palladium dust, which a chemical reactor turns into palladium with hydrochloric acid."
	]
	quest.28203C51BE80D3C4.quest_subtitle: "Element #46"
	quest.28203C51BE80D3C4.title: "Palladium"
	quest.2827645A006C231F.quest_desc: [
		"Battery Buffers are your basic machines to store and manage energy — though technically, they don't store energy on their own. They simply serve as a housing for your batteries."
		""
		"&c⚠ If you don't want them to explode&r:"
		"- &4Never input higher-tier energy&r into a lower-tier Battery Buffer."
		"- Batteries can only be charged if they are of &cequal or lower tier&r than the Battery Buffer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"A Battery Buffer takes in up to two amps and puts out one amp for each battery inside."
		"So a full 4x Battery Buffer can take in &a8A&r — but will only output &e4A&r max."
		""
		"&eReminder&r:"
		"- No batteries = no output."
		"- The number of batteries sets the number of Amps it outputs. (That means a &68x Battery Buffer&r with only &e3 batteries&r will only output &e3A&r.)"
		""
		"Use them wisely — they are the foundation of any stable energy network."
	]
	quest.2827645A006C231F.quest_subtitle: "The basic battery buffer beckons batteries"
	quest.2827645A006C231F.title: "Battery Buffer"
	quest.2843A7A3EBCBB556.quest_desc: [
		"Surround a Resin Circuit Board with eight copper single wires to make your first &aResin Printed Circuit Board&r!"
		""
		"Create's mechanical saw slits a copper plate into two wires. Later the assembler makes boards from glue and copper foil instead."
	]
	quest.2843A7A3EBCBB556.quest_subtitle: "The easier component for circuits"
	quest.2843A7A3EBCBB556.title: "Electronics #2: Circuit Boards"
	quest.28505A85304EF63B.quest_desc: [
		"Hot-air envelopes take wool and brass nuggets: two nuggets for four envelopes by hand, one for three with a deployer. Build them into a closed balloon."
	]
	quest.28505A85304EF63B.quest_subtitle: "The balloon"
	quest.28505A85304EF63B.title: "Envelopes"
	quest.2851F7375B178EFC.quest_desc: [
		"Steam isn't complicated — just boil water."
		""
		"To do it at scale, build GregTech's &6Large Boilers&r: Bronze first (LV circuits, tin cables and a Bronze Firebox Casing), then Steel, Titanium and Tungstensteel. Each tier makes a lot more steam. They burn solid fuels or liquids such as lava and creosote; EMI lists them all."
		""
		"As a reminder: &e2 mB&r of steam = &e1 EU&r in a steam turbine."
	]
	quest.2851F7375B178EFC.quest_subtitle: "Not much of a choice"
	quest.2851F7375B178EFC.title: "This is Steam"
	quest.288FDFED8EEFAC6C.quest_desc: [
		"A fuel-burning rotation source for vehicles: an engine assembly, a brass plate and TFC fire bricks."
	]
	quest.288FDFED8EEFAC6C.quest_subtitle: "Power on board"
	quest.288FDFED8EEFAC6C.title: "Portable Engine"
	quest.28ED4E500F052E8C.quest_desc: [
		"Oxygen is used in &7LV&r+ in countless chemical reactions, and in the electric blast furnace to roast sulfide ores."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r in infinite amounts by centrifuging air or electrolyzing water. Flint dust, centrifuged into silicon dioxide and electrolyzed, gives oxygen and silicon."
	]
	quest.28ED4E500F052E8C.quest_subtitle: "Element #8"
	quest.28ED4E500F052E8C.title: "Oxygen"
	quest.29109E15AE724F8D.quest_desc: [
		"To create your Copper Anvil you'll need both a basic Stone Anvil and a Charcoal Forge. To make a Stone Anvil, you will need a block of Raw &6Igneous&r rock: granite, diorite, gabbro, andesite, basalt, dacite or rhyolite."
		""
		"To obtain Raw Rock you can carefully break the blocks &laround&r the Raw Rock you want to mine. Once all 6 sides of the Raw Rock are exposed to air, it'll pop off into its Item form. An exposed block in the world works too: right-click its top face with a hammer to turn it into your Stone Anvil."
	]
	quest.29109E15AE724F8D.quest_subtitle: "No, it isn't just \"Stone\""
	quest.29109E15AE724F8D.title: "Raw Rock"
	quest.2942B4128DBF45CA.quest_desc: [
		"A &3Sluice&r, made from sticks and lumber, processes those &aore deposits&r in a faster, slightly automated way: water must flow through it, and deposits dropped into the stream wash onto it and come out the bottom as ore, rocks or gems, with slightly better ore odds than panning. Check the &2Field Guide&r entry for the water setup!"
	]
	quest.2942B4128DBF45CA.quest_subtitle: "Panning on Steroids"
	quest.2942B4128DBF45CA.title: "Sluices"
	quest.2997543765EAE246.quest_desc: [
		"Getting &bChromium&r will be one of the first ore processing challenges you encounter. In this pack it comes from TFC's &cRuby&r:"
		""
		"- Washing crushed ruby in the &dOre Washer&r gives chromium dust a third of the time."
		""
		"- Centrifuging impure ruby dust gives a little more."
		""
		"- An &bMV Electrolyzer&r splits ruby dust into chromium and aluminium."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Later, &6Ruby Slurry&r (crushed or purified ruby mixed with aqua regia) gets more chromium out of each ruby, along with aluminium."
		""
		"GregTech's other chromium sources, chromite and garnet sand, have no veins here."
	]
	quest.2997543765EAE246.quest_subtitle: "Chrome me up, choom!"
	quest.2997543765EAE246.title: "Chromium"
	quest.29BF6E4C939D8EA2.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't made any yet, there are two ways to get paper without electricity."
		""
		"1) Papyrus: cut it into strips with a knife, soak the strips in a barrel of water, weave four soaked strips on a loom and scrape the unrefined paper with a knife."
		""
		"2) Craft it from treated hide, an egg, flour and lime."
		""
		"Later, a chemical bath turns wood pulp straight into paper."
	]
	quest.29BF6E4C939D8EA2.quest_subtitle: "Not from sugarcane"
	quest.29BF6E4C939D8EA2.title: "Paper"
	quest.29C4606F4DA9F088.quest_desc: [
		"You've unlocked the &1IV&r Machine Hull, but it may not be very useful until you have &1IV&r Circuits. Still, you may find one or two uses for it, and at least you will be ready to build the &1IV Assembler&r as soon as you make your first &1IV&r Circuits."
	]
	quest.29C4606F4DA9F088.quest_subtitle: "IV Already?"
	quest.29C4606F4DA9F088.title: "IV Already?"
	quest.29CBECDB71C151D7.quest_desc: [
		"Your first &5EV&r Circuit gets a unique texture. If you still consider yourself to be in &bMV&r, &ahold off&r on making too many of these, as they won't benefit you right now. We can't stop you from making these if you &djust wanna flex&r on us, though."
	]
	quest.29CBECDB71C151D7.quest_subtitle: "Standing out amongst the rest"
	quest.29CBECDB71C151D7.title: "First EV Circuits!"
	quest.2A3616367AF16F2E.quest_desc: [
		"Once you craft the next tier of Anvil (such as going from Copper to Bronze, or Bronze to Wrought Iron), the previous tier basically becomes useless."
		""
		"However, since it's made out of metal, you &ocan and should&r melt the previous tier of Anvil back into its liquid metal form!"
		"Grab a Vessel and place it on the right hand side of the Charcoal Forge interface, then place the Anvil and slowly heat it until it reaches the melting temperature. The molten metal will be deposited inside the Vessel, then you can cast it back into ingots or whatever you like!"
	]
	quest.2A3616367AF16F2E.quest_subtitle: "Because 14 ingots is a lot now"
	quest.2A3616367AF16F2E.title: "Anvil Recycling?"
	quest.2AA712A252708D08.quest_desc: [
		"Lanthanum goes into a few late alloys."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aCassiterite&r gives &aMonazite&r as its &3Ore Washer&r by-product. An &3Electrolyzer&r splits monazite dust into rare earth and phosphate, and a &3Centrifuge&r separates rare earth into small piles of cadmium, neodymium, samarium, cerium, yttrium and lanthanum."
	]
	quest.2AA712A252708D08.quest_subtitle: "Element #57"
	quest.2AA712A252708D08.title: "Lanthanum"
	quest.2AB8B4DDC3C44244.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the world of &dLarge Multiblocks&r. These alloys build the casings of the large versions of GregTech's machines, starting with the &eAlloy Blast Smelter&r, which needs Tantalum Carbide plates. Tantalum Carbide needs the heat of your new RTM Coils."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&o&6&lLore&r:&r &oGregicality Multiblocks originally began as a mod for GTCEu on Minecraft 1.12, adding the large versions of GregTech machines and the &6Parallel Hatch&r. &oWhen GTCEu was ported to 1.20, this mod was fully integrated into &dGTm&r - &osomething no one ever complained about&r. For the 1.12 enjoyers out there, you might remember them as the &dGCYM multis&r."
	]
	quest.2AB8B4DDC3C44244.quest_subtitle: "More alloys means more fun!"
	quest.2AB8B4DDC3C44244.title: "Large Multiblock Alloys"
	quest.2AE9373E8C1D79C6.quest_desc: [
		"Fluorine is the rarest gas to obtain from electrolysis in this game."
		""
		"Your best source is &aTopaz&r: TFC's topaz forms in the fissures at the heart of volcanoes. The Macerator turns it into crushed Topaz ore; process that into dust and electrolyze it."
		""
		"&aBiotite&r, one of the byproducts of centrifuging Stone Dust, also gives some."
	]
	quest.2AE9373E8C1D79C6.quest_subtitle: "Have you brushed your teeth today?"
	quest.2AE9373E8C1D79C6.title: "Fluorine"
	quest.2B605D05F49DF852.quest_desc: [
		"Barium is used in &6HV&r to make mercury barium calcium cuprate, the &6HV&r superconductor."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here. Centrifuge stone dust into metal mixture, centrifuge that in &5EV&r for barite, and electrolyze the barite."
	]
	quest.2B605D05F49DF852.quest_subtitle: "Element #56"
	quest.2B605D05F49DF852.title: "Barium"
	quest.2B8C0171DA56DEA2.quest_desc: [
		"Mercury is used in &7LV&r+ in the chemical bath to wash ores for extra byproducts, and in the &6HV&r superconductor."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r by centrifuging cinnabar dust (from TFC cinnabar) or redstone."
	]
	quest.2B8C0171DA56DEA2.quest_subtitle: "Element #80"
	quest.2B8C0171DA56DEA2.title: "Mercury"
	quest.2B9F4179B0245299.quest_desc: [
		"Proper ore processing is a large, complex beast that you'll learn more about as you progress; it gets much more metal and other byproducts out of every ore you mine."
		""
		"Crushed ore comes from Create's millstone and crushing wheels or GregTech's macerator. Wash it in a cauldron or ore washer, smelt it in a steam furnace or with Create's fan, or keep processing it for byproducts. Crushed hematite, magnetite, limonite and pyrite smelt into cast iron."
		""
		"TFC's quern doesn't make crushed ore in this pack: it grinds ores into powders that don't melt, so keep your metal ores out of it."
	]
	quest.2B9F4179B0245299.quest_subtitle: "Crushed ore"
	quest.2B9F4179B0245299.title: "Ore Processing"
	quest.2BA6F65143A5B353.quest_desc: [
		"Another abundant item on the ground are sticks, which have many uses! They can create tools, torches, firestarters and more. Breaking leaves by hand drops sticks too."
		""
		"To avoid having your inventory get clogged with different types of twigs, you can craft them into 'regular' sticks to stack them together. Later, at a workbench, nine sticks make a Stick Bunch and two bunches a Stick Bundle, which burns like a log in firepits, pit kilns and charcoal pits."
	]
	quest.2BA6F65143A5B353.quest_subtitle: "You gotta handle that tool somehow"
	quest.2BA6F65143A5B353.title: "Find some Sticks"
	quest.2BE542F809DBC2BA.quest_desc: [
		"&aBenzene&r is a &9Gas Fuel&r. To skip some frustration, let's check out the two best ways to obtain it."
		""
		"The first option is &dWood based&r. Put Logs in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r for &9Wood Tar&r, which you &3distill&r for &aBenzene&r. The extra Charcoal can either be broken down further into &9Coal Tar&r or sent to a Boiler."
		""
		"Your second option is &dHeavy Oil based&r. Put Heavy Oil in a &3Distillery&r for &9Heavy Oil Residue&r, which you &aseverely steam-crack&r and &3distill&r again for &aBenzene&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For information on how to process Oil, check the Light Oil Residue and Naphtha Quests."
		""
		"In general, it is better to prioritize placing down more machines (&dparallelisation&r) over overclocking the recipes. That way, you end up losing less energy processing the resources."
		""
		"&aBenzene&r is burned in a &3Gas Turbine&r. Ultimately, your power source is your choice."
	]
	quest.2BE542F809DBC2BA.quest_subtitle: "In the end, it &lwas&r always Benzene"
	quest.2BE542F809DBC2BA.title: "The Church of Benzene"
	quest.2C2EF06B453F81F2.quest_desc: [
		"&bThe Terminal&r has one main purpose, and &awe highly encourage you to craft it&r."
		""
		"Building all these &eMultiblocks&r can be a bit &cintimidating&r, right? Well, here's a tip: use &dShift + Right-Click&r on any &6Multiblock Controller&r to &aautomatically assemble the entire structure&r!"
		""
		"You might need to &emove around some buses and hatches&r to suit your setup, but overall, this feature will save you a &alot of time&r."
	]
	quest.2C2EF06B453F81F2.quest_subtitle: "Automatic Multiblock Builder"
	quest.2C2EF06B453F81F2.title: "Terminal"
	quest.2D1FE248FD5327A1.quest_desc: [
		"Gather some Clay: knapping takes 5 clay per item, and you'll want a vessel, a saw blade mold, ingot molds and more (see the next quests). Once you mold the clay, put the pieces in a Pit Kiln to bake them into Ceramic. You mold clay the same way you knap stone, but if you make a mistake you can just close the interface and reshape it."
	]
	quest.2D1FE248FD5327A1.quest_subtitle: "It's Clay!"
	quest.2D1FE248FD5327A1.title: "Clay"
	quest.2D26159BF629829B.quest_desc: [
		"Getting into &7LV&r opens up a LOT of options, so it's easy to get lost. Here's our recommendations:"
		""
		"1) Set up a source of power: Steam Turbines fed by your boilers. Don't cheap out, build multiple generators!"
		""
		"Be sure to &eread the GregTech Power chapter&r so you get a good understanding of how EU, Volts, Amps, and Cable Loss all work."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"2) Focus on machines that make building more machines cheaper."
		""
		"The Polarizer is a super cheap machine that can magnetize rods for basically free. Create's press and saw already make plates and wires; add a Bender for foils, a Lathe for screws and a Cutter for bolts."
		""
		"After that, focus on making Rubber cheaper with a Chemical Reactor and Fluid Solidifier, and making electronic components cheaper with an Assembler."
		""
		"Once everything's at its cheapest, make sure you craft components in batches to save you lots of time."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"3) Build a Canner and make some batteries. Battery Buffers will help a lot with the growth of your factory."
		""
		"4) &7LV&r has two main end goals, the &aCircuit Assembler&r and the &aElectric Blast Furnace&r. You should now be ready to tackle those."
	]
	quest.2D26159BF629829B.quest_subtitle: "This is all very overwhelming"
	quest.2D26159BF629829B.title: "Lost?"
	quest.2D327656CC5534AE.quest_desc: [
		"You're gonna need a lot of &6Rubber Sheets&r, and later on other plastics too."
		""
		"With the Chemical Reactor's cheaper molten Rubber, the &3Fluid Solidifier&r and a Plate Casting Mold cast it straight into sheets: 144 mB each, no rubber ingots or press in between."
	]
	quest.2D327656CC5534AE.quest_subtitle: "Even cheaper rubber"
	quest.2D327656CC5534AE.title: "Casting Mold and Rubber Sheets"
	quest.2E21F0981C1E0CF3.quest_desc: [
		"In this quest, we'll bestow upon you &5cursed wisdom&r... the ability to easily automate the Electrolyzer."
		""
		"The &9Smart Item Filter&r is a filter that recognises Recipe Maps. When placed on the side of a machine, you can set it to \"&3Electrolyzer&r\" to allow insertion of electrolyzable items specifically. You heard that right - no need to filter manually!"
		""
		"Oh, and it only gets &abetter&r. If you combine this bad boy with a &aRobot Arm&r, it'll only supply the &6exact amount&r of items required for a successful recipe to the machine."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Place the &aRobot Arm&r on your Electrolyzer, open its GUI, then place the &9Smart Filter&r inside. Ensure that the Smart Filter is set to Electrolyzer."
		""
		"Next, configure it to &d&lImport&r and &d&lSupply Exact&r. Finally, attach any inventory &7(a chest will do)&r onto the side where you placed the &aRobot Arm&r. Ta-dah! You've figured out how to handle &6all&r Electrolyzer recipes!"
		""
		"What about the output of the &3Electrolyzer&r? You may want to route the Fluids to several Tanks - or even &3Super Tanks&r if you've gotten that far. We highly recommend that you avoid any methods involving voiding Fluids.&7.&7. except for Water for obvious reasons."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r The Robot Arm has to facilitate the item transfer for its filtering functionality to work! Inserting directly into the machine &7(for instance, pushing with a Hopper!)&r will ignore the Robot Arm's &dSupply Exact&r setting."
	]
	quest.2E21F0981C1E0CF3.quest_subtitle: "Knock, knock - who's that? It's MENSA!"
	quest.2E21F0981C1E0CF3.title: "Smart Item Filter"
	quest.2EB449E77D3A9658.quest_desc: [
		"Like the Steam Oven, the &3Steam Grinder&r is a multiblock version of a single machine, the macerator, that can do up to 8 items at the same time. Its recipe takes two potin gears. Is it worth it? That's totally up to you."
	]
	quest.2EB449E77D3A9658.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Macerator's little sister"
	quest.2EB449E77D3A9658.title: "Steam Grinder"
	quest.2F2352F74A7D6D52.quest_desc: [
		"Vanadium is used to make vanadium steel, which the &bMV&r cutter's buzzsaw blade is made of, and vanadium-gallium."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: wash crushed TFC &aMagnetite&r in an &3Ore Washer&r (or centrifuge impure magnetite dust) for &aVanadium Magnetite&r, then &3Centrifuge&r that into magnetite and vanadium."
	]
	quest.2F2352F74A7D6D52.quest_subtitle: "Element #23"
	quest.2F2352F74A7D6D52.title: "Vanadium"
	quest.2F58F9EF3BC1004B.quest_desc: [
		"Moving Energy in GregTech means understanding a few core mechanics."
		""
		"First, &bEnergy Tiers&r. From &aLV&r to &cUHV&r, everything in GregTech — wires, machines, recipes — is tied to a tier. You’ll need the &ecorrect cable material&r to move energy. For example:"
		"&7•&r Tin wire = &aLV&r"
		"&7•&r Copper wire = &bMV&r"
		""
		"Second, you’ve got the &bAmperage&r mechanic. Think of 1 Amp (or 1A) as &ea packet of energy&r. Machines request energy \"packets\", which then get sent down the wire."
		"&7•&r 1A of LV = &a32 EU&r"
		"&7•&r 1A of HV = &e512 EU&r"
		""
		"Most machines and energy hatches will only request &62A at maximum&r."
		""
		"Mastering these two ideas is key before going further into energy distribution."
	]
	quest.2F58F9EF3BC1004B.quest_subtitle: "So, energy transfer, huh"
	quest.2F58F9EF3BC1004B.title: "Moving your Energy"
	quest.2FABEDB61F73CB73.quest_desc: [
		"The bellows forces air into the firepit or forge in front of it (or in front and one block down), raising its maximum temperature for a short time at the cost of burning fuel faster."
		""
		"Charcoal burns at 1350 °C: not quite hot enough to fire pottery in a forge (1399 °C), and iron melts at 1535 °C. The bellows makes up the difference. Bituminous coal burns at 1415 °C on its own."
		""
		"Made from lumber and leather. TFC's blast furnace needs one too."
	]
	quest.2FABEDB61F73CB73.quest_subtitle: "Higher temperatures can be reached, at a small price."
	quest.2FABEDB61F73CB73.title: "Bellows"
	quest.2FEA213C7927F27F.quest_desc: [
		"LV pumps contain a Create mechanical pump, LV pistons a Create cogwheel."
		""
		"Pump: an LV motor, a Create mechanical pump, a tin rotor, a tin screw, two rubber rings and a tin cable. Piston: an LV motor, a Create cogwheel, three steel plates, two steel rods and two tin cables."
		""
		"Both are crafting components first, but the pump is also a &9cover&r: placed on a machine it moves fluids in or out, and it takes a Fluid Filter."
	]
	quest.2FEA213C7927F27F.quest_subtitle: "Create inside"
	quest.2FEA213C7927F27F.title: "Pumps and Pistons"
	quest.3017AC6CEC8FD09A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Large Gas Turbine&r — also known as &dLGT&r — is the large generator for gas fuels. You can build your first one at &5EV&r from an EV hull, EV circuits, stainless steel gears and large stainless steel pipes."
		""
		"Like the other large turbines it needs a Maintenance Hatch, an Input Hatch for the gas, a Rotor Holder and a Dynamo Hatch. It also needs a Muffler Hatch, but no Output Hatch."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Its output doubles with every Rotor Holder tier above &5EV&r, and the rotor's power multiplies it further. Size the Dynamo Hatch to match: a normal one handles 2A, so a strong turbine may need a 4A hatch."
		""
		"The Efficiency stat of a Turbine Rotor makes each mB of fuel last longer."
		""
		"Turbines burn fuel while they run, so switch them off when your batteries are full, for example with an Energy Detector cover and a Machine Controller cover."
	]
	quest.3017AC6CEC8FD09A.quest_subtitle: "The big gas burner"
	quest.3017AC6CEC8FD09A.title: "The Large Gas Turbine"
	quest.302EFCB09E95B4A7.quest_desc: [
		"&bFactory Gauges&r can do two things:"
		""
		"1) Monitor levels of items attached to a connected Packager"
		"2) Automatically order crafting requests when those levels drop below a certain amount."
		""
		"You heard that right, Gauges enable &6autocrafting&r! Hold &eW&r over one to Ponder a full breakdown of how to use them."
	]
	quest.302EFCB09E95B4A7.quest_subtitle: "Automation, reinvented"
	quest.302EFCB09E95B4A7.title: "Factory Gauge"
	quest.3041E7661AB2C712.quest_desc: [
		"This column shows how to process crushed ore, which is almost always the second step."
	]
	quest.3041E7661AB2C712.title: "Crushed Ore"
	quest.30C3B9319A96DEAE.quest_desc: [
		"&bFluid Pipes&r will transport &7Steam&r and other fluids between machines for you."
		""
		"Each pipe has a throughput in mB/t and a &6Temperature Limit&r. This is relevant right now, as steam will burn wooden pipes. The bigger the pipe, the &ahigher&r the throughput, but the more &dexpensive&r the craft; hover over one for its numbers."
		""
		"To start off, use wooden pipes for room-temperature fluids and bronze ones for steam and anything hot."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aReminder:&r 1 second = 20 ticks... assuming the server isn't lagging."
		""
		"&dNote:&r pipes connect only to the block they were placed against. To open more connections, use your wrench on the pipe. You can also sneak-right-click with your wrench to disable input from a side, which helps against sloshing."
	]
	quest.30C3B9319A96DEAE.quest_subtitle: "Liquids, gases... we don't discriminate"
	quest.30C3B9319A96DEAE.title: "Fluid Pipes"
	quest.30E3D476C0CDB561.quest_desc: [
		"Well... can you show us an &bMV&r Circuit as well?"
		""
		"&aAluminium&r is the main ingredient for &bMV&r machinery. Get ready to need a lot of it. The EBF smelts aluminium dust at &c1700K&r, so Cupronickel Coils (1800K) are just hot enough."
		""
		"Smelting takes about a third less time with &9Nitrogen&r, which you get by centrifuging &9Air&r from a &3Gas Collector&r."
		""
		"&6You will still need MV Circuits in order to make MV machines!&r"
	]
	quest.30E3D476C0CDB561.quest_subtitle: "We're basically in MV now, right?"
	quest.30E3D476C0CDB561.title: "Your first Aluminium Ingot"
	quest.312B76EC8D7E1466.quest_desc: [
		"Antimony is used in &7LV&r to make battery alloy and soldering alloy."
		""
		"It can be obtained as a byproduct of processing TFC tetrahedrite."
	]
	quest.312B76EC8D7E1466.quest_subtitle: "Element #51"
	quest.312B76EC8D7E1466.title: "Antimony"
	quest.326094BCCF778B49.quest_desc: [
		"&2We hope you're getting the hang of &9GregTech&r, because now it's time to push your skills a bit further."
		"In this chapter, you'll unlock &eadvanced multiblocks&r and &ecomplex processes&r."
		""
		"&6Your main goal for this chapter:&r craft your first &5EV&r Machine Hull."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To craft the &5EV&r Machine Hull:"
		"- Build your first &aCleanroom&r"
		"- Construct a &bVacuum Freezer&r to cool hot ingots"
		"- Process &9Rutile&r into &7Titanium&r"
		""
		"Along the way you'll make &dEnder Pearls&r from scratch, take on new &aChemistry&r with Fluorine and Nitric Acid, and upgrade your &6EBF coils&r."
	]
	quest.326094BCCF778B49.quest_subtitle: "Things are heating up"
	quest.326094BCCF778B49.title: "Welcome to HV!"
	quest.3263EC4F86DD673D.quest_desc: [
		"Congrats on successfully reaching a new tier of circuits! These &dLuV&r Circuits won't have much use just yet, as &dLuV&r machines need materials from the full &bPlatline&r."
		""
		"Most of those recipes will require an &1IV&r Assembler, so be sure you have one ready."
	]
	quest.3263EC4F86DD673D.quest_subtitle: "Your first LuV circuits"
	quest.3263EC4F86DD673D.title: "Your first LuV circuits"
	quest.328432D28122149B.quest_desc: [
		"Aluminium Cells are a big upgrade over the Steel Cells or Universal Fluid Cells."
		""
		"They can hold any fraction of Fluid - up to &d32 buckets&r!"
	]
	quest.328432D28122149B.quest_subtitle: "Like cells... only larger!"
	quest.328432D28122149B.title: "Large Cells"
	quest.32CC2CAF976BF298.quest_desc: [
		"Every time you enter a new tier, things can get a bit overwhelming. You'll be faced with lots of &enew machines&r to build and &echemicals&r to produce."
		""
		"As you've probably seen in the quests, you have &2three main objectives&r to complete before progressing into &6HV&r. Let's break them down one by one."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"First, you'll need to upgrade your &dEBF&r with two new &bMV Energy Hatches&r. This will allow it to overclock and run &6HV recipes&r. That upgrade is key for producing &estainless steel&r, the main material for &6HV&r, and also &eKanthal&r, which you'll need to upgrade your &dEBF coils&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Your second objective (although you can tackle it first if you prefer) involves diving into chemistry. Your first plastic, &ePolyethylene&r, is essential for future progress. There are two possible paths you can follow, and the quests will help guide you:"
		""
		"- &ePetrochem route&r: pump oil from deep underground with a Fluid Drilling Rig. This path also unlocks &eDiesel&r production for fuel combustion."
		""
		"- &eBiochem route&r: use a &6Pyrolyse Oven&r and wood (a Create-powered tree farm works great) or a Brewery. This method gives you more &eBenzene&r and opens the door to using a &eGas Turbine&r."
		""
		"Each path has its pros and cons, but eventually, you'll need both anyway."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The final step here is unlocking the &6second HV Circuit&r. It only requires &atwo steps&r, making it faster than crafting the &6first HV Circuit&r, which needs &cthree steps&r."
		""
		"To achieve this, you'll need to get your hands on a &dLaser Engraver&r, which allows you to produce your first &dWafers&r. With those, you can craft an &6HV Circuit&r that you'll use to build the &bMV Circuit Assembler&r."
		""
		"It's not strictly necessary to do this now (you can continue using the first HV Circuit for progression), but &ait will make your life much easier&r if you take care of it now. Trust us."
	]
	quest.32CC2CAF976BF298.quest_subtitle: "More technology, more problems"
	quest.32CC2CAF976BF298.title: "Welcome to MV!"
	quest.3301BC2AB9D9FDFA.quest_desc: [
		"In your travels, you may explore a whole &olot&r and end up picking up a lot of junk. This quest branch covers a couple of ways to carry and store more: TFC's &dvessels&r and Create's &dtoolboxes&r."
	]
	quest.3301BC2AB9D9FDFA.quest_subtitle: "Turns out your inventory is quite small."
	quest.3301BC2AB9D9FDFA.title: "Portable Storage Solutions"
	quest.331DC173FD5C7953.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Sifter&r can output &6Purified Dust&r, which you can toss into a centrifuge for a few extra byproducts."
	]
	quest.331DC173FD5C7953.quest_subtitle: "Byproducts of byproducts"
	quest.331DC173FD5C7953.title: "Centrifuging the dust"
	quest.335ED29B44B74BC3.quest_desc: [
		"Each new tier unlocks additional materials used to craft an entirely new set of &eTools&r."
		""
		"While you may not want to replace your full set every time, it is still worth reviewing their stats, as some provide higher mining speed while others offer greater durability, and there is no absolute best choice. It ultimately depends on your priorities."
		""
		"&bVanadium Steel Tools&r are a big step up in durability from Steel."
	]
	quest.335ED29B44B74BC3.quest_subtitle: "A whole new set of Tools"
	quest.335ED29B44B74BC3.title: "Vanadium Steel Tools"
	quest.33BA9B2114A4B57C.quest_desc: [
		"The Forge is a crafting station used to heat materials to high temperatures. It heats things considerably faster than the Pit Kiln, and is much easier to control too."
		""
		"To make the forge, surround a charcoal pile of 7 or 8 layers with 5 stone blocks (raw rock, cobblestone and the like) and light it. It needs open air above it and a view of the sky. The Forge doesn't burn logs; it burns Charcoal or Coal (bituminous coal or lignite), and a Bellows makes it hotter."
		""
		"Check the field guide for walkthroughs on how to make a Charcoal Pit and a Charcoal Forge."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"In this pack a Create basin set on a charcoal forge is Create's heat source: 750 °C and up counts as heated and 2000 °C (a forge with bellows) as superheated, for heated mixing and alloying in the basin."
	]
	quest.33BA9B2114A4B57C.quest_subtitle: "The Fabric doesnt exist by the way."
	quest.33BA9B2114A4B57C.title: "The Forge"
	quest.33C7C1497D8521F9.quest_desc: [
		"Cadmium is a subpar &7LV&r to &6HV&r battery electrolyte."
		""
		"It can be obtained as a byproduct of washing crushed TFC tetrahedrite with sodium persulfate in the chemical bath, or of macerating refined sphalerite or tetrahedrite ore."
	]
	quest.33C7C1497D8521F9.quest_subtitle: "Element #48"
	quest.33C7C1497D8521F9.title: "Cadmium"
	quest.346393F4B3CDA726.quest_desc: [
		"With &5GregTech&r, you get access to various &6filters&r that help you ease into &aautomation&r. All of them are compatible with different &dCovers&r, which you'll learn more about during the &7LV&r Chapter."
		""
		"Here, we're introducing two more specific filters that you might find &bhandy&r in certain situations."
		""
		"To use a filter, simply apply it as a &dCover&r on any &5GT Machine&r or &6pipe&r."
	]
	quest.346393F4B3CDA726.title: "Filters"
	quest.349835095C5DD04C.quest_desc: [
		"Metal armor requires a two-step forging process, but don't be scared off by its difficulty: smith an unfinished piece from a &7double sheet&r (a single sheet for boots), then weld a sheet onto it (a double sheet for chestplates)."
		""
		"All metal armor will give you bonus protection to &6Slashing&r, &9Piercing&r, and &2Crushing&r damage, and steel armor adds toughness on top."
	]
	quest.349835095C5DD04C.quest_subtitle: "Only the shiniest suit of armor"
	quest.349835095C5DD04C.title: "Metal Armor"
	quest.34C4CC12E9F88274.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Chemical Bath&r dyes Glass Lenses with &aChemical Dye&r (a dye, Sulfuric Acid and Salt reacted in a Chemical Reactor). Coloured lenses let you engrave more types of Wafers."
		""
		"It also turns Ender Pearls into &5Ender Eyes&r with molten Blaze, and you'll want plenty of those for &6HV&r Emitters and Sensors."
	]
	quest.34C4CC12E9F88274.quest_subtitle: "Please don't bathe with your toaster..."
	quest.34C4CC12E9F88274.title: "High Voltage Bathing"
	quest.34D2518FB05ACB0A.quest_desc: [
		"Make some &aBattery Alloy&r, used for Battery Hulls: mix 4 lead dust with 1 antimony dust in a Mixer."
		""
		"Neither has its own ore here. &aLead&r is a byproduct of TFC native silver (macerate its crushed ore), and &aAntimony&r one of tetrahedrite."
		""
		"A Battery Hull is two battery alloy plates and a tin cable."
		""
		"&9Note:&r This quest does &lnot&r contain functional Batteries - head on for that."
	]
	quest.34D2518FB05ACB0A.quest_subtitle: "Batteries are great!"
	quest.34D2518FB05ACB0A.title: "Battery Preparations!"
	quest.34E7CDA9F06D1126.quest_desc: [
		"&dSilk Cloth&r is woven on the &3Loom&r from 24 &aString&r, which you get from killing &bSpiders&r underground. No silkworms exist yet, sorry! Much later, GregTech's wiremill spins Polycaprolactam (nylon) into string."
		""
		"Silk Cloth can stand in for wool cloth in some recipes, such as beds."
		""
		"Silk Cloth is considered a &bHigh Quality Cloth.&r"
	]
	quest.34E7CDA9F06D1126.quest_subtitle: "Very, very smooth."
	quest.34E7CDA9F06D1126.title: "Silk Cloth"
	quest.350F820A8F7F234E.quest_desc: [
		"The direct upgrade of &cGasoline&r is a &5two times more powerful fuel&r. An &5EV&r Large Chemical Reactor mixes gasoline with octane, nitrous oxide, toluene and ethyl tert-butyl ether. By then you'll know your way around EMI's petrochemistry, so trace each ingredient there and begin the fabrication of this insanely strong fuel."
	]
	quest.350F820A8F7F234E.quest_subtitle: "Highly Powerful"
	quest.350F820A8F7F234E.title: "High Octane Gasoline (HOG)"
	quest.3527CC82D25E6ABA.quest_desc: [
		"Certain &6Dusts&r have no direct use and need splitting into their elements. &cRuby&r dust, for example, electrolyzes into &dChromium&r and &dAluminium&r, and clay dust gives aluminium too."
		""
		"Most of these recipes will only be available with an &bMV Electrolyzer&r, so come back to this later!"
	]
	quest.3527CC82D25E6ABA.quest_subtitle: "An encore for ore!"
	quest.3527CC82D25E6ABA.title: "Further refinement"
	quest.35B058DBA424A790.quest_desc: [
		"At this point, you have all the tools you need for &9Plastic Circuit Boards&r: a Polyethylene sheet and Copper Foil, treated with &aSulfuric Acid&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r. Better plastics later (PVC, PTFE) give more boards per sheet."
		""
		"Then etch more Copper Foil onto the board with &aIron III Chloride&r or &aSodium Persulfate&r for a &9Plastic Printed Circuit Board&r."
		""
		"The recipe chains are starting to get pretty long, so we recommend processing large batches in two dedicated &3Chemical Reactors&r."
	]
	quest.35B058DBA424A790.quest_subtitle: "It's a Casio on a Plastic Board"
	quest.35B058DBA424A790.title: "Plastic Boards"
	quest.35DB3DB9B82613B7.quest_desc: [
		"Blowing through lava or fire smelts items like a furnace: crushed copper becomes copper ingots. Crushed iron ores become cast iron; only the bloomery makes wrought iron."
		""
		"Blowing through water washes items instead, but it doesn't clean GregTech crushed ore here: wash that in a cauldron or an ore washer."
	]
	quest.35DB3DB9B82613B7.quest_subtitle: "Bulk smelting"
	quest.35DB3DB9B82613B7.title: "Encased Fan"
	quest.36157161E51BC937.quest_desc: [
		"Here's a list of the components you will need in &bMV&r. To ease the pain, be sure to &dbulk-craft&r these parts, especially &aMotors&r."
		""
		"Familiar with the &aEmitter&r? This tier's Emitter needs a &dFlawless Emerald&r, which you'll mostly get from the &3Sifting Machine&r for now."
		""
		"Conveyors, Pumps and Robot Arms are objective upgrades to &7LV&r versions if you use them as covers."
	]
	quest.36157161E51BC937.quest_subtitle: "Hated crafting these in the previous tier?"
	quest.36157161E51BC937.title: "The MV Components"
	quest.3636F02D991F4ABA.quest_desc: [
		"Back in the old days of GregTech, this little bad boy saw a lot of use—you used to get a ton of &6Small&r and &6Tiny Dusts&r from ore processing."
		""
		"Nowadays, it's only really useful for automatic packing, such as &dRare Earth&r in a &6Centrifuge&r returning many &6Small Piles of Dust&r."
		""
		"Don't forget: a &eRobot Arm&r set to Supply Exact mode can be useful to avoid clogging the input slots."
	]
	quest.3636F02D991F4ABA.quest_subtitle: "It's real fast"
	quest.3636F02D991F4ABA.title: "The Packer"
	quest.3638A7D2BEDD4C10.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium is the base material of &5EV&r: its machine casings are titanium plates."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here. Centrifuge stone dust (left over from washing ores) into metal mixture, then centrifuge that in &5EV&r for ilmenite and bauxite. Ilmenite with carbon in the electric blast furnace, or electrolyzed bauxite, gives rutile; a chemical reactor turns rutile, carbon and chlorine into titanium tetrachloride, and the electric blast furnace reduces that with magnesium. Cool the hot ingot in the vacuum freezer."
	]
	quest.3638A7D2BEDD4C10.quest_subtitle: "Element #22"
	quest.3638A7D2BEDD4C10.title: "Titanium"
	quest.3662C74FF3312438.quest_desc: [
		"Moving energy around in GregTech can be tricky — &bcables lose energy&r. For every block, for every amp, some EU is lost along the way. But don't worry, there are solutions:"
		""
		"&7•&r Cover your wires with rubber. Cables (insulated wires) lose less than bare wires, and they won't shock you. Just check the quest items for a reference."
		""
		"&7•&r Pick the right material. Hover over a wire or cable to see its maximum voltage, maximum amperage and loss per block; better materials lose less for the energy they carry."
		""
		"&7•&r &bSuperconductors&r. These beauties are a bit pricier, but they have &9zero loss&r. They don't need rubber covers, and won't zap you either. Just be aware that they're usually only craftable near the end of their tier."
		""
		"Optimize your energy flow — &breduce losses&r and make your systems more efficient."
	]
	quest.3662C74FF3312438.quest_subtitle: "Funky to place"
	quest.3662C74FF3312438.title: "Moving with wires"
	quest.36664E69CF201E82.quest_desc: [
		"The &eLarge Steam Turbine&r is a very powerful &bMultiblock&r for generating power at &6HV&r. Single-block generators stop at the &6HV&r Steam Turbine, so if you plan to keep using steam power beyond that, you will need to invest in this multiblock."
		""
		"It takes an &6HV&r Rotor Holder with a Turbine Rotor inside and outputs through a Dynamo Hatch. To understand how turbines work, refer to the power chapter."
	]
	quest.36664E69CF201E82.quest_subtitle: "Expensive but so good"
	quest.36664E69CF201E82.title: "Large Steam Turbine"
	quest.3689F02C475B307B.quest_desc: [
		"These could actually be cheaper to make than the &bMicroprocessor&r equivalent if you manage to mass-produce &bNano CPUs&r efficiently. Once that line is fully automated, these circuits will become an extremely cost-effective option for your high-end builds."
		""
		"Also, note that you can use Advanced SMD components from now on!"
	]
	quest.3689F02C475B307B.quest_subtitle: "Back to the usual circuit progression"
	quest.3689F02C475B307B.title: "Back to the usual circuit progression"
	quest.36949F536D7AB789.quest_desc: [
		"As you begin your journey, the first thing you'll notice is a completely changed world. You can no longer break trees with your fists, but fret not, for any caveman is not a real caveman without his stone tools!"
		""
		"Instead of crafting a wooden pickaxe, you can just pick up rocks from the ground. Begin by collecting at least 4 rocks. You can collect rocks by breaking or right-clicking them with an empty hand. Obsidian shards knap just like rocks."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:tfc:textures/gui/book/gui/rock_knapping.png width:100 height:100 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.36949F536D7AB789.quest_subtitle: "Grug smash rock"
	quest.36949F536D7AB789.title: "Find some Rocks"
	quest.36CC046818525B7C.quest_desc: [
		"Just like &bMV&r, you'll need to make higher-tier components."
		""
		"The &dFlawless Emeralds&r of MV Emitters and Sensors are replaced with &dEnder Eyes&r. Also notice that the &aMotors&r require &d2x Silver Cables&r and &dElectrum&r wire, while most of the other parts, the &aHull&r and the &aMachines&r use &dGold Cables&r."
		""
		"Finally, a use for that stockpile of Gold!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9&lTips to make life less painful:&r"
		""
		"- &eEnder Eyes&r: craft an Ender Pearl with &eBlaze Powder&r, which an &6HV&r Chemical Reactor makes from Carbon and Sulfur dust."
		"- &eElectrum&r is Gold and Silver dust in a &3Mixer&r."
		"- Bathe crushed Copper, Magnetite or Silver ore in &dMercury&r in the &3Chemical Bath&r for bonus &eGold&r, and crushed Gold ore for bonus &eSilver&r. Mercury comes from centrifuging Cinnabar."
	]
	quest.36CC046818525B7C.quest_subtitle: "We call this \"fun\""
	quest.36CC046818525B7C.title: "High Voltage Components"
	quest.37408B085E9CB67C.quest_desc: [
		"Iridium comes at the end of the platinum line: TFC &aTetrahedrite&r's purified ore gives &aPlatinum Group Sludge&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r, and its later separation steps (follow EMI from the sludge) leave iridium."
	]
	quest.37408B085E9CB67C.quest_subtitle: "Element #77"
	quest.37408B085E9CB67C.title: "Iridium"
	quest.37E454F09AD6727B.quest_desc: [
		"Too lazy to harvest and replant your crops? Mount harvesters on a moving contraption and they'll pick mature crops and replant them as they pass."
	]
	quest.37E454F09AD6727B.quest_subtitle: "Robotic Cherrypicking"
	quest.37E454F09AD6727B.title: "Mechanical Harvester"
	quest.3833BA84050D44D0.quest_desc: [
		"Progressing beyond the stone age will require a lot of metal, and just picking up small ores on the surface won't be enough. You'll have to dig down and begin mining."
		"Assuming you &odid&r mark the place where you found your copper, find the rough middle of where the ore pieces were and start digging! It might be pretty deep, but you'll eventually strike it rich. A Prospector's Pick helps you home in on the vein. The next page has some equipment you'll want to bring along for your first mining trip!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lPickaxe&r: Pretty obvious what this does, you'll need a way to break the stone and harvest the ore. Cast a copper pickaxe head in a mold."
		""
		"&lLadders and Torches&r: You'll need some way to climb back up out of the hole and see what you're doing!"
		""
		"&lSupport Beams and Planks&r: Mining here is much more dangerous - not only do monsters spawn underground, but carelessly digging around can cause a cave-in! The next quest goes over how to mitigate dangers while mining."
		""
		"Now go and dig your hole, diggy diggy hole!"
	]
	quest.3833BA84050D44D0.quest_subtitle: "Hope you remember where you found those ore indicators!"
	quest.3833BA84050D44D0.title: "Mining Preparations"
	quest.3847A90124C0831F.quest_desc: [
		"We know that GregTech isn’t the easiest mod to get into — especially when it comes to the &cenergy system&r. That’s why we’ll take our time in this chapter to explain as much as we can."
		""
		"Some things here might not make full sense until later in your progression, so don’t stress yourself. Just try to understand what you can for now, and feel free to &dcome back to this chapter&r whenever you have questions."
		""
		"We’ve split this chapter into &efour categories&r, each one covering a topic related to the GregTech Energy System. We’ll provide as many examples as possible to help you understand how it all works."
	]
	quest.3847A90124C0831F.quest_subtitle: "It's not as bad as you think"
	quest.3847A90124C0831F.title: "Let's do some explaining"
	quest.384A5B5FC75C2891.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Electromagnetic Separator&r pulls magnetic metals out of &dPurified Dusts&r, which you get by crushing purified ores. From TFC's ores: purified &6Magnetite&r dust gives some &eGold&r, and purified hematite, limonite and pyrite dust give a little &7Iron&r."
	]
	quest.384A5B5FC75C2891.quest_subtitle: "Probably the least useful GregTech machine"
	quest.384A5B5FC75C2891.title: "Electromagnetic Separator"
	quest.385D62BB715D6351.quest_desc: [
		"Iron is the metal of TFC's iron age, and steel is the base material of &7LV&r."
		""
		"In this pack iron means TFC wrought iron: smelt TFC hematite, magnetite or limonite in a bloomery and work the bloom on an anvil. Iron melted or smelted anywhere else becomes cast iron, and steel comes only from pig iron (TFC blast furnace)."
	]
	quest.385D62BB715D6351.quest_subtitle: "Element #26"
	quest.385D62BB715D6351.title: "Iron"
	quest.386572E7B641951D.quest_desc: [
		"Steel plates and tin cable (tin wire covered in rubber). Every LV machine starts as a hull."
		""
		"The LV Machine Casing is eight steel plates and a wrench; the hull adds two wrought iron plates, a steel plate and two tin cables. Try to make at least three or four to begin."
		""
		"These quests mark each new tier by its machine hull. As a quick reminder, &cmachines explode when exposed to rain or water&r, so keep them under a roof."
	]
	quest.386572E7B641951D.quest_subtitle: "Steel and cable"
	quest.386572E7B641951D.title: "LV Machine Hull"
	quest.38675AAD8AD89B02.quest_desc: [
		"Quite simply, it functions the same as the vanilla crossbow. Like the bow, it fires arrows, which deal &9Piercing&r damage, so don't waste them on Skeletons."
	]
	quest.38675AAD8AD89B02.quest_subtitle: "It's like a manual gun"
	quest.38675AAD8AD89B02.title: "Crossbow"
	quest.386ACBE47E2AEB13.quest_desc: [
		"Finally, after all this time, you've obtained a new circuit and unlocked an entirely new tier. Mainframes are made in the &6HV&r Circuit Assembler inside your Cleanroom."
		""
		"Your main focus should be the &5EV Circuit Assembler&r, which takes two of them and unlocks &bNanoprocessor Circuits&r. Keep in mind, though, that these will require Nano CPU Chips."
		""
		"More details will be provided as you go, so you can finally feel fully comfortable progressing into this new tier."
	]
	quest.386ACBE47E2AEB13.quest_subtitle: "Are we done with EV yet?"
	quest.386ACBE47E2AEB13.title: "Mainframes - First IV Circuits!"
	quest.387D7F928D362C32.quest_desc: [
		"Many materials going forward cannot be smelted directly from any Ores! They are instead obtained as byproducts from processing of other ores. Gallium and Arsenic are &4among&r these materials."
		""
		"For &dGallium&r, from worst to best:"
		""
		"&9- &3Electrolyze &aSphalerite&r dust for a low chance of it. Note that you lose out on direct smelting value."
		""
		"&9-&r Process TFC &aSphalerite&r: macerating purified sphalerite ore, or running the crushed ore through a &3Thermal Centrifuge&r, gives it as a &6Byproduct&r."
		""
		"For &dArsenic&r: TFC &aTetrahedrite&r carries &aRealgar&r. Run crushed tetrahedrite through a &3Thermal Centrifuge&r (or centrifuge pure tetrahedrite dust) for realgar dust, then &3Centrifuge&r the realgar into arsenic and sulfur."
		""
		"Mix one gallium and one arsenic dust for two Gallium Arsenide."
	]
	quest.387D7F928D362C32.quest_subtitle: "I hate byproducts, they're awesome"
	quest.387D7F928D362C32.title: "Gallium Arsenide"
	quest.38A051C57C68817F.quest_desc: [
		"Molds only take copper and the bronzes. From wrought iron on, you will need to forge your weapons: work the blade or head on an anvil of at least the metal's tier (a wrought iron anvil for wrought iron, a steel anvil for steel...), then finish it on the crafting grid."
	]
	quest.38A051C57C68817F.quest_subtitle: "To wrought iron and beyond!"
	quest.38A051C57C68817F.title: "Forged Weapons"
	quest.398C964C5BC720D9.quest_desc: [
		"Some machines are critical for progression, and the &6Mixer&r is one of them."
		""
		"It unlocks several essential alloys required to move forward, notably the &6RTM Alloy&r, which you’ll need to upgrade the coils of your &6EBF&r. This alloy is gated behind both the Tungsten Line and part of the Platline, so don’t expect it to be an easy one."
		""
		"Soon, you’ll also unlock the &5Large Mixer&r, which allows you to install two Energy Hatches. This could be the last time you’ll need to build a single-block Mixer, though as always, the choice is yours."
	]
	quest.398C964C5BC720D9.quest_subtitle: "Faster than your local bartender"
	quest.398C964C5BC720D9.title: "&5EV Mixer&r"
	quest.3994247262E25EAC.quest_desc: [
		"&3GregTech&r can be quite intimidating, this quest branch should help you out."
	]
	quest.3994247262E25EAC.quest_subtitle: "The industrial third of this pack."
	quest.3994247262E25EAC.title: "GregTech"
	quest.39F059704DE0FE03.quest_desc: [
		"To make a better bed, you'll need to create some textiles. The &3Loom&r is the work-station of choice for doing this, as it allows you to create different textiles that each have different uses."
	]
	quest.39F059704DE0FE03.quest_subtitle: "You'll need to work harder if you want to sleep..."
	quest.39F059704DE0FE03.title: "Loom"
	quest.3A03A0E33944514A.quest_desc: [
		"Want to quickly smelt something into an ingot? The &3Steam Furnace&r does just that! It can turn crushed ores and dusts quickly into their ingot form, at the expense of not getting any byproducts."
		""
		"Iron ores (hematite, magnetite, limonite, pyrite) and iron dusts come out as TFC cast iron, as if you'd melted them; wrought iron still comes only from the bloomery."
	]
	quest.3A03A0E33944514A.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Furnace furnaces..."
	quest.3A03A0E33944514A.title: "Steam Furnace"
	quest.3A4AC456356DFB6B.quest_desc: [
		"You'll want to grab these two lenses, dyed in the &3HV Chemical Bath&r. The &3Cyan&r lens engraves &aSimple System on Chip&r wafers, used for the best &8ULV&r Circuit recipe, while the &6Orange&r lens engraves the &aLPIC&r Wafer required for your next Energy Hatch."
		""
		"Cutting LPIC wafers into chips takes an &6HV&r Cutter inside your &3Cleanroom&r."
	]
	quest.3A4AC456356DFB6B.title: "I see the world in colour"
	quest.3A4EF49D167E27A4.quest_desc: [
		"Boron goes into borosilicate glass and into magnesium diboride, the &bMV&r superconductor."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &bMV&r by electrolyzing borax dust, which the macerator makes from TFC borax."
	]
	quest.3A4EF49D167E27A4.quest_subtitle: "Element #5"
	quest.3A4EF49D167E27A4.title: "Boron"
	quest.3AC0DA943E0DFF10.quest_desc: [
		"Helium is used in &6HV&r+ to speed up the electric blast furnace, and as liquid helium to cool hot ingots in the vacuum freezer."
		""
		"It can be obtained from liquid air: freeze air from a gas collector in the vacuum freezer, then distill it in the distillation tower. Both multiblocks need &5EV&r circuits."
		""
		"Helium-3 can be obtained by centrifuging helium (&bMV&r)."
	]
	quest.3AC0DA943E0DFF10.quest_subtitle: "Element #2"
	quest.3AC0DA943E0DFF10.title: "Helium"
	quest.3AEFFCF8FADDFD7F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Soft Mallet&r is a particularly useful tool during the steam age. Hit a GregTech machine with it to pause it, and again to start it back up."
		""
		"When your boilers can't keep up, pause the machines you don't need right now so the rest get the steam."
	]
	quest.3AEFFCF8FADDFD7F.quest_subtitle: "Time for a break"
	quest.3AEFFCF8FADDFD7F.title: "Soft Mallet"
	quest.3B68E023B0B96765.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Platinum Line&r will be your first real challenge to process, providing you with essential platinum-group metals: &bPlatinum&r, &bPalladium&r, &bRuthenium&r, &bRhodium&r, &bIridium&r, and &bOsmium&r."
		""
		"GregTech's platinum-bearing ores don't generate here, so this line is the main way to get any of them. &aPlatinum Group Sludge&r comes from purified &6Tetrahedrite&r, a TFC copper ore, in a Chemical Reactor with nitric acid."
		""
		"The Platline can be started at &6HV&r, but you won't be able to complete it fully until later in &5EV&r."
	]
	quest.3B68E023B0B96765.quest_subtitle: "GregTech players vs Mekanism players when they need Osmium:"
	quest.3B68E023B0B96765.title: "The Infamous Platline"
	quest.3B96B56BEF022F4C.quest_desc: [
		"&3Long-Distance Item Pipes&r can be used to send items across great distances. Place one endpoint at each end, and connect them with pipeline blocks."
		""
		"These pipes instantly transfer from the input side to the output side."
		""
		"They also have a minimum distance between pipe endpoints, so you can't use these for short-range operations."
	]
	quest.3B96B56BEF022F4C.quest_subtitle: "Wondering how to move those ores around?"
	quest.3B96B56BEF022F4C.title: "Long-Distance Item Pipes"
	quest.3C06EB454053DF65.quest_desc: [
		"The coke oven is your first GregTech multiblock! It needs no fuel: it bakes a log into charcoal and 250 mB of creosote, or coal (TFC bituminous coal counts) into coke and 500 mB of creosote, and holds up to 32 buckets of creosote."
		""
		"Charcoal feeds the forge, the bloomery and TFC's blast furnace; coke refines pig iron into steel in GregTech's primitive blast furnace. Creosote turns planks into treated wood."
		""
		"Press U (uses) on the coke oven in EMI to see how to build it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Coke ovens can be fully automated with a coke oven hatch on their side: the hatch works as both input and output, for items and fluids. A crate for the input, a chest for the output and a drum or tank for the creosote make a simple one-way coke oven."
	]
	quest.3C06EB454053DF65.quest_subtitle: "Finally, No More Charcoal Piles"
	quest.3C06EB454053DF65.title: "Coke Oven"
	quest.3C0FD7A40911ACF4.quest_desc: [
		"This questline serves as a quick guide to &9GregTech Amperage&r."
		""
		"&6&lTL;DR:&r For safety, match the Amperage limit of your Cables with the max amount of Amps provided by your Energy Producers."
		""
		"Still confused? Check the &cGregTech Power&r chapter for a full rundown on GregTech's electricity system, voltage tiers included!"
	]
	quest.3C0FD7A40911ACF4.quest_subtitle: "Amps and You: a how-to"
	quest.3C0FD7A40911ACF4.title: "But what are Amps?"
	quest.3C4D718ED647B684.quest_desc: [
		"Your first Electric Blast Furnace needs &a16 Cupronickel Coils&r. Each is assembled from 8 Cupronickel Double Wires, 8 Bronze Foils and 144 mB of molten Tin Alloy, so the set takes &a128 Cupronickel&r ingots, &a128 Bronze Foils&r and &a16 Tin Alloy&r ingots' worth of metal."
		""
		"You will also need Invar for the Heat Proof Casings, so get mining."
		""
		"The Cupronickel Coils will allow the EBF to perform recipes up to &d1,800K&r (ignoring Voltage bonuses). That's pretty hot if you ask us."
		""
		"&6Coils are explained further in the GregTech Power chapter (Blast Overclocking).&r"
	]
	quest.3C4D718ED647B684.quest_subtitle: "Baby's first heating coil"
	quest.3C4D718ED647B684.title: "Cupronickel Coils"
	quest.3C6F82F7D99B77A5.quest_desc: [
		"The &eCPU Wafer&r is a special one—it can be upgraded later through a &2Chemical Reaction&r."
		""
		"But for now, you’ll need the &eCPU Chip&r to craft the best &bMV&r circuits available at this stage."
		""
		"Make sure to produce a few extra, as they’ll be essential for future upgrades."
	]
	quest.3C6F82F7D99B77A5.quest_subtitle: "Gamers usually prefer GPU"
	quest.3C6F82F7D99B77A5.title: "Get a better CPU"
	quest.3CF09447EDDB3B33.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't learnt about Perfect Overclocking yet, read the Overclock quest first."
		""
		"The &3Electric Blast Furnace&r has a special ability: it can &ePerfect Overclock&r recipes depending on the &ctemperature of the machine&r. You can check its current temperature by clicking on the controller."
		""
		"There are two ways to increase the temperature:"
		"1) Upgrade the coils"
		"2) Use higher-tier energy: every tier above &bMV&r adds 100K"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"To see the temperature of a coil, hover over it."
		""
		"Once you know your machine's temperature, you'll need the temperature of the recipe. The easiest way to find it is to use EMI."
		""
		"With both values, you can do a quick calculation to see if Perfect Overclocking applies:"
		"&bYour machine must be at least 1800K hotter than the recipe for each overclock you want to be perfect.&r"
		""
		"It also gets a small energy discount for every 900K it runs above the recipe."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Example:"
		"- Stainless Steel requires &c1700K&r and is an &6HV&r recipe."
		"- You run it on &5EV&r power: that's one overclock."
		"- For it to be perfect, the furnace needs 1700 + 1800 = &c3500K&r."
		"- Cupronickel coils (1800K) reach 2000K on EV and Kanthal coils (2700K) 2900K: a normal overclock. Nichrome coils (3600K) reach 3800K: a perfect one."
		""
		"Feeling overwhelmed? Just remember this: better coils = faster and cheaper recipes."
	]
	quest.3CF09447EDDB3B33.quest_subtitle: "You don't need to understand this one"
	quest.3CF09447EDDB3B33.title: "The Blast Overclocking"
	quest.3D0A5D059655EB83.quest_desc: [
		"&o...or little brother. Don't let him know!&r"
		""
		"The &3Steam Oven&r is a great multiblock option if you need to &6effortlessly smelt large quantities of items.&r No more lines of furnaces that you have to manually empty and refuel!"
		""
		"It effectively behaves as a parallel furnace, smelting up to 8 items at a time for a low cost of Steam. Like every steam multiblock, its recipes take half again as long as EMI shows. Press the EMI 'Uses' key (U) on the controller to see the structure; click a block to see what fits there."
	]
	quest.3D0A5D059655EB83.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Furnace's big brother"
	quest.3D0A5D059655EB83.title: "Steam Oven"
	quest.3D682B481D907011.quest_desc: [
		"Utilizing a &bHigh Quality Cloth&r, such as &aWool&r or &aSilk Cloth&r, you can create your very own &dBed.&r Unlike the &2Thatch Bed&r, a real &dBed&r is comfortable enough to sleep through the night. Sweet Dreams!"
	]
	quest.3D682B481D907011.quest_subtitle: "Rest your weary soul."
	quest.3D682B481D907011.title: "Beds"
	quest.3D897027F7BD8EE2.quest_desc: [
		"A tier-2 anvil works brass and bronze; wrought iron needs it too."
		""
		"Weld 14 ingots in pairs on your copper anvil (with flux) and craft the seven double ingots into the anvil. Bismuth bronze and black bronze make tier-2 anvils as well, but don't mix the three."
		""
		"Bronze also opens Create (andesite alloy takes bronze nuggets) and GregTech's bronze steam machines."
	]
	quest.3D897027F7BD8EE2.quest_subtitle: "For brass and iron"
	quest.3D897027F7BD8EE2.title: "Bronze Anvil"
	quest.3DB2937CFB46B93D.quest_desc: [
		"Melt native copper, malachite or tetrahedrite in a small vessel and pour it into a fired ingot mold. Ingot molds have a 10% chance to break each cast."
		""
		"TFC ores come in grades: small 10 mB, poor 15, normal 25, rich 35; an ingot is 100 mB."
		""
		"Anvils aren't cheap! Each anvil takes 14 ingots, welded into 7 double ingots: 140 small ore pieces' worth of copper. You might want to start mining (or panning) at this point if you haven't already."
	]
	quest.3DB2937CFB46B93D.quest_subtitle: "Your first metal"
	quest.3DB2937CFB46B93D.title: "Copper"
	quest.3DBFA585D3177E1B.quest_desc: [
		"Gold is used in the bronze age for TFC's rose gold, and in GregTech for electrum and the gold cables of &6HV&r."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC native gold."
	]
	quest.3DBFA585D3177E1B.quest_subtitle: "Element #79"
	quest.3DBFA585D3177E1B.title: "Gold"
	quest.3DC9B17AFDD3500E.quest_desc: [
		"A wrought iron grill turns a firepit into a grill: use it on a firepit. It cooks five items at once, and food cooked on it gets the Wood Grilled trait, which makes it keep a little longer."
		""
		"Work a wrought iron double sheet into a grill on a wrought iron anvil."
	]
	quest.3DC9B17AFDD3500E.quest_subtitle: "Cook five at once"
	quest.3DC9B17AFDD3500E.title: "Grill"
	quest.3DDCFC0DA1D27547.quest_desc: [
		"Weld two wrought iron sheets. Create's mechanical press needs one."
	]
	quest.3DDCFC0DA1D27547.quest_subtitle: "For the press"
	quest.3DDCFC0DA1D27547.title: "Wrought Iron Double Sheet"
	quest.3F3722D5DCBF2FAD.quest_desc: [
		"Obtain &aPhenol&r from:"
		""
		"&91 -&r &aWood Tar&r distillation."
		""
		"&92 -&r Reacting &aBenzene&r with &dChlorine&r and &dSodium Hydroxide&r This should be performed in an &3LCR&r, and the Chlorine is perfectly looped."
		""
		"&93 -&r Shortcutting the above recipe by ignoring the &dSodium Hydroxide&r. This is net negative on &dChlorine&r."
		""
		"&94 -&r Reacting &aBenzene&r, &dPropene&r and &dOxygen&r using a small amount of &4Phosphoric Acid&r - normally a catalyst, but consumed here in small quantities. This is called the Cumene process."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"If you're having trouble deciding between the options presented, here's the appeal of each route:"
		""
		"&91 -&r Great if you're willing to set up a &3Pyrolyse Oven&r + &3Distillation Tower&r combo."
		""
		"&92 -&r This one's our preference! You can use the &dSalt&r to make more &dSalt Water&r, then electrolyze to create a loop."
		""
		"&93 -&r Very appealing if you have an infinite supply of &dChlorine&r. You could achieve this by setting up a &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r on a Salt Water vein."
		""
		"&94 -&r ...&4Phosphoric Acid&r is a pain to produce. You'd be mad to consider this."
	]
	quest.3F3722D5DCBF2FAD.title: "Phenol"
	quest.3FFCD30F9F072365.quest_desc: [
		"To work &dGlass&r you'll need a variety of tools, held in your off-hand while you use the blowpipe."
		""
		"&3Paddle&r: Performs flatten, mainly used for creating &dGlass Panes&r and &dLamp Glass.&r"
		""
		"&3Gem Saw&r: Performs saw, the last step of most glass products. It also breaks placed &dGlass Blocks&r and &dPanes&r so you get them back."
		""
		"&3Jacks&r: Used to pinch glass, needed for &dLamp Glass&r and &dJars.&r"
		""
		"&3Wool Cloth&r: Used for rolling glass, needed for &dLenses&r and &dJars.&r"
	]
	quest.3FFCD30F9F072365.quest_subtitle: "Tools of the Trade"
	quest.3FFCD30F9F072365.title: "Glassblowing Tools"
	quest.400E9781E2007E3F.quest_desc: [
		"Once you find graphite, bring back as much as you can, though you'll need far less of it than kaolin clay."
		""
		"Grind it in a quern: one graphite gives four graphite powder, enough for one fire clay."
	]
	quest.400E9781E2007E3F.quest_subtitle: "Pencils do not exist"
	quest.400E9781E2007E3F.title: "Graphite"
	quest.406A3F6F0D74FC37.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Large Steam Turbine&r — or &dLST&r — is GregTech's first large generator, built at &6HV&r from an HV hull, HV circuits, steel gears and large steel pipes. In a pack that runs on boilers, it's the natural next step after a wall of single-block steam turbines."
		""
		"To make it work you'll need an Input Hatch for steam, an Output Hatch for the distilled water it gives back, and a Maintenance Hatch. Like all Large Turbines, it takes a Rotor Holder on one side and a Dynamo Hatch to extract the power."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Rotor Holder must be at least &6HV&r, and each tier above that doubles the output. The rotor's power multiplies it further, and its efficiency stretches each mB of steam."
		""
		"Size the Dynamo Hatch to what your holder and rotor produce: a normal Dynamo Hatch handles 2A. Check EMI's multiblock preview for the exact structure."
	]
	quest.406A3F6F0D74FC37.quest_subtitle: "Your boilers, scaled up"
	quest.406A3F6F0D74FC37.title: "The Large Steam Turbine"
	quest.4100AE6929808748.quest_desc: [
		"Ruthenium is used in RTM alloy, for heating coils, and in ruridit."
		""
		"It comes from GregTech's platinum line: a chemical reactor turns purified TFC tetrahedrite ore and nitric acid into platinum group sludge, and centrifuging the sludge with aqua regia (&6HV&r) gives inert metal mixture. A chemical reactor (&5EV&r) splits that with sulfuric acid into rhodium sulfate and ruthenium tetroxide, and ruthenium tetroxide with carbon gives ruthenium."
	]
	quest.4100AE6929808748.quest_subtitle: "Element #44"
	quest.4100AE6929808748.title: "Ruthenium"
	quest.4168ACDF3DB192BD.quest_desc: [
		"From now on, all Circuits should be made in a &3Circuit Assembler&r. Use it now to enjoy &6far cheaper LV and MV circuits&r."
		""
		"Each time you upgrade to a new tier of &3Circuit Assembler&r, you will be able to craft more &dadvanced themes&r of circuit. These will use &ccomplex&r and &msometimes&r unfamiliar ingredients, but will be more efficient to craft overall."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The Circuit Assembler has made appearances in and out of GregTech versions. GT5 did not have it, and it was reimplemented in GT5 Unofficial. GTCE decided not to port it, and the tug-of-war continues with its inclusion in GTCEu."
	]
	quest.4168ACDF3DB192BD.quest_subtitle: "Hopefully, your first MV Circuit expense"
	quest.4168ACDF3DB192BD.title: "The Circuit Assembler"
	quest.41852D3A9E54EFE7.quest_desc: [
		"Besides the monsters, the biggest challenge when mining is dealing with cave-ins. Mining raw rock near rock that isn't supported can start a collapse, and once one has started even supported rock can come down. Rock with a solid block beneath it is supported, and cave roofs are naturally supported. The safest thing you can do is just mine the floor, but if you want to safely mine anything else you'll have to learn how to use support beams! These are crafted from logs and a saw."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Placing a support beam on a block raises a vertical column up to three tall, and horizontal beams connect two vertical ones up to five blocks apart. Only the horizontal beams support rock: anything within a 9 x 5 x 9 area around them. The field guide's Support Beams page has diagrams."
		""
		"Ore that collapses drops a grade (rich becomes normal, normal becomes poor), so support your veins!"
	]
	quest.41852D3A9E54EFE7.quest_subtitle: "Thought the surface was difficult? Think again."
	quest.41852D3A9E54EFE7.title: "Mining Hazards"
	quest.418E0D495286B5E0.quest_desc: [
		"Steel Crates are a big upgrade over wooden and bronze crates or walls of chests, boasting a whopping &672&r inventory slots."
	]
	quest.418E0D495286B5E0.quest_subtitle: "That's a lot of space!"
	quest.418E0D495286B5E0.title: "Steel Crate"
	quest.419312C4AB7C7771.quest_desc: [
		"&dSticky Resin&r stands in for slime balls in some recipes, and goes into &aResistors&r and &aCircuit Boards&r, which you'll need a fair bit of to advance into the &7Low Voltage&r age."
		""
		"GregTech's rubber trees grow in this world: chop their natural logs and they usually drop sticky resin. A steam extractor turns it into raw rubber."
	]
	quest.419312C4AB7C7771.quest_subtitle: "No, it's not Rosin"
	quest.419312C4AB7C7771.title: "Sticky Resin"
	quest.421D5FC3023E98A7.quest_desc: [
		"&6The best MV Circuits&r! You will be making these for the remainder of the game."
		""
		"Eventually (in &9IV&r), they will become even cheaper."
	]
	quest.421D5FC3023E98A7.quest_subtitle: "MV has peaked"
	quest.421D5FC3023E98A7.title: "Best MV Circuits"
	quest.42260225CD66E0D4.quest_desc: [
		"Hello there, and welcome to &bMV Energy Production&r."
		""
		"In this quest, we'll go over the options for keeping your &bMV machines&r powered and running smoothly."
		""
		"We won't cover this in every chapter, so we highly recommend that you &aread the GregTech Power chapter&r for a deeper understanding of how everything works."
		""
		"For now, here are your options:"
		""
		"&7- &bUse an MV Generator&r to directly produce &bMV-level energy&r."
		""
		"&7- &bStep up your &7LV&r power with transformers&r, with a &e4:1 ratio&r between &7LV&r and &bMV&r amps."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Higher-tier Generators burn fuel faster in proportion to what they produce, so a bucket of fuel still gives the same energy. The &3Advanced Steam Turbine&r uses &d5,120 mB Steam&r per second, equivalent to &d256 mB/t&r."
		""
		"Get &eany&r of these generators or transformers to complete this quest, but you may prefer starting off with the &3Advanced Steam Turbine&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are a few new power options at &bMV&r. Look up the Generators in EMI and press &4U&r to see which fuels count as &aCombustion&r or &aGas&r fuels."
		""
		"The quests about fuels in this chapter cover the valuable options."
		""
		"If you stick to &9Steam&r for your Power generation, you'll probably want a &3Large Boiler&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&3Transformers&r step power safely up and down between voltage tiers. They turn the power they receive into the same amount of power one tier above or below."
		""
		"Apart from running machines on other tiers, Transformers help carry power over long distances, as cable loss matters less at higher voltages. Just like real life!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Transformers have 5 low voltage sides, and 1 high voltage side."
		""
		"The basic Transformer converts 1A <-> 4A; the &9Hi-Amp&r Transformers move more amps at once."
		""
		"A new Transformer steps down; use a &aScrewdriver&r to switch it to stepping up. From &bMV&r up, Transformers also need integrated circuit chips (ULPIC chips at &bMV&r)."
	]
	quest.42260225CD66E0D4.quest_subtitle: "Things are 'boutta get rough"
	quest.42260225CD66E0D4.title: "Electricity Generation in MV"
	quest.42C3416594DABC22.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Sapphire Lens, engrave a Silicon Wafer into an ULPIC Wafer."
		""
		"This can be processed in a Cutter for ULPIC Chips, which are important for some multiblock components!"
		""
		"More specifically, the MV Energy Hatches that you will need to upgrade your EBF to the &6HV&r energy tier."
	]
	quest.42C3416594DABC22.quest_subtitle: "Pickin' up Chips"
	quest.42C3416594DABC22.title: "ULPIC Chips"
	quest.43233C1BE7B94FCA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Superconductors&r are special Wires available for each Voltage tier. They don't come with a Cable counterpart, but that isn't necessary, as they have absolutely &6zero cable loss&r."
		""
		"They also won't damage you when you touch them. This makes them the best choice for wiring, if not a little expensive in comparison to the other wires."
		""
		"The &7LV&r one is Manganese Phosphide. Manganese has no ore of its own here: electrolyzing spessartine (from red garnet) gives it, and that needs an &bMV&r Electrolyzer."
		""
		"When it's time, replace your crappy &aTin Cables&r. The &3Extractor&r melts them back into tin and rubber."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o No version of GregTech has had actual Superconductors for &7LV&f up until Gregicality and GTCEu, though some modpacks had lossless cables."
	]
	quest.43233C1BE7B94FCA.quest_subtitle: "No loss no bzzz"
	quest.43233C1BE7B94FCA.title: "LV Superconductor"
	quest.432641555426039E.quest_desc: [
		"&dUltimet&r is a high-performance material, providing excellent &eSpeed&r for your &bDrill&r or &bWrench&r, and makes for a &eTurbine Rotor&r with very good &bEfficiency&r."
		""
		"You'll need it even if you skip the tools: the &5EV&r Cutter, the &5EV&r Rotor Holder and the casing of &5EV&r Lapotronic Batteries are all made from it. Mix Cobalt, Chromium, Nickel and Molybdenum in the &6HV&r Mixer; the ingots come out of the EBF hot, so cool them in the &dVacuum Freezer&r."
	]
	quest.432641555426039E.quest_subtitle: "Ultimet is the ultimate"
	quest.432641555426039E.title: "Ultimet"
	quest.438BDE947E1F9FD5.quest_desc: [
		"Niobium dust is a by-product of refined pyrolusite when it is macerated (14%). It makes niobium nitride (HV chemistry) and, with titanium, the superconductor wire of IV and above."
	]
	quest.438BDE947E1F9FD5.quest_subtitle: "Superconductors start here"
	quest.438BDE947E1F9FD5.title: "Niobium"
	quest.440CA363F5E74068.quest_desc: [
		"While combat may not be the first thing you think to do with your hammer, it can be surprisingly effective. Hammers deal &2Crushing&r damage which can help you against Skeletons. "
		""
		"For more information on &cDamage Types&r consult the &3Field Guide&r."
	]
	quest.440CA363F5E74068.quest_subtitle: "It's hammer time!"
	quest.440CA363F5E74068.title: "Hammers"
	quest.4428D6E39558777F.quest_desc: [
		"For now, you should use &9Water&r for its recipes instead of trying to acquire Lubricant."
		""
		"If you don't have one yet, this machine will also cut &6Rods into four Bolts&r."
		""
		"This machine is the only way to obtain &dGem Plates&r, which are needed to craft Filters, and by extension, the &3Gas Collector&r."
	]
	quest.4428D6E39558777F.quest_subtitle: "The Cutter... cuts..."
	quest.4428D6E39558777F.title: "Basic Cutter"
	quest.44717F43067E0B98.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Implosion Compressor&r turns the Dust form of Gems into their Gem form."
		""
		"It's required to get &aEnder Pearls&r."
		""
		"&cTNT&r can be used for the Implosion."
	]
	quest.44717F43067E0B98.title: "Implosion Compressor"
	quest.447F14001EAF97A0.quest_desc: [
		"With the black steel anvil you can work black steel ingots into tools, armour and parts."
		""
		"GregTech doesn't wait for it in this pack: high-pressure steam and LV electrics need only steel. Dive into industry now, or finish the last tier of anvils first."
	]
	quest.447F14001EAF97A0.quest_subtitle: "Tier V"
	quest.447F14001EAF97A0.title: "T5 Anvil: Black Steel"
	quest.44F85BB206730CA4.quest_desc: [
		"Create's press already turns one ingot into one plate, but the Bender does more. It rolls a plate into &6four Foils&r (a hammer gets two), and you'll want a pile of bronze foils for your first heating coils. At &bMV&r it also bends double plates."
		""
		"And yes, it bends plates one for one too, if you'd rather keep it all electric."
	]
	quest.44F85BB206730CA4.quest_subtitle: "The Bender bends!"
	quest.44F85BB206730CA4.title: "Basic Bender"
	quest.454D1CA82011EC37.quest_desc: [
		"Resistors are components that will be used to make your first Circuit: sticky resin, paper, copper wire and a pinch of coal or charcoal dust."
		""
		"Wires may be expensive right now: Create's mechanical saw slits a copper plate into two. Once you have an LV &3Wiremill&r, switch to the recipes with &aFine Wires&r; one copper ingot makes eight."
	]
	quest.454D1CA82011EC37.quest_subtitle: "The more... resistant... component for circuits"
	quest.454D1CA82011EC37.title: "Electronics #1: Resistors"
	quest.45A2E9C48352339D.quest_desc: [
		"When you try to &aparallelize your setup&r with more machines, it can be a bother to set all the &einputs&r and &eoutputs&r for each one. Yeah, we're thinking of you, &dSuper Chests&r and &dTanks&r."
		""
		"If you ever find yourself needing this little tool, don't hesitate to use it."
	]
	quest.45A2E9C48352339D.quest_subtitle: "Copy and Paste"
	quest.45A2E9C48352339D.title: "Machine Memory Card"
	quest.45D61D76A472A3EE.quest_desc: [
		"The &aFluid Regulator&r is sort of the equivalent to a &9Robot Arm&r for Fluids."
		""
		"It can transfer fluids, but has two useful modes:"
		""
		"&9-&r &dSupply Exact&r will transfer the amount of specified Fluid per tick if available. No more, no less."
		"&9-&r &dKeep Exact&r will make sure the exact amount of Fluid in the attached machine is being kept."
		""
		"You won't need it much, because natively GT machines will fill only one slot with the &6Pump Cover&r"
	]
	quest.45D61D76A472A3EE.quest_subtitle: "A cover that you may not use much"
	quest.45D61D76A472A3EE.title: "LV Fluid Regulator"
	quest.45F778BD6955A5B6.quest_desc: [
		"You can create &dBurlap Cloth&r by soaking &aJute&r in a sealed barrel of water and weaving the resulting &aJute Fiber&r on the &3Loom&r (12 fibers per cloth)."
		""
		"In this pack burlap matters: Create's belts, spouts, funnels, tunnels and pulleys take burlap cloth (or leather), and the sewing table uses it too."
	]
	quest.45F778BD6955A5B6.quest_subtitle: "Made out of Jute or Flax!"
	quest.45F778BD6955A5B6.title: "Burlap Cloth"
	quest.463612770FB9427E.quest_desc: [
		"&eTungsten&r comes from &aScheelite&r or &aTungstate&r dust: bathe it in Hydrochloric Acid in an &5EV Chemical Bath&r to get &bTungstic Acid&r, with Calcium Chloride or Lithium Chloride on the side."
		""
		"Neither mineral has its own veins in this pack."
		""
		"Take your time, optimize, and the Tungsten Line will become the foundation of your mid-to-late game progress."
	]
	quest.463612770FB9427E.quest_subtitle: "Why? Just why?"
	quest.463612770FB9427E.title: "The Tungsten Line"
	quest.4639037DE458ADC1.quest_desc: [
		"With your new Stone Axe, you'll be able to chop down trees. Breaking the base of a tree fells the whole tree, logs and leaves included; break leaves one by one if you want saplings and sticks."
		""
		"Gather at least 10 logs -- 8 of these will be used for a Pit Kiln while the other two will be used for a Fire Pit."
	]
	quest.4639037DE458ADC1.quest_subtitle: "Timber!"
	quest.4639037DE458ADC1.title: "Gather Logs"
	quest.465196AF7894448D.quest_desc: [
		"It's all about making energy, right? This part won't be the most complicated one: in this pack all electricity comes from &5GregTech's&r own generators. Steam turbines fed by your boilers come first; gas turbines and combustion generators join them as you unlock their fuels."
		""
		"You'll learn about the various &6methods to generate energy&r, as well as some of the &afuels&r you can use to get the most out of your setup."
	]
	quest.465196AF7894448D.quest_subtitle: "Gas or Oil?"
	quest.465196AF7894448D.title: "Producing Energy"
	quest.46A24390F82ABD8C.quest_desc: [
		"Takes a TFC wrought iron double sheet. Presses ingots into GregTech plates one for one (by hand, GregTech takes two ingots per plate)."
		""
		"Over a basin it compacts the basin's contents instead of pressing single items."
	]
	quest.46A24390F82ABD8C.quest_subtitle: "Heavy machines"
	quest.46A24390F82ABD8C.title: "Mechanical Press"
	quest.479C04A608D19A0D.quest_desc: [
		"&dGlass Blocks&r come from a &3Basin Pour&r and glass panes (TFC's &dPoured Glass&r) from a &3Table Pour&r. Depending on the type of sand used for the &aGlass Batch&r, your glass will have a different natural color; silica glass from white sand is clear."
		""
		"Check out the &2Field Guide&r section on &3Glass Products&r to learn how powders added from a &aBowl&r make other colors. Later on, &3GregTech&r's Chemical Bath can dye glass blocks with liquid dye."
	]
	quest.479C04A608D19A0D.quest_subtitle: "Get yourself some windows."
	quest.479C04A608D19A0D.title: "Glass Blocks"
	quest.4815EA0FDABCC49F.quest_desc: [
		"We won't go over the &dfull scale of regular Ore Processing&r. Why regular? Some ores require special treatment, but that's a topic for much later. Oh no, we're already getting carried away!"
		""
		"Some machines like the &bChemical Bath&r or the &bElectrolyser&r could be useful."
		""
		"Intimidated by ore processing? Check the dedicated &cOre Processing&r chapter for a full walkthrough!"
	]
	quest.4815EA0FDABCC49F.quest_subtitle: "You can't escape Greg..."
	quest.4815EA0FDABCC49F.title: "But wait, there's more!"
	quest.4885FED598655330.quest_desc: [
		"Obviously, storing energy can also mean storing the fuel that makes it."
		""
		"For this, Drums and Crates are decent early options, but don't overlook GregTech's &dSuper Tanks&r and &dSuper Chests&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"These hold huge amounts of fluid or items — handy for fuelling generators far from your main base without building a whole cable network."
		""
		"Load them up with fuel and let them handle the rest. With proper planning, an outpost can run with no live connection to your central grid."
		""
		"Energy doesn't always come in wires — sometimes, it comes in barrels."
	]
	quest.4885FED598655330.quest_subtitle: "There's more kinds of batteries than just electric ones"
	quest.4885FED598655330.title: "Storing Fuel"
	quest.48FB5CBF72033CB9.quest_desc: [
		"This column shows what to do with your purified ore."
	]
	quest.48FB5CBF72033CB9.title: "Purified Ore"
	quest.4936A2CB9A0BE3EB.quest_desc: [
		"Steam machines take over the hand work: the &3Steam Macerator&r crushes TFC ore at twice TFC's yield and crushed ore into impure dust, the &3Steam Forge Hammer&r does the hammer's crafting-grid steps, and the &3Steam Furnace&r smelts crushed ore and dusts."
		""
		"Washing still means a cauldron, and byproducts wait for LV."
	]
	quest.4936A2CB9A0BE3EB.quest_subtitle: "Steam does the hammering"
	quest.4936A2CB9A0BE3EB.title: "Steam Age Ore Processing"
	quest.49433FB7142A4A72.quest_desc: [
		"Extracting valuable resources from the ground is a major part of this modpack, and you will consume a &llot&r of metal from here on. One way to mine a lot of it at once is a GregTech mining hammer: it breaks a 3x3 area at a slower speed. Hold sneak to break single blocks."
		""
		"The spade does the same for dirt, sand and gravel. The first ones you can make, in bronze, rose gold or sterling silver, come with the bronze age."
		""
		"Mind TFC's cave-ins: big holes in raw rock bring the roof down unless you put up support beams."
	]
	quest.49433FB7142A4A72.quest_subtitle: "ROCK AND STONE!"
	quest.49433FB7142A4A72.title: "Mining in the Metallurgy Age"
	quest.4973E7360D59CD0F.quest_desc: [
		"Once you get to LV, you may be interested in using a &bChemical Bath&r with &dSodium Persulfate&r to get some extra byproducts. Not all ores can be processed this way, but the ones that can will get a &670 percent&r chance of a byproduct, compared to the &633 percent&r of the &bOre Washer&r."
		""
		"Sodium persulfate comes from electrolyzing sodium bisulfate, and it can be a little annoying to mass produce."
		""
		"The quest below gives the crushed ores worth the investment."
	]
	quest.4973E7360D59CD0F.quest_subtitle: "Not just for circuit board etching"
	quest.4973E7360D59CD0F.title: "Bathe them in Sodium Persulfate"
	quest.4A27ACFA2CB363AD.quest_desc: [
		"Wash that dirty dust!"
	]
	quest.4A27ACFA2CB363AD.title: "Impure Dust"
	quest.4A3D52DC9A46F608.quest_desc: [
		"Carrying around a water source would be an easy way to never run out, but it doesn't work here."
		""
		"A Wooden Bucket, made from lumber, holds 1000 mB of any fluid for filling barrels and pots, but it cannot place source blocks: pouring it out only makes a small puddle that quickly disappears."
	]
	quest.4A3D52DC9A46F608.quest_subtitle: "Not as easy as you think"
	quest.4A3D52DC9A46F608.title: "Wooden Bucket"
	quest.4A3F3437DFC7ABE5.quest_desc: [
		"&aAmmonia&r is &doptional&r in &6HV&r."
		""
		"You may use it in the production of:"
		"&9-&r Nitric Acid, although we don't recommend this."
		"&9-&r Polybenzimidazole (now THAT'S a tongue twister!) in &1IV&r."
		""
		"The \"least painful\" recipe should be the one in the &3HV Chemical Reactor&r, from Hydrogen and Nitrogen. Make sure your &aHydrogen&r production (mostly from &aWater electrolysis&r) is enough to support the demand."
		""
		"Distilling Coal Gas or Fermented Biomass also gives some &aAmmonia&r."
	]
	quest.4A3F3437DFC7ABE5.title: "Ammonia"
	quest.4A85761B9BD5B512.quest_desc: [
		"With &5GregTech&r comes its own line of armor. Sure, it was cool to wear &7metal plates&r, but now that you're an &bindustrial maniac&r, maybe it's time to check out some &atechnological armor&r."
		""
		"The first model, the &6NanoMuscle™ Suite&r, becomes available around &6HV&r. It runs on charge like the power tools and brings night vision, freedom from fall damage and, later, a &dJetpack&r upgrade."
		""
		"The second model, &dQuarkTech™&r, won't be available until much later — around &1IV&r and &dLuV&r."
	]
	quest.4A85761B9BD5B512.title: "GregTech Armor"
	quest.4AFA6ED4A5A1FE79.quest_desc: [
		"Anvils are the foundation of all early game metal working. To create a proper metal anvil, you'll need to weld ingots using the previous tier of Anvil. Since Copper is the first tier, you have to use a Rock Anvil to weld them. Make one by right-clicking the top face of a block of raw igneous rock with a hammer. Welding ingots is the only thing it can do, unfortunately - you'll need the metal's proper anvil to shape them into anything else."
	]
	quest.4AFA6ED4A5A1FE79.quest_subtitle: "This won't last long"
	quest.4AFA6ED4A5A1FE79.title: "Rock Anvil"
	quest.4B0C155879B01B90.quest_desc: [
		"Rotor Holders naturally require a Rotor to use, but there's a lot of options and they all have different stats, so what do they all mean?"
		""
		"Higher &9Efficiency&r makes each mB of fuel last longer. Meanwhile, &9Power&r will increase how much EU the turbine will generate. Lastly, &9Durability&r should be obvious."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Ideally, you'll want to maximize all three, but the choice depends on how much fuel you're producing, how many turbines you have, and how often you want to replace them, so there's no definitive correct answer."
		""
		"A rotor is eight turbine blades on a long magnalium rod, put together in an &6HV&r Assembler. Hover over a rotor to compare its stats."
	]
	quest.4B0C155879B01B90.quest_subtitle: "So many choices!"
	quest.4B0C155879B01B90.title: "Turbine Rotors"
	quest.4B718D8FDA012BA8.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Arc Furnace&r uses a lil' bit of &9Oxygen&r to smelt items in a different fashion than Furnaces."
		""
		"It can &adouble your Glass&r (two per sand), gives you &aAnnealed Copper&r for cheaper electronic components, and melts metal parts such as plates, rods, wires and pipes back into ingots."
	]
	quest.4B718D8FDA012BA8.quest_subtitle: "The Arc Furnace has never been so good"
	quest.4B718D8FDA012BA8.title: "The Arc Furnace"
	quest.4B964648327668AF.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you've got some electricity going, it's time to use it! We recommend starting by making machines that will make it easier and cheaper to make even more machines."
		""
		"Create already does part of that job in this pack: the press makes plates one for one and the saw slits a plate into two wires. GregTech's machines add what Create can't: foils, screws, fine wire, magnetic rods, molten metals and chemistry."
	]
	quest.4B964648327668AF.quest_subtitle: "More options!"
	quest.4B964648327668AF.title: "Your next machines"
	quest.4B98A0DD1B3B274A.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a Firestarter from two sticks. Throw one log and three sticks on the ground (up to five pieces of kindling, such as straw, raise the odds), then hold right-click on them with the firestarter until they catch."
		""
		"The firepit cooks food, heats metal and later lights pit kilns and charcoal pits. Heating sticks in it makes torches. Keep it burning by adding logs (or stick bundles or peat) in its screen; if it goes out, add fuel and light it again."
		""
		"Monsters don't spawn on the surface here, but nocturnal predators prowl at night."
	]
	quest.4B98A0DD1B3B274A.quest_subtitle: "A firepit"
	quest.4B98A0DD1B3B274A.title: "Fire"
	quest.4C08B04860EA4578.quest_desc: [
		"Want to try something plant-based but without a tree farm? Give &3Bio Diesel&r a shot! Extract &dSeed Oil&r from seeds (look it up in EMI), then just mix it with a little Ethanol and Sodium Hydroxide (from Sea Water!) in a Chemical Reactor and you're done! As a bonus, this route also outputs Glycerol, which you can react with Carbon Dioxide into &dEthylene&r!"
	]
	quest.4C08B04860EA4578.quest_subtitle: "Flower Power"
	quest.4C08B04860EA4578.title: "The Church of Bio Diesel"
	quest.4C2F42149272CA77.quest_desc: [
		"The final tier of anvil! A red or blue steel anvil (tier VI) works both red and blue steel ingots."
		""
		"This is the top of TerraFirmaCraft's metalworking; from here on, GregTech carries the metal."
	]
	quest.4C2F42149272CA77.quest_subtitle: "It's over"
	quest.4C2F42149272CA77.title: "T6 Anvil: Red or Blue Steel"
	quest.4C5A3B14C4AED0B7.quest_desc: [
		"The sea floor holds ores that no land vein has. Copper diving gear is enough to reach all of it: there is no pressure or depth limit, only air. A full backtank is fifteen minutes; place it, give it rotation and it fills again."
		""
		"Deep ocean floors lie at about y -17 and the trenches at -48, and lava starts at -54: red steel diving gear does not make lava safe (see the Tips). Mining under water is slow without Aqua Affinity."
	]
	quest.4C5A3B14C4AED0B7.quest_subtitle: "The ocean is open at copper"
	quest.4C5A3B14C4AED0B7.title: "Down to the Floor"
	quest.4CBBBA90E6A30001.quest_desc: [
		"Steel boilers make steam faster; high-pressure steam machines run at full speed."
	]
	quest.4CBBBA90E6A30001.quest_subtitle: "Steel boilers"
	quest.4CBBBA90E6A30001.title: "High-Pressure Steam"
	quest.4CCDA49060A81CA3.quest_desc: [
		"TerraFirmaCraft on a real-scale Earth, mechanized with Create, industrialized with GregTech, with airships from Create Aeronautics."
		""
		"The route: TFC's stone, copper and bronze ages; Create from the bronze age; TFC's iron; GregTech's steam age, which runs on Create parts; TFC steel; GregTech electricity. Airships open with brass."
		""
		"Look up any recipe in EMI: hover an item and press R for its recipes, U for its uses. TFC's field guide explains survival, knapping, pottery and metalworking."
		""
		"On a server, /startat <latitude> <longitude> moves you once to any place on Earth (south and west are negative), e.g. /startat 59.33 18.07 for Stockholm."
	]
	quest.4CCDA49060A81CA3.quest_subtitle: "TFC, then Create, then GregTech"
	quest.4CCDA49060A81CA3.title: "The Route"
	quest.4CDE5CF99FF8439B.quest_desc: [
		"As is common for every tier, the &3Circuit Assembler&r is an essential part of progression, always opening up a new Tier of circuits."
		""
		"At this point you should be placing a &3Drum&r next to your Circuit Assembler. Fill it absolutely full of solder fluid, and you won't have to worry about refilling for a long time."
	]
	quest.4CDE5CF99FF8439B.quest_subtitle: "Yippee, yahoo"
	quest.4CDE5CF99FF8439B.title: "Your Second Circuit Assembler"
	quest.4CE856BC14AE2185.quest_desc: [
		"This column shows ways to process raw ore, the first step of ore processing! Here that's TFC's ore pieces (small, poor, normal and rich, plus the mineral and gem ores); GregTech's own ore blocks and raw ores don't generate in this pack."
	]
	quest.4CE856BC14AE2185.title: "Raw Ore"
	quest.4CE8AF3DAB10B051.quest_desc: [
		"To help you along, here's an overview of the steps to &dRuthenium&r through the Platline: centrifuge &dPlatinum Group Sludge&r with Aqua Regia, react the &aInert Metal Mixture&r with Sulfuric Acid in an &5EV&r Chemical Reactor for &aRuthenium Tetroxide&r, then reduce it with Carbon."
		""
		"Don't worry, you don't need to complete the entire &dPlatline&r yet."
	]
	quest.4CE8AF3DAB10B051.quest_subtitle: "A rare material"
	quest.4CE8AF3DAB10B051.title: "Ruthenium"
	quest.4CFECFD85067967E.quest_desc: [
		"Not much happens at MV except that the electrolyzer becomes much more powerful."
	]
	quest.4CFECFD85067967E.title: "&bMV&r Ore Processing"
	quest.4D1A3CDFA01373C4.quest_desc: [
		"Yttrium goes into yttrium barium cuprate and other superconductors."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aCassiterite&r gives &aMonazite&r as its &3Ore Washer&r by-product. An &3Electrolyzer&r splits monazite dust into rare earth and phosphate, and a &3Centrifuge&r separates rare earth into small piles of cadmium, neodymium, samarium, cerium, yttrium and lanthanum."
	]
	quest.4D1A3CDFA01373C4.quest_subtitle: "Element #39"
	quest.4D1A3CDFA01373C4.title: "Yttrium"
	quest.4D533A724C2FCE97.quest_desc: [
		"Congrats on making your first &6Tungsten&r! Electrolyze &bTungstic Acid&r in an &5EV&r Electrolyzer for Tungsten dust, plus some Hydrogen and Oxygen back."
		""
		"Tungsten ingots need an &3EBF&r at 3,600K (Nichrome coils will do) and come out hot."
		""
		"Remember that the further you progress, the more important it will be to build dedicated and passive lines for all these complex processes that will be required until the end of the pack. Don't be afraid of lacking resources, be afraid of lacking time."
	]
	quest.4D533A724C2FCE97.quest_subtitle: "Heavy metal"
	quest.4D533A724C2FCE97.title: "Tungsten"
	quest.4E35DAC659C5E12C.quest_desc: [
		"Molybdenum goes into RTM alloy, molybdenum disilicide coils and several high-tier alloys."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aMalachite&r gives &aMolybdenite&r as its &3Thermal Centrifuge&r by-product; an &3Electrolyzer&r splits it into molybdenum and sulfur."
	]
	quest.4E35DAC659C5E12C.quest_subtitle: "Element #42"
	quest.4E35DAC659C5E12C.title: "Molybdenum"
	quest.4E49CEA68BDBAFC1.quest_desc: [
		"Arsenic goes into gallium arsenide, and with it every diode and silicon boule."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r: TFC &aTetrahedrite&r carries &aRealgar&r, the &3Thermal Centrifuge&r's by-product of crushed tetrahedrite. &3Centrifuge&r realgar dust into arsenic and sulfur."
	]
	quest.4E49CEA68BDBAFC1.quest_subtitle: "Element #33"
	quest.4E49CEA68BDBAFC1.title: "Arsenic"
	quest.4E7CE1039CEF5852.quest_desc: [
		"Fish have never been so easy to catch. Well, almost. Forge a &dFish Hook&r on an anvil and craft it into a &dFishing Rod&r with sticks and string."
		""
		"A rod is useless without &abait&r, added on the crafting grid: &aseeds&r or &ashellfish&r for normal fish, and cod, salmon, tropical fish or bluegill for big catches like dolphins and orcas."
		""
		"Cast, wait for a bite, then reel in without pulling too fast or the fish gets away with your bait. Pull it onto land and finish it with a tool."
	]
	quest.4E7CE1039CEF5852.quest_subtitle: "Patience is a virtue."
	quest.4E7CE1039CEF5852.title: "Fishing Rods"
	quest.4EB5E57BDDC0647B.quest_desc: [
		"The &7LV Combustion Generator&r burns liquid fuels that carry a lot of energy per mB, so a drum of fuel can power a generator far from your base."
		""
		"Like other &7LV Generators&r, it produces &a32 EU/t&r."
		""
		"In this pack its fuels (ethanol, methanol, &2Bio Diesel&r, then oil products) arrive at &bMV&r, so this one can wait until then."
	]
	quest.4EB5E57BDDC0647B.quest_subtitle: "It does boom and make energy"
	quest.4EB5E57BDDC0647B.title: "The Combustion Generator"
	quest.4F07D0C306DFEE2B.quest_desc: [
		"One of the cheapest - if not the cheapest - &7LV&r machine. Use this to make &6Redstone-free Magnetic Rods&r for your Motors. Whenever you start to batch your Motors, this machine will save you stacks and stacks of Redstone."
	]
	quest.4F07D0C306DFEE2B.quest_subtitle: "The Polarizer polarizes!"
	quest.4F07D0C306DFEE2B.title: "Basic Polarizer"
	quest.4F151015B399577E.quest_desc: [
		"&6The best LV Circuits&r! You can start to churn these guys out, as you'll be making them for the rest of the game."
		""
		"Try to keep a stockpile of these crafted at all times - making these on-demand can take a while."
		""
		"Reaching &5EV&r will unlock methods to make them even cheaper."
	]
	quest.4F151015B399577E.quest_subtitle: "It Feels Good to be the Best"
	quest.4F151015B399577E.title: "Best LV Circuits"
	quest.4F1B33EABB6DB5EC.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to be less fancy, just call it plastic."
		""
		"For the polymerization process, add &aOxygen&r, which gives better returns than Air, then solidify like you would with Rubber."
		""
		"&aPolyethylene (PE)&r is the key to unlocking &6many new things&r. It's commonly used as &dSheets&r, or in &dFluid&r form."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The OreDict and fluid name for Polyethylene in 1.12.2 GTCEu was &bplastic&f, for cross-mod compatibility."
	]
	quest.4F1B33EABB6DB5EC.quest_subtitle: "Baby's first polymer!"
	quest.4F1B33EABB6DB5EC.title: "Polyethylene"
	quest.4F5B805BB902A5A4.quest_desc: [
		"Charge them up and put them on your face to get a permanent Night Vision effect as long as the batteries last!"
		""
		"The glass lens they need takes an &bMV&r Lathe."
	]
	quest.4F5B805BB902A5A4.quest_subtitle: "See in the dark!"
	quest.4F5B805BB902A5A4.title: "Nightvision Goggles"
	quest.4FCC02D5C11472D5.quest_desc: [
		"The final two anvils are made of complex alloys that take a lot of metal. Weld weak steel and pig iron into high carbon black steel, then work it on the anvil into black steel."
	]
	quest.4FCC02D5C11472D5.quest_subtitle: "Conservation of matter does not apply"
	quest.4FCC02D5C11472D5.title: "Black Steel Ingredients"
	quest.4FD6437348156D90.quest_desc: [
		"By crafting a pot and some bowls out of clay, you'll be able to create soups! Put the fired pot on a lit firepit, fill it with water, add 3 to 5 fruits, vegetables or meats and let it boil, then scoop the soup out with a bowl."
		""
		"Soups are one of the first and easiest ways to create more complex meals. Unlike eating plain ingredients, they let you consume multiple nutrients at once!"
	]
	quest.4FD6437348156D90.quest_subtitle: "Which store were you in?"
	quest.4FD6437348156D90.title: "Soups"
	quest.4FDFBB2D73FB512C.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Laser Engraver&r engraves patterns into &9Silicon Wafers&r based on the type of &9Lens&r it is given. After the wafers are engraved, they must be passed through a &3Cutting Machine&r to turn them into components ready to be put into Circuits."
		""
		"Higher tier Engravers can etch more complex wafers for more efficient Circuits."
	]
	quest.4FDFBB2D73FB512C.quest_subtitle: "Teaching rocks to think"
	quest.4FDFBB2D73FB512C.title: "Laser Engraving"
	quest.500C13EC1D23A17D.quest_desc: [
		"Don't let EMI fool you... at &7LV&r only two of its recipes work: the liquid glass ones, with fine copper (or annealed copper) wire and a small pile of Gallium Arsenide."
		""
		"Diodes have an infamously &4nasty recipe&r, but they will become cheaper and more convenient once you can obtain &ePolyethylene&r."
		""
		"This is required for &dMV Circuits&r."
	]
	quest.500C13EC1D23A17D.quest_subtitle: "Don't be swayed by EMI!"
	quest.500C13EC1D23A17D.title: "Diode"
	quest.5064EFEE162D91DC.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &6basics&r of what you need to build your first &bEBF&r, though it is highly customisable. Remember to use &6EMI&r, use &6U&r on the controller and don't hesitate to &6left click on the structure blocks&r to see what the possibilities are."
		""
		"An important notice, each Energy Hatch can accept &a2A&r, which means that at &7LV&r they can each handle &a64 EU/t&r. With two of them, your &eEBF&r can run at &a128 EU/t&r."
		""
		"For more details about this mechanic, refer to the &eGregTech Power&r chapter, specifically the &eSpending Energy&r quest."
		""
		"Multiblocks bear a large variety of interesting mechanics that might seem daunting, but don't worry - you don't need to do anything fancy right yet. You'll learn more as you go!"
	]
	quest.5064EFEE162D91DC.quest_subtitle: "Oh we love multiblocks right?"
	quest.5064EFEE162D91DC.title: "Multiblock Techniques"
	quest.506A730B9AD2ED88.quest_desc: [
		"Once you find kaolin clay, bring back as much as you can carry! Only 20% of it turns into kaolinite powder when heated (500 °C), so it's worth firing it on the spot in pit kilns to save inventory space."
		""
		"Each fire clay takes four kaolinite powder, about twenty kaolin clay, and GregTech's steam machines keep asking for fire bricks long after the crucible and blast furnace are built. Bring home more than you think you'll need, to avoid a repeat journey."
		""
		"P.S.: If you've found blood lilies but no clay, try digging down a little further! Sometimes it lies a little underground."
	]
	quest.506A730B9AD2ED88.quest_subtitle: "Kaolin Trek: The Next Generation"
	quest.506A730B9AD2ED88.title: "Kaolin Clay"
	quest.50AEDF49CB96BB60.quest_desc: [
		"These brass-geared devices measure the world around you, and each gives out a redstone signal directly, no comparator needed."
		""
		"The Precision Clock reads the hour, or the month after you toggle it."
		""
		"The Thermometer reads the air temperature, or the heat of the device it's placed on."
		""
		"The Anemometer and Weather Vane read wind speed and direction respectively."
	]
	quest.50AEDF49CB96BB60.quest_subtitle: "Detect the world around you!"
	quest.50AEDF49CB96BB60.title: "Redstone Devices"
	quest.50EAC77686C8619B.quest_desc: [
		"GregTech's energy system (EU, Energy Units) works differently to FE (Forge Energy), the system used by almost every other mod, so the book has a whole chapter on it: &eGregTech Power&r."
		""
		"It might look like a lot of reading, but it's important to understand if you want to avoid accidents and get the most out of your power generation."
		""
		"In this pack, &7LV&r power comes from Steam Turbines fed by your boilers. Gas Turbines can burn methane, and Combustion Generators get their fuels at &bMV&r."
	]
	quest.50EAC77686C8619B.quest_subtitle: "There is a whole chapter about energy"
	quest.50EAC77686C8619B.title: "Explain energy to me"
	quest.50FA8DF5D69FC4DA.quest_desc: [
		"Copper is TFC's first metal. In GregTech, copper wires, fine wires and foil go into circuit boards and electronic components from &7LV&r on."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC native copper, malachite and tetrahedrite."
	]
	quest.50FA8DF5D69FC4DA.quest_subtitle: "Element #29"
	quest.50FA8DF5D69FC4DA.title: "Copper"
	quest.5101210367294D7B.quest_desc: [
		"Besides Create's usual milling, it grinds TFC ores into GregTech crushed ore at TFC's own yield: a rich piece gives a crushed ore 35% of the time, a normal one 25%."
		""
		"It's an automatic quern: throw items in the top and take the results out with right-click (or let a funnel pull them). It's slow when turned slowly, so gear it up."
	]
	quest.5101210367294D7B.quest_subtitle: "Grinding ore"
	quest.5101210367294D7B.title: "Millstone"
	quest.51073AB9BEAC50AD.quest_desc: [
		"This is the &cu&6l&et&ai&bm&9a&5t&4e&r portable item and storage solution if you have a lot of single items or fluids. While the first (&7LV&r) Super Chests and Tanks start out relatively small, higher tiers, and the Quantum Chests and Tanks after them, can hold an insane amount of stuff - all in one single block without any regard to temperature or acidity!"
		""
		"Like Drums, Super Tanks and Chests &6keep their contents when broken&r, can be cleared in the crafting grid, and can automatically void any overflow. Unlike drums, however, Super Tanks also &asafely contain&r their contents, preventing you from getting burnt, frozen, or floating."
	]
	quest.51073AB9BEAC50AD.quest_subtitle: "Super Storage Drawers"
	quest.51073AB9BEAC50AD.title: "Super Chests and Super Tanks"
	quest.51536FE961408316.quest_desc: [
		"When placed on a machine, Robot Arms are a more configurable version of a Conveyor Module. They allow you to transfer items in specific batches, at specific rates, or keep a certain amount of items stocked."
		""
		"&9Note:&r The functionalities provided by the Robot Arm work &lonly&r if it is &lrequired&r to perform the operation."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o GregTech 5 had blocks such as the Buffer, Filter and Type Filter to allow fine control over items. In GTCE it's all been replaced by the almighty Robot Arm and various Filter Covers. Much more compact!"
	]
	quest.51536FE961408316.quest_subtitle: "You're going to hate making these"
	quest.51536FE961408316.title: "LV Robot Arm"
	quest.51FBF221533E48E8.quest_desc: [
		"If you haven't encountered them yet, Dynamo Hatches are essentially the Output equivalent of Energy Hatches. You'll want to use these on your new Large Generators for some proper EV power, covered in the next quests."
	]
	quest.51FBF221533E48E8.title: "EV Dynamo Hatch"
	quest.525033D77DA8820F.quest_desc: [
		"An important part of &6GregTech&r is its &dOre Processing Mechanics&r, but it can get pretty complicated, so this chapter is here to help!"
		""
		"In this pack GregTech's own ore veins are off: every ore is a TFC ore. Create's millstone and crushing wheels and GregTech's macerator turn TFC ore pieces into GregTech &aCrushed Ore&r, and from there GregTech's usual chain applies. GregTech-only minerals (bauxite, galena, platinum, ...) have no veins here, so their lines don't apply."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"EMI has an &6Ore Processing Diagram&r tab: press the Show Uses key (default &bU&r) on a crushed ore and look for it. It starts from GregTech's ore blocks, which don't generate here, so start reading at crushed ore."
		""
		"A major part of GregTech philosophy is that there's not just one way to solve a problem. The columns of this chapter follow an ore from raw ore to dust; the rows are the tiers that bring new machines."
	]
	quest.525033D77DA8820F.quest_subtitle: "To Process, Ore Not To Process"
	quest.525033D77DA8820F.title: "Welcome to Ore Processing"
	quest.5292CA411DA7DB85.quest_desc: [
		"In TerraFirmaCraft, the world is a harsh place, and one of the most important aspects of survival is being able to obtain food. Most food by itself yields little nutritional value, and all of it rots in time."
		""
		"Begin by obtaining any form of food."
	]
	quest.5292CA411DA7DB85.quest_subtitle: "Where's my easy food?"
	quest.5292CA411DA7DB85.title: "Hungry?"
	quest.52B7C682C9AA9316.quest_desc: [
		"Struggling to keep up with all the recipes and items you need? Here's a couple of options which may help:"
		""
		"&3Clipboard&r: a portable to-do list, letting you check off items as you like."
		""
		"&3Crafting Blueprint&r: hang it on a wall and set a recipe on it, then craft that recipe straight from your inventory without looking it up in EMI."
		""
		"&3EMI favourites&r: press A while hovering over an item in EMI to add it to your favourites. It works on recipe outputs too, to keep the whole recipe."
	]
	quest.52B7C682C9AA9316.quest_subtitle: "You're already in the first circle of microcrafting hell"
	quest.52B7C682C9AA9316.title: "Staying Organized"
	quest.52BA6ED6D4A7FD62.quest_desc: [
		"Here's what TFC's ores give in a Mercury bath:"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Gold&r: &dSilver&r"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Copper&r: &dGold&r"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Silver&r: &dGold&r"
		""
		"- &6Crushed Magnetite&r: &dGold&r"
	]
	quest.52BA6ED6D4A7FD62.quest_subtitle: "Liquid metal bath time"
	quest.52BA6ED6D4A7FD62.title: "Mercury bathing examples"
	quest.52C5AC88BEFEC5D4.quest_desc: [
		"Is your chest monster starting to grow out of control? Create's logistics can help: a &3Packager&r boxes up items from an inventory, belts, chain conveyors and frogports carry the packages, and stock links let you order from your whole storage at once."
		""
		"Factory Logistics does the same for fluids, in jars. Hold W over any of these items for Create's Ponder scenes."
	]
	quest.52C5AC88BEFEC5D4.quest_subtitle: "\"We have AE2 at home\""
	quest.52C5AC88BEFEC5D4.title: "Create Logistics"
	quest.52FC4E64963DC8F0.quest_desc: [
		"Clay is an essential part of stone age tech! Similar to knapping rocks, clay can be molded into different shapes and then fired in a Pit Kiln to create a wide variety of items. Stone Tools and Clay Ceramics will be the backbone of your survival until you learn how to work with Metals."
		""
		"Clay is found in patches in the ground, usually covered by grass, in areas with at least 175 mm of annual rainfall. Certain plants, known as \"Clay Indicators\" (athyrium fern, canna, goldenrod, pampas grass, perovskia and water canna), grow right on top of it. Smaller deposits sit close to rivers, lakes and ponds."
	]
	quest.52FC4E64963DC8F0.quest_subtitle: "You'll need a lot of this"
	quest.52FC4E64963DC8F0.title: "Clay Sources"
	quest.5384CC9235FF3876.quest_desc: [
		"&3Kanthal Heating Coils&r are the next major step in progression. They increase the temperature of your &3Blast Furnace&r to &d2,700K&r, allowing you to process new materials. They may also &eaccelerate&r less hot recipes; check the &aGregTech Power&r chapter for how Blast Furnace overclocks work."
		""
		"Remember that you &ccannot&r mix coils in an EBF."
	]
	quest.5384CC9235FF3876.quest_subtitle: "Is it getting hot in here?"
	quest.5384CC9235FF3876.title: "Kanthal Coils"
	quest.53C2EC535971A36B.quest_desc: [
		"Your third coil alloy is here and it's essential for your next set of coils in the &6EBF&r."
		""
		"As usual you will need &9128 ingots&r for 16 coils, but this time the ingots come out hot and, unlike Kanthal, they can't be cooled in a &6Chemical Bath&r. Instead, you're required to use a &6Vacuum Freezer&r."
		""
		"Good news: it's actually simpler and faster."
		""
		"The EBF recipe runs at &5EV&r voltage, so give your EBF two &6HV&r Energy Hatches."
		""
		"You'll only be using &6Nichrome&r for these coils, but don't get too comfortable - it will return later for the next set of &5RTM Coils&r."
	]
	quest.53C2EC535971A36B.quest_subtitle: "It doesn't have much use"
	quest.53C2EC535971A36B.title: "Nichrome Ingots"
	quest.53FBD2DECB32F26A.quest_desc: [
		"&dPotin Fluid Pipes&r carry plenty of fluid for an early pipe (check the tooltip for the numbers). You may want to look into making some of these to aid with fluid logistics."
		""
		"Potin is six copper, two tin and one lead: craft its &eDust&r form by hand, then smelt it. TFC has no lead ore; lead is a byproduct of silver, from washing crushed silver in the &3Ore Washer&r or centrifuging impure silver dust."
		""
		"This quest calls for any size of potin pipe."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o &dPotin Fluid Pipes&r were originally created in &9GT++&r, and were a huge power spike for players in a little pack called &4GT:NH&r."
		""
		"In the real world, &dPotin&r is an alloy used in coins, not pipes. GTCEu just gets more unrealistic by the day..."
	]
	quest.53FBD2DECB32F26A.quest_subtitle: "...I'm going into battle, and I need only your finest Potin."
	quest.53FBD2DECB32F26A.title: "Potin Seller..."
	quest.5411253EA7898A26.quest_desc: [
		"Stack logs in a pit, cover them and light them: a charcoal pit. Charcoal is hot enough for a forge, the bloomery and the blast furnace, and you'll need a lot of it."
		""
		"Sneak and right-click with logs to place log piles in your pit; the more logs in the piles, the more charcoal. Cover them with non-flammable blocks, leaving one pile open, light it with a firestarter or a torch, then cover it too. Once the smoke stops, dig out the charcoal piles, preferably with a shovel."
		""
		"Later, with wrought iron plates, GregTech's coke oven turns logs into charcoal (plus creosote) and coal into coke."
	]
	quest.5411253EA7898A26.quest_subtitle: "Fuel that burns hot"
	quest.5411253EA7898A26.title: "Charcoal"
	quest.54277F0D544DEF06.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Steam Compressor&r can turn ingots and gems into blocks, nuggets into ingots, and most importantly, wood pulp into single Planks. You'll see why those are important soon!"
	]
	quest.54277F0D544DEF06.quest_subtitle: "The Steam Compressor compresses..."
	quest.54277F0D544DEF06.title: "Steam Compressor"
	quest.542F4F6916343D21.quest_desc: [
		"Alloy copper (88-92%) with zinc from sphalerite (8-12%). Brass is Create's precision metal and the airship metal."
	]
	quest.542F4F6916343D21.quest_subtitle: "Copper and zinc"
	quest.542F4F6916343D21.title: "Brass"
	quest.5433DE98285A4854.quest_desc: [
		"The &dToolbox&r has 8 inventory slots which can each hold 4 stacks of items. Additionally, you can use a &ckeybind&r to access your placed &dToolbox&r from a few blocks away. You can even &bdye&r your &dToolbox&r to personalize it!"
	]
	quest.5433DE98285A4854.quest_subtitle: "A builders dream"
	quest.5433DE98285A4854.title: "Toolboxes"
	quest.5458EEC6D129ED86.quest_desc: [
		"Manganese is used in &6HV&r+ to make stainless steel, and in manganese phosphide, the &7LV&r superconductor."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here. Manganese can be obtained in &bMV&r by electrolyzing tantalite (centrifuged from lava) or spessartine (centrifuged from red garnet, a byproduct of TFC ruby)."
	]
	quest.5458EEC6D129ED86.quest_subtitle: "Element #25"
	quest.5458EEC6D129ED86.title: "Manganese"
	quest.54A73DD3BD21D343.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Assembler&r is the next step in progression. It makes the &aSMD components&r, &aNichrome Heating Coils&r and the &6HV&r Energy Hatch, among other things - check around this quest for more."
	]
	quest.54A73DD3BD21D343.title: "HV Assembler"
	quest.54E75E6C6CD49CE1.quest_desc: [
		"Use both of your new machines to turn a material into a Fluid, and solidify it back into a Rotor! That's &6four Ingots per Rotor&r, with no plates, ring or screw to make first."
		""
		"You can do the same for &6Gears&r and &6Small Gears&r with their casting molds."
		""
		"&9Note:&r Some metals require higher voltages than &7LV&r for Fluid Extraction, so make sure to keep an eye on the recipe tier in EMI."
	]
	quest.54E75E6C6CD49CE1.quest_subtitle: "Time to end the misery of hand crafting rotors!"
	quest.54E75E6C6CD49CE1.title: "Combo!"
	quest.5508395B2D635717.quest_desc: [
		"This kind soul will mine ores for you when placed above an ore vein, TFC's included."
		""
		"Vertical range is unlimited below the miner. Horizontal range is displayed in the tooltip."
		""
		"Higher tiers cover a wider area, so the &6HV&r variant reaches much more of a big vein; you may wish to hold off for now. Get &eany&r of them to complete this Quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You will need &9Power&r. &aCharged Batteries&r may work, but they tend to run out of power, which is a bit inconvenient."
		""
		"Our top suggestion is to use a filled &3Drum&r of some kind of fuel &7(if you're using Steam, no dice!)&r and a &3Generator&r."
		""
		"Place the Drum above your Generator and right-click it with a &5Soft Mallet&r or &5Screwdriver&r to auto-output into the Generator."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cNote:&r Do not forget to keep the area &dchunk-loaded&r while the miner works: a chunk loader from &3Create: Power Loader&r does the job."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r Use a &3GT Crate&r as the output inventory to make carrying the ores back home a simple task."
	]
	quest.5508395B2D635717.quest_subtitle: "So are you bored of mining yourself?"
	quest.5508395B2D635717.title: "Automatic Mining"
	quest.5556D43BFD90C796.quest_desc: [
		"At &6HV&r the single-block generators get their last upgrade: the HV Steam Turbine, Combustion Generator and Gas Turbine."
		""
		"There are no &5EV&r versions; past &6HV&r, power comes from the large turbines."
		""
		"Still, they remain strong choices for energy generation at the &6HV&r tier."
	]
	quest.5556D43BFD90C796.quest_subtitle: "Third time's the charm?"
	quest.5556D43BFD90C796.title: "The last single block generators"
	quest.55B9E873A37B07AC.quest_desc: [
		"Fire clay bricks, fired and set with mortar. GregTech's steam machines use them where they wanted a vanilla furnace."
		""
		"Knap fire clay into unfired fire bricks and fire them at 1399 °C (a pit kiln, or a forge with bellows), then craft the bricks with mortar into fire bricks blocks. TFC's blast furnace takes them too, as reinforced fire bricks: a fire bricks block and a wrought iron sheet."
	]
	quest.55B9E873A37B07AC.quest_subtitle: "Fireboxes"
	quest.55B9E873A37B07AC.title: "Fire Bricks"
	quest.55D2BB22B5852DF6.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Sifter&r should be used for all your &aGems&r: TFC's ruby, sapphire, emerald, topaz, opal, amethyst and diamond. Sifting a purified gem ore gives more gems than any other method, and it's the easiest way to get Exquisite and Flawless gems."
	]
	quest.55D2BB22B5852DF6.quest_subtitle: "The Skyblock Simulator"
	quest.55D2BB22B5852DF6.title: "The Sifter"
	quest.55EE9925E60E0986.quest_desc: [
		"Refines TFC pig iron with charcoal, coal or coke into steel, faster than working it on the anvil. It takes pig iron only."
	]
	quest.55EE9925E60E0986.quest_subtitle: "Faster steel"
	quest.55EE9925E60E0986.title: "Primitive Blast Furnace"
	quest.5647CFCF82DC5C51.title: "Primitive Metallurgy"
	quest.5689009E1F0B38BB.quest_desc: [
		"Put your previously made &aBiomass&r into a &3MV Distillery&r to make &aEthanol&r."
		""
		"You will need this for &dEthylene&r by reacting it with &aSulfuric Acid&r in a &3MV Chemical Reactor&r... unless you chose to go down the Oil path."
		""
		"Once you have a hefty starting stock of Ethanol, consider making and distilling &9Fermented Biomass&r in a &3Distillation Tower&r (when you get there!) for extra chemicals."
		""
		"&cDo not try&r to use Ethanol as a Power source... it's quite possibly its worst use. If it's organic &9Power&r that you want, we suggest taking a look at &dBenzene&r instead!"
	]
	quest.5689009E1F0B38BB.quest_subtitle: "Yo, wait - that's alcohol!"
	quest.5689009E1F0B38BB.title: "Ethanol"
	quest.5695B1A09E36E60F.quest_desc: [
		"Tungsten makes tungstensteel, the material of &9IV&r machines, and tungsten carbide."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &5EV&r: TFC &aCassiterite&r gives &aScheelite&r as its &3Thermal Centrifuge&r by-product. An &5EV&r &3Chemical Bath&r turns scheelite and hydrochloric acid into tungstic acid, and an &5EV&r &3Electrolyzer&r splits that into tungsten."
	]
	quest.5695B1A09E36E60F.quest_subtitle: "Element #74"
	quest.5695B1A09E36E60F.title: "Tungsten"
	quest.56B7D5F41BC74321.quest_desc: [
		"GregTech can make Ender Pearls from scratch."
		""
		"Mix &2Beryllium Dust&r, &2Potassium Dust&r and &bNitrogen&r in an &6HV&r Mixer to create &5Ender Pearl Dust&r, then throw it into an &7Implosion Compressor&r to recreate the iconic Ender Pearl - GregTech style."
		""
		"Beryllium comes from electrolyzing Emerald dust, Potassium from electrolyzing Rock Salt (TFC's Sylvite) or Saltpeter."
	]
	quest.56B7D5F41BC74321.quest_subtitle: "Sci-fi gemstones, or something"
	quest.56B7D5F41BC74321.title: "Ender Pearls"
	quest.56D1A7BA6216C70A.quest_desc: [
		"Get ready to make some explosives, as they will be required for the &cImplosion Compressor&r. Four kinds work: Powderbarrels, &cTNT&r, &dIndustrial TNT&r and Dynamite. One Industrial TNT does the work of four TNT, so we advise you to work towards it whenever you can."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cTNT&r (Trinitrotoluene) can't be prepared with the usual Gunpowder and Sand anymore. Instead, you'll have to produce &aGelled Toluene&r and react it with Sulfuric Acid to make TNT."
		""
		"Using the &3HV Chemical Reactor&r recipe (Toluene, Sugar and Polyethylene dust) will double the yield of &aGelled Toluene&r compared to the Fluid Solidifier."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"We don't have any easy tips to give you for &aToluene&r. It's going to be tricky no matter which route you take."
		""
		"That being said, don't miss out on the direct &aHeavy Fuel&r and &aWood Tar&r to &aToluene&r recipes in the single block &3Distillery&r. Wood Tar comes from logs in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r."
		""
		"&aToluene&r can also optionally be used in &5EV&r to make &dGasoline&r."
		""
		"&cTNT&r is used in the &3Implosion Compressor&r to make Gems. It also blows stuff up."
	]
	quest.56D1A7BA6216C70A.title: "TNT"
	quest.5770630C59A82777.quest_desc: [
		"Aluminium is the base material of &bMV&r: its machine casings are aluminium plates. Smelt the dust in the electric blast furnace (1700 K, &bMV&r power)."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here. Aluminium can be obtained in &7LV&r by electrolyzing sapphire dust (from TFC sapphire) and as a byproduct of processing TFC sapphire and emerald, and in &bMV&r by electrolyzing ruby or clay dust."
	]
	quest.5770630C59A82777.quest_subtitle: "Element #13"
	quest.5770630C59A82777.title: "Aluminium"
	quest.57A510F4AE0283D4.quest_desc: [
		"You now have access to &6centralized, searchable storage&r!"
		""
		"A basic setup is straightforward: you only need a &eStock Ticker&r, a &eStock Link&r and a &ePackager&r, as well as somewhere to put everything, such as a large &9Vault&r."
		""
		"Hold &eW&r over any of them to Ponder how they work."
	]
	quest.57A510F4AE0283D4.quest_subtitle: "Waiter! Waiter! More Silty Loam Rooted Dirt, please!"
	quest.57A510F4AE0283D4.title: "Stock Ticker"
	quest.57DB11B86C2A2EB4.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, &4Red Steel&r takes Create's diving gear to its netherite tier: weld a Red Steel Helmet, Chestplate or Boots onto the matching copper piece to get the &4Netherite Diving Helmet&r, &4Backtank&r and &4Boots&r. They're much tougher than copper, and with air in the backtank the helmet lets you breathe even in &clava&r."
		""
		"Create only makes you immune to burning when &oall four&r armor slots are fire-resistant, and the leggings would have to be netherite, which needs the Nether. So treat lava as deadly all the same."
	]
	quest.57DB11B86C2A2EB4.quest_subtitle: "Almost lava-proof"
	quest.57DB11B86C2A2EB4.title: "Red Steel Diving Gear"
	quest.58196CCD395A207E.quest_desc: [
		"The &bMV&r Circuit for the Integrated Tier. Don't make a ton of these, and only use them to make your first HV Circuits, because you'll soon gain access to an even better MV circuit."
	]
	quest.58196CCD395A207E.quest_subtitle: "More... I demand more!"
	quest.58196CCD395A207E.title: "More MV Circuits"
	quest.585AAED73FE3C5DA.quest_desc: [
		"A Circuit Component that you can now make thanks to the &3MV Assembler&r and &3Polyethylene&r."
		""
		"If you want the cheapest recipe, &aNickel-Zinc Ferrite&r is the way to go."
	]
	quest.585AAED73FE3C5DA.quest_subtitle: "Z = jwL"
	quest.585AAED73FE3C5DA.title: "Inductors"
	quest.585E54567985032C.quest_desc: [
		"All of these fuels are used in &2Gas Turbines&r — ranked here from the least efficient to the best: natural gas, methane, refinery gas, LPG, benzene and nitrobenzene."
		""
		"Gas fuels hold less energy per mB than combustion fuels. That doesn't make them worse — you just need more millibuckets for the same output. Later, they can feed the &2Large Gas Turbine&r, a very powerful multiblock."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"At &7LV&r your gas is &eMethane&r: a Centrifuge gets 60 mB from every rubber log, along with sticky resin. The others come from oil processing at &bMV&r and later; check EMI for each one's chain."
	]
	quest.585E54567985032C.quest_subtitle: "Everyone's favorite"
	quest.585E54567985032C.title: "Gas Fuels"
	quest.58737E4CE402E036.quest_desc: [
		"Weld ingots into double ingots and shape them on a stone anvil. The anvil makes tools, sheets and most metal parts."
		""
		"From here you climb the anvil tiers: copper (I); bronze, bismuth bronze and black bronze (II); wrought iron (III); steel (IV); black steel (V); red and blue steel (VI). An anvil works metals of its own tier and welds metals one tier higher, so each new anvil opens new tools and parts."
	]
	quest.58737E4CE402E036.quest_subtitle: "Metalworking"
	quest.58737E4CE402E036.title: "Copper Anvil"
	quest.58990A6698E07973.quest_desc: [
		"This jetpack enables flight, and requires energy."
		""
		"Charge it like you would charge a Battery."
		""
		"Press &4H&r (default) to enable Hover Mode."
		""
		"&o&7(Yeah, yeah, a jetpack is supposed to work off propellants. Y'all are always here to nitpick.)&r"
	]
	quest.58990A6698E07973.quest_subtitle: "...still not quite there."
	quest.58990A6698E07973.title: "I Believe I Can Fly II"
	quest.58A4E185C690D07E.quest_desc: [
		"By itself, the Battery Buffer does nothing. However, if you place batteries inside its internal storage, it will act as a power buffer."
		""
		"The &3Battery Buffer&r handles &9two Amps in&r, and &9one Amp out&r, &dper Battery&r. The output side has the dot, and all other sides are used as inputs."
		""
		"&6It also charges electric tools placed inside it.&r"
		""
		"This is a must have if you don't have unlimited power at hand. Get &eany&r &7LV&r Battery Buffer to finish the quest. However, the 16 slots variant is likely overkill at this stage."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r Don't loop your lossy Cables back to your Battery Buffer! If you think about it, you'll just end up voiding energy."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o To be frank with you, the GTCE Battery Buffer was... mediocre. It's been reworked in GTCEu to provide a mix between GT5 and GTCE's functionality. Energy now splits evenly across all batteries!"
	]
	quest.58A4E185C690D07E.quest_subtitle: "Useful if you don't want to build tons of generators"
	quest.58A4E185C690D07E.title: "Battery Buffer"
	quest.598C71EB59EFF457.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to keep your foes away from you, javelins are the weapon for you. They are the earliest ranged weapons you will have available to you. They deal &9Piercing&r damage, which can help you against Zombies, but Skeletons shrug it off completely."
		""
		"For more information on &cDamage Types&r consult the &3Field Guide&r."
	]
	quest.598C71EB59EFF457.quest_subtitle: "Caveman's bow"
	quest.598C71EB59EFF457.title: "Javelins"
	quest.599D49582B9592CA.quest_desc: [
		"Do you have a huge pile of barrels as you try to store all that creosote?"
		""
		"Look no further than multiblock tanks: even the cheapest, wooden one holds far more than barrels, and there are bronze and steel versions for even more storage. Fill and drain them through the controller or a tank valve."
	]
	quest.599D49582B9592CA.quest_subtitle: "Huge amounts of fluid storage"
	quest.599D49582B9592CA.title: "Multiblock Tanks"
	quest.59A2A6FD8395E094.quest_desc: [
		"Thorium has little use in GregTech; it is here for the set."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here, but macerating deepslate has a small chance to give thorium dust. TFC worlds have no deepslate: compact four TFC loose slate rocks into deepslate with a mechanical press over a basin."
	]
	quest.59A2A6FD8395E094.quest_subtitle: "Element #90"
	quest.59A2A6FD8395E094.title: "Thorium"
	quest.59FBF1430046DF9E.quest_desc: [
		"Beryllium is used in &6HV&r to make ender pearl dust, together with potassium and nitrogen."
		""
		"It is a byproduct of processing TFC emerald: macerating or washing crushed emerald ore gives beryllium dust."
	]
	quest.59FBF1430046DF9E.quest_subtitle: "Element #4"
	quest.59FBF1430046DF9E.title: "Beryllium"
	quest.5A217517DE657179.quest_desc: [
		"&aEpoxy&r is the foundation for all future Circuit Boards in the game!"
		""
		"&9&lNote:&r This Quest is quite complicated, so tackle everything else before trying to make Epoxy. You'll need all the help you can get!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"There are several ways to obtain the ingredients for &aEpoxy&r."
		""
		"We will ignore recipes related to Glycerol, as they're never worth it."
		""
		"Try and use &3Large Chemical Reactors&r to shortcut recipes."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&dChlorine&r is only partially recycled, so you'll need a constant supply. Feeding it manually will be sufficient at first."
		""
		"Recipes involving &dSodium Hydroxide&r could be looped by electrolyzing the &9Salt Water&r co-product."
		""
		"Doing this will probably require you to make some Quadruple Pipes, Pump Covers and Fluid Filters."
		""
		"In general, closed loop setups are nice to prevent overproduction or overconsumption, but go for whatever's more fun for you."
	]
	quest.5A217517DE657179.quest_subtitle: "Artificial Resin"
	quest.5A217517DE657179.title: "Epoxy"
	quest.5AD56024436BEB5A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hazardous Materials Suit&r is the best way to protect yourself from &cany kind of harm&r. You’ll be able to craft it once you reach &bMV&r, and &ayou should definitely take the time to do so&r."
	]
	quest.5AD56024436BEB5A.quest_subtitle: "Jesse! JESSE!"
	quest.5AD56024436BEB5A.title: "Hazardous Materials Suit"
	quest.5AF74E64533D9213.quest_desc: [
		"&aSodium Persulfate&r can be used in &9Ore Processing&r in the &3Chemical Bath&r to get various bonus outputs you would not normally obtain. It's completely optional, but pretty rewarding."
		""
		"&lWait, stop! That's only a distraction&r - the real topic of this Quest is..."
		""
		"&aSodium Persulfate&r and &aIron III Chloride&r are used to make cheaper &9Good Circuit Boards&r, as they cut Silver usage by a factor of four. They also etch your &9Plastic Circuit Boards&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Making &aSodium Persulfate&r from Salt and &aSulfuric Acid&r yields &aHydrochloric Acid&r as a coproduct, which you can react with Iron Dust to make &aIron III Chloride&r. This should be the best approach right now, but the decision is entirely yours."
		""
		"Though if you are pumping &9Sea Water&r, Iron III Chloride is easy: its Chlorine and Hydrogen make plenty of Hydrochloric Acid."
	]
	quest.5AF74E64533D9213.quest_subtitle: "Let's etch some Copper off Circuit Boards!"
	quest.5AF74E64533D9213.title: "Sodium Persulfate / Iron III Chloride"
	quest.5B177F2400CD6242.quest_desc: [
		"Every GregTech boiler is built around a Create mechanical pump, so GregTech's steam age starts here."
		""
		"It also moves fluids, from tanks and source blocks into Create's or GregTech's pipes, which work differently. Create's pipes hold no fluid themselves, need a pump to move anything and reach 16 blocks from it; a wrench turns a pipe into a straight window pipe so parallel pipes don't join. GregTech's pipes have their own buffer, keep fluid moving without a pump once it's inside, and connect only where you open them with a wrench."
	]
	quest.5B177F2400CD6242.quest_subtitle: "The steam age needs it"
	quest.5B177F2400CD6242.title: "Mechanical Pump"
	quest.5B285FE05C376C82.quest_desc: [
		"You already know about the &dChemical Reactor&r from the &7LV Chapter&r—but here’s a refresher."
		""
		"At &bMV&r, you unlock &anew recipes&r and also gain the ability to &aoverclock your LV recipes&r. That means they can run &atwice as fast&r, but will consume &e4x the energy&r. It’s up to you to decide whether the trade-off is worth it."
		""
		"But that’s not the only reason to build the &bMV Chemical Reactor&r. If you’re taking the &dorganic chemistry path&r, you’ll need it to run the &dEthylene&r recipe, which uses &dSulfuric Acid&r and &dEthanol&r—this one requires &bMV power&r."
		""
		"In any case, it’s a solid machine, and not too expensive. Go ahead and build it when you have a bit of spare time."
	]
	quest.5B285FE05C376C82.quest_subtitle: "Stronger, better, faster"
	quest.5B285FE05C376C82.title: "Advanced Chemical Reactor"
	quest.5B3F3A59D257A974.quest_desc: [
		"Flux is an item that is primarily used in metal working to weld things together, and later in the blast furnace, leather making and glass."
		"Some rocks - Chalk, Dolomite, Limestone and Marble - can be turned into Flux, as can shells, scutes and barnacles: craft one with any hammer (even a stone one) for 2 flux, or grind it in a Quern."
	]
	quest.5B3F3A59D257A974.quest_subtitle: "It's basically metal glue"
	quest.5B3F3A59D257A974.title: "Fluxstones"
	quest.5C30AD6D9656C52C.quest_desc: [
		"Struggling with aquifers in your ore veins? Create's copper diving helmet, backtank and boots let you work underwater. A full backtank holds 900 air, fifteen minutes of breathing; place it and give it rotation to fill it."
		""
		"Later, red steel armour welded onto the copper pieces turns them into netherite diving gear."
	]
	quest.5C30AD6D9656C52C.quest_subtitle: "If mining wasn't dangerous enough"
	quest.5C30AD6D9656C52C.title: "Copper Diving Equipment"
	quest.5C62CC07BA64479E.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Distillation Tower&r splits crude oils and cracked fuels into all their fractions at once."
		""
		"You will want to set this up &lbefore&r moving to &1IV&r."
		""
		"Heavy Oil comes from logs in the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r, the other oils from bedrock fluid veins. Distill them into sulfuric fuels, clean those with Hydrogen, steam-crack the Light Fuel or Naphtha and distill the result again for &aBenzene&r, &aToluene&r, &aButene&r and &aButadiene&r."
	]
	quest.5C62CC07BA64479E.title: "True Oil Distillation"
	quest.5C79B0DF7CC7D6E7.quest_desc: [
		"&aPolytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE)&r is a &7Carbon&r-&bFluorine&r polymer. Similarly to PVC, PTFE can be used to increase the yield of Plastic Circuit Boards and other crafts. Presently, it is used to make the walls of &3Large Chemical Reactors&r."
		""
		"&3Chlorine&r is required in the process, which is fully recycled if you electrolyze the &aHydrochloric Acid&r waste."
		""
		"&bFluorine&r will also be used in the &aUranium&r and &7Naquadah&r refinement processes."
		""
		"&9Tip:&r From this point onwards, you should be solidifying Polymers as &dBar&r (Ingot) form, as they can easily be shaped to whichever form you will need using the &3Extruder&r."
	]
	quest.5C79B0DF7CC7D6E7.quest_subtitle: "A.K.A - Teflon"
	quest.5C79B0DF7CC7D6E7.title: "Polytetrafluoroethylene"
	quest.5CBC781ACF0A44E1.quest_desc: [
		"A wrench rotates Create blocks, and sneak + right-click picks them up (an axe or pickaxe still breaks them too). Create's wrench takes gold sheets and a cogwheel; any GregTech wrench completes this quest as well."
		""
		"The goggles let you see much more about your machines, such as how much stress they produce or use. They're optional for now, but will prove very useful later."
	]
	quest.5CBC781ACF0A44E1.quest_subtitle: "These may be useful"
	quest.5CBC781ACF0A44E1.title: "Tools of the Trade"
	quest.5CE73B7ADDB6F42B.quest_desc: [
		"Slits a GregTech plate into two single wires (copper, tin, red alloy, gold, ...), GregTech's wiremill rate without electricity."
		""
		"On a moving contraption it fells trees; facing up, it cuts blocks like a stonecutter."
	]
	quest.5CE73B7ADDB6F42B.quest_subtitle: "Wires"
	quest.5CE73B7ADDB6F42B.title: "Mechanical Saw"
	quest.5CFD1E92F6BFBA1F.quest_desc: [
		"All of these fuels are used in &6Combustion Generators&r — ranked here from the least efficient to the best."
		""
		"In this pack the first combustion fuels arrive at &bMV&r: ethanol and methanol, and &2Bio Diesel&r made from seed oil, either of them and a pinch of sodium hydroxide. At &6HV&r a mixer turns diesel or bio diesel plus a little tetranitromethane into &eCetane-Boosted Diesel&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aGasoline&r comes from oil: a large chemical reactor makes raw gasoline from naphtha, refinery gas, methanol and acetone, and an &6HV&r chemical reactor finishes it with toluene. &cHigh Octane Gasoline&r, twice as strong, needs an &5EV&r large chemical reactor."
		""
		"These oil fuels need a proper refinery, so distill your oils carefully: a Distillation Tower beats a row of single Distilleries."
	]
	quest.5CFD1E92F6BFBA1F.quest_subtitle: "The polluter's favourite"
	quest.5CFD1E92F6BFBA1F.title: "Liquid Fuel"
	quest.5D38663954C86E73.quest_desc: [
		"Alright... technically, obtaining &6HV&r Circuits and Stainless Steel lets you progress to &6HV&r - but let's not rush things."
		""
		"The first thing you should make with these is a &3MV Circuit Assembler&r to unlock the new tier of Circuits right away; cheaper recipes is the &dreal payoff&r here."
	]
	quest.5D38663954C86E73.quest_subtitle: "...but hold on before getting too giddy"
	quest.5D38663954C86E73.title: "First HV Circuits!"
	quest.5D52545E34E93B11.quest_desc: [
		"Lithium is the best electrolyte for &7LV&r, &bMV&r and &6HV&r batteries."
		""
		"GregTech's ore veins are off here, so lithium comes from clay: electrolyze clay dust (macerated clay) in an &bMV&r electrolyzer for lithium, sodium, aluminium and silicon."
	]
	quest.5D52545E34E93B11.quest_subtitle: "Element #3"
	quest.5D52545E34E93B11.title: "Lithium"
	quest.5D652DF7356DC4C5.quest_desc: [
		"The Quern and Handstone are two big rocks grinding against each other to break down materials. The bottom piece is called a Quern while the top piece is called a Handstone. The quern takes three smooth stone, which you make by chiseling raw rock, so it comes once you've cast a metal chisel."
		""
		"The Quern grinds Flux, Flour, Bone Meal, Salt, dyes and mineral powders such as sulfur and redstone. Don't grind your metal ores in it: here its ore powders don't melt, and crushed ore comes from Create's millstone and GregTech's macerator instead."
	]
	quest.5D652DF7356DC4C5.quest_subtitle: "Your first step into ore processing"
	quest.5D652DF7356DC4C5.title: "Quern and Handstone"
	quest.5DF6FAD9C5EDDE4D.quest_desc: [
		"Don't panic! We'll mostly be doing this to get hydrocarbons."
		""
		"There are many ways to acquire &dEthylene&r from Oil processing. It's easy to get lost in all the options and recipes!"
		""
		"The best way is to steam-crack &aNaphtha&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r. Be sure to make the &aSeverely Steam-Cracked&r version for a higher yield of Ethylene."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Once in &6HV&r, you'll have the option to do this recipe in the &3Cracking Unit&r at 100 percent efficiency. Unfortunately, the recipes you are doing with the Chemical Reactor have a loss of &450 percent&r."
		""
		"&9Note:&r All of this looks and feels terribly inefficient - we hope that's strong motivation to tier up! The &3Distillation Tower&r will be a huge upgrade for petrochem, but you're not quite there... yet. Right now, you'll have to use a &3Distillery&r to get &dEthylene&r."
	]
	quest.5DF6FAD9C5EDDE4D.quest_subtitle: "Fuel and oil cracking can get complicated..."
	quest.5DF6FAD9C5EDDE4D.title: "Fuel Cracking"
	quest.5E5F28E833B3C34D.quest_desc: [
		"Mechanical crafters build Create's oversized recipes: set out enough of them in the recipe's shape, give them rotation and put one ingredient in each."
		""
		"You'll want them for Create's &3Crushing Wheels&r, whose 5x5 recipe needs them. The wheels grind TFC ore at the macerator's rate."
	]
	quest.5E5F28E833B3C34D.quest_subtitle: "For those extra large crafting recipes"
	quest.5E5F28E833B3C34D.title: "Mechanical Crafter"
	quest.5EC4160C4B3475E3.quest_desc: [
		"&aBlue Alloy&r is an excellent Cable material for &6HV&r power."
		""
		"Nothing is preventing you from using it for &bMV&r power too! Make sure that you don't overvolt your machines, though."
		""
		"Superconductors for &6HV&r are unlocked... later."
		""
		"It's one part Silver to four parts &aElectrotine&r. Electrotine has no ore here: mix &dElectrum&r and &dRedstone&r dust in a Mixer. You'll also need Blue Alloy bolts for your first &5EV&r Circuits."
	]
	quest.5EC4160C4B3475E3.quest_subtitle: "You're blue now... that's my alloy"
	quest.5EC4160C4B3475E3.title: "Blue Alloy"
	quest.5EF922E23D7A9AEC.quest_desc: [
		"Chromium is used in &6HV&r+ to make stainless steel (the base material of &6HV&r) and in nichrome and kanthal for heating coils."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r as a byproduct of processing TFC ruby, or by electrolyzing ruby dust (&bMV&r). Smelt it in the electric blast furnace."
	]
	quest.5EF922E23D7A9AEC.quest_subtitle: "Element #24"
	quest.5EF922E23D7A9AEC.title: "Chromium"
	quest.5F01F1984B2EB701.quest_desc: [
		"The &aLow Power Integrated Circuit&r requires an &3HV Cutter&r inside your &3Cleanroom&r."
		""
		"&3HV Energy Hatches&r will be nice additions so you can run your Multiblocks (mainly your Electric Blast Furnace and Large Chemical Reactor) directly off a &6HV&r line."
	]
	quest.5F01F1984B2EB701.quest_subtitle: "Noticing a pattern here?"
	quest.5F01F1984B2EB701.title: "Upgrade your EBF II"
	quest.5F155C91B477A331.quest_desc: [
		"Well... got any Aluminium Ingots yet?"
		""
		"Each Electric Age has Circuits corresponding to its tier. The Good Electronic Circuit is the &dfirst MV Circuit&r you can make: a Phenolic Printed Circuit Board, Basic Electronic Circuits, Diodes and copper wire."
		""
		"Always be on the lookout for a cheaper way to make your circuits - new sets of recipes become available each time you make a new tier of &2Circuit Assembler&r. Conveniently, this circuit unlocks the first one."
		""
		"&6Having this and Aluminium will grant access to MV Machines.&r"
	]
	quest.5F155C91B477A331.quest_subtitle: "Does that mean we're at MV yet?"
	quest.5F155C91B477A331.title: "First MV Circuit!"
	quest.5F1FA7A3CE009FF5.quest_desc: [
		"&bSilicone Rubber&r is essentially an improved version of regular rubber. As you progress through &bGregTech&r, you will unlock better substitutes for older materials, and this is one of them."
		""
		"It coats your &eWires&r for half the cost of rubber and can replace rubber in parts like Conveyors and Pumps. From &5EV&r on, most cables can't be insulated with plain rubber at all."
		""
		"If you are struggling to get enough &fSticky Resin&r from rubber trees, this material will solve the issue, as it is made from &eSilicon&r, &aChlorine&r, &7Methane&r and a little Sulfur, resources you can easily produce endlessly at this stage."
	]
	quest.5F1FA7A3CE009FF5.quest_subtitle: "Silicon, silicon, silicon everywhere!"
	quest.5F1FA7A3CE009FF5.title: "Silicone Rubber"
	quest.5F2E970FD74F1633.quest_desc: [
		"Every propeller sits on brass casing. Spin it with any Create power on board."
	]
	quest.5F2E970FD74F1633.quest_subtitle: "Thrust"
	quest.5F2E970FD74F1633.title: "Propeller Bearing"
	quest.5F469997A004EEE0.quest_desc: [
		"You can right-click a Crate with Tape, which will then make the crate keep its contents when broken, making it easy to move around. This only works once per tape, however."
		""
		"Good thing it's cheap!"
	]
	quest.5F469997A004EEE0.quest_subtitle: "Moving stuff around"
	quest.5F469997A004EEE0.title: "Tape for Crates"
	quest.5F4E5DDB4D7DEC95.quest_desc: [
		"Each basic food contains nutrients, split into 5 categories: &lGrain&r, &lFruit&r, &lVegetables&r, &lProtein&r and &lDairy&r."
		""
		"While you could eat only one kind of nutrient such as Protein, your maximum health will suffer, while a balanced diet gives you much higher max health. Only recent meals count, so keep eating a variety; soups, salads and sandwiches combine several nutrients at once."
		""
		"Look at the field guide's \"Food and Water\" section for full details. The nutrition tab of your inventory shows your current levels."
	]
	quest.5F4E5DDB4D7DEC95.quest_subtitle: "What do you mean I can't just eat steak?"
	quest.5F4E5DDB4D7DEC95.title: "Mechanic: Nutrition"
	quest.5F5B259C099A2916.quest_desc: [
		"A modern suit of armor for the modern era! Like GregTech's power tools, every piece runs on charge."
		""
		"- The Helmet comes with built-in night vision goggles."
		""
		"- The Chestplate doesn't do a lot on its own, but can be upgraded to have a jetpack."
		""
		"- The Leggings round off the set."
		""
		"- The Boots completely protect you from fall damage and have a toggleable Step Assist mode."
	]
	quest.5F5B259C099A2916.quest_subtitle: "Nanomachines, son!"
	quest.5F5B259C099A2916.title: "NanoMuscle™ Suite"
	quest.5FB592A117BBCFA9.quest_desc: [
		"Build this machine next to your &3Chemical Reactor&r to automatically solidify Rubber into &aRubber Sheets&r."
		""
		"You can make your Chemical Reactor auto-output if you &dwrench&r the side of your &3Chemical Reactor&r and enable Fluid &9auto-output&r."
		""
		"There will be more Fluids to solidify, so you may re-purpose your &3Fluid Solidifier&r when not crafting Rubber - or make a second one!"
	]
	quest.5FB592A117BBCFA9.quest_subtitle: "The Fluid Solidifier solidifies..."
	quest.5FB592A117BBCFA9.title: "Basic Fluid Solidifier"
	quest.5FB5D9AB580D4799.quest_desc: [
		"&7By now, you should be getting used to the pattern: with every new Energy Tier comes a fresh batch of components.&r"
		""
		"The &5EV&r tier comes with a few twists - first, &eNeodymium&r: the Motors need Magnetic Neodymium rods, along with &eKanthal&r wire. If you've been diligently upgrading your EBF, Kanthal should be significantly faster to craft than when you first made it, and the Alloy Blast Smelter will be able to make it even faster."
		""
		"Secondly, Sensors and Emitters require &bQuantum Eyes&r - Ender Eyes bathed in Radon in the Chemical Bath - along with &ePlatinum&r rods."
	]
	quest.5FB5D9AB580D4799.quest_subtitle: "The \"Fun\" will never stop"
	quest.5FB5D9AB580D4799.title: "Extreme Voltage Components"
	quest.5FF149CEA2CAEBB6.quest_desc: [
		"Built from eight bronze double sheets, with charcoal and iron ore inside."
		""
		"Wrought iron comes only from the bloomery: anything iron that is smelted or melted (GregTech's furnaces, Create's fan, TFC heat) becomes cast iron."
		""
		"Set the bloomery in a chimney of stone blocks; a full chimney holds 48 items. Throw in iron ore (hematite, limonite, magnetite, or any iron item, even cast iron ingots) with charcoal: each bloom takes 100 mB of cast iron and two charcoal. Light it and wait 12 hours, then mine the bloom for raw iron blooms and work them on a bronze anvil into refined blooms and then wrought iron ingots. The field guide shows the build."
	]
	quest.5FF149CEA2CAEBB6.quest_subtitle: "The only way to wrought iron"
	quest.5FF149CEA2CAEBB6.title: "Bloomery"
	quest.5FFCA992614EAEE3.quest_desc: [
		"An &9Electron Tube&r is polished rose quartz on a wrought iron sheet. Rose quartz is nether quartz crafted with eight redstone; polish it with sand paper."
		""
		"Quartz comes from grinding TFC rock: a millstone finds a little in raw quartzite, crushing wheels more in diorite. A quern grinds TFC cinnabar or cryolite into redstone."
		""
		"Deployers and mechanical crafters are built with them."
	]
	quest.5FFCA992614EAEE3.quest_subtitle: "Ultra Ultra Low Voltage...?"
	quest.5FFCA992614EAEE3.title: "Electron Tube"
	quest.60422B9925594BA6.quest_desc: [
		"Distilling &aOil&r or &aRaw Oil&r gives you fuels that you need to desulfurize with &bHydrogen&r in a &3Chemical Reactor&r."
		""
		"The &aHydrogen Sulfide&r it leaves is perfectly &drecycled&r in an &3Electrolyzer&r, back into Hydrogen and Sulfur."
		""
		"To automate this process, simply place your &3Chemical Reactor&r and your &3Electrolyzer&r next to each other. Be sure to use your &5Screwdriver&r to &4enable input from the output side&r."
		""
		"&aNaphtha&r is a good &9Product&r source, and surprisingly it's also a decent fuel, but if you don't have Raw Oil then Light Oil Residue may be better. Keep following the quests for more details."
	]
	quest.60422B9925594BA6.quest_subtitle: "We're still confused on how Naphtha is pronounced"
	quest.60422B9925594BA6.title: "Naphtha or Light Oil Residue"
	quest.6055977436A34ECA.quest_desc: [
		"&bThis one should look familiar&r: you've seen it before."
		"&2We highly recommend crafting it as soon as possible,&r as it opens up many new sources of &7Aluminium&r."
		""
		"Until now, you were limited to electrolyzing Sapphire or ore processing byproducts to obtain &7Aluminium Dust&r."
		"The &bMV&r Electrolyzer runs the recipes that need more than &7LV&r power, and a whole new world of resources opens up."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6Here are some key materials to look for:&r"
		"&9Ruby&r: &7Aluminium&r and &5Chromium&r."
		"&9Clay Dust&r (macerated clay): &7Aluminium&r, &bSilicon&r, Sodium and Lithium."
		"&9Emerald&r: &7Aluminium&r, &bSilicon&r and Beryllium."
		"&9Garnets&r (centrifuged from the Red Garnet that Ruby processing gives): &7Aluminium&r, &bSilicon&r, and &2Manganese&r from Spessartine."
		"&9Sodalite&r and &9Lazurite&r (from processing Lapis): &7Aluminium&r, &bSilicon&r, Sodium and &3Chlorine&r."
		""
		"&2And that's just the beginning!&r Use &aEMI&r to explore even more options; we promise, there's a lot to discover."
	]
	quest.6055977436A34ECA.quest_subtitle: "We made it to MV, and, well..."
	quest.6055977436A34ECA.title: "MV Electrolyzer"
	quest.609AC80858CA0F39.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Item Magnet&r is exactly what you'd expect — a magnet that pulls nearby &6items&r straight to you. &aVery useful&r. What more could you ask for?"
	]
	quest.609AC80858CA0F39.quest_subtitle: "2010 called, it wants its juggalo meme back"
	quest.609AC80858CA0F39.title: "Item Magnets"
	quest.60DDE4DD9AA992CA.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSMD&r (surface-mount device) &aComponents&r are CEu-exclusive components that are required for the next tier of circuits (&5Nano&r). They can also be used in place of their non-SMD counterparts in most Circuit recipes."
		""
		"Of course they're more complicated to make, this is GregTech! What did you expect?"
		""
		"Invest in automation for these - you won't stop needing them."
	]
	quest.60DDE4DD9AA992CA.quest_subtitle: "Alternate components!"
	quest.60DDE4DD9AA992CA.title: "SMD Components"
	quest.60E2DB6C3FFBF19B.quest_desc: [
		"Less common as a component, but used in a number of critical machines."
		""
		"When placed on a machine, conveyor modules will transfer items. You can configure them to import or export."
		""
		"They can also accept various &9Item Filters&r."
	]
	quest.60E2DB6C3FFBF19B.quest_subtitle: "A crafting component, but also a cover!"
	quest.60E2DB6C3FFBF19B.title: "LV Conveyor Module"
	quest.615C6D742F443F43.quest_desc: [
		"&aTitanium&r has the highest corrosion resistance and strength-to-density ratio of any metallic element, so it's only natural that we'll be using it as the main material in our &5EV&r machinery."
		""
		"Confirm that your closed loop for &aRutile&r is up to standard, and prepare to run a dedicated &3EBF&r for hours."
		""
		"A quick aside - now that we're heading to &5EV&r, single block generators are about to fall out of style! They stop at &6HV&r, so you'll need to run several &3HV Generators&r to keep up - later, upgrades to Multiblock Generators will be required."
		""
		"While Multiblock generators are much more expensive, you'll find them to be much more energy efficient! Have a look at the power chapter for more info!"
	]
	quest.615C6D742F443F43.title: "Titanium"
	quest.616329CB5D11DA43.quest_desc: [
		"Along riverbeds and lakebeds, you may notice gravel with specks of minerals, known as &aOre Deposits&r. Use a &bPan&r (knapped from clay and fired) on one, then stand in water and hold right-click to pan it. With luck you'll get &dsmall pieces of ore&r (native copper, native silver, native gold or cassiterite), sometimes a loose rock or even a gem. These can come in a pinch when you're missing a few millibuckets to fill a mold."
	]
	quest.616329CB5D11DA43.quest_subtitle: "Re-experience the gold rush!"
	quest.616329CB5D11DA43.title: "Panning"
	quest.6176A1497306A32B.quest_desc: [
		"This Quest requires the &3Pyrolyse Oven&r and is &doptional&r, yet convenient."
		""
		"These four fluids are the important products of &aWood Tar&r Distillation:"
		""
		"&9-&r Phenol: useful for Epoxy and PBI"
		"&9-&r Benzene: an important hydrocarbon"
		"&9-&r Toluene: useful for TNT"
		"&9-&r Dimethylbenzene: useful for PBI"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"These three are the important products from &aWood Vinegar&r Distillation:"
		""
		"&9-&r Acetic Acid: useful to make more Acetone"
		""
		"&9-&r Methanol: a moderately important hydrocarbon"
		""
		"&9-&r Acetone: useful for Epoxy and Gasoline"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"It's also possible to use a \"full combo\" of 4 &3DTs&r - input &aCharcoal Byproducts&r into a first tower, splitting into &aWood Tar&r, &aWood Gas&r and &aWood Vinegar&r."
		""
		"This isn't the most efficient cost-to-production ratio, but the option is there if you get bored."
	]
	quest.6176A1497306A32B.title: "True Organic Distillation"
	quest.619EF631682EDD43.quest_desc: [
		"The first mold you should make out of clay is the Saw Mold. With it and some small amount of metal you can create a Saw. The Saw is an important tool, as it's required to create &lLumber&r, and with it, you'll be able to create your first &l&oWorkbench.&r"
	]
	quest.619EF631682EDD43.quest_subtitle: "Time for your first metal tool"
	quest.619EF631682EDD43.title: "Saw Mold"
	quest.61EE59B4042883AD.quest_desc: [
		"The &dNano CPU Wafer&r is your gateway to Nano Circuits and your second kind of &1IV&r Circuit."
		""
		"Coat a CPU Wafer with molten Glowstone and Raw Carbon Fibers (Carbon dust and Epoxy in an Autoclave) in an &5EV&r Chemical Reactor inside your Cleanroom, then cut it into chips in an &6HV&r Cutter."
		""
		"You'll need a huge amount of these circuits, so automate the line early."
	]
	quest.61EE59B4042883AD.quest_subtitle: "That sounds like marketing"
	quest.61EE59B4042883AD.title: "That sounds like marketing"
	quest.627BF49FE6F099D7.quest_desc: [
		"The Mixer is the GregTech way of alloying: &amix dusts together&r, then smelt them into ingots or melt them into fluids. Any new alloy goes through it, and the old ones can too."
		""
		"It also &6speeds up&r TFC's colored steels: &aBlack Steel&r, &aRed Steel&r and &aBlue Steel&r dust come straight out of it, ready for the EBF. Even if you don't think you need it now, you'll find it &6essential&r later on."
	]
	quest.627BF49FE6F099D7.quest_subtitle: "The Mixer mixes..."
	quest.627BF49FE6F099D7.title: "Basic Mixer"
	quest.62A2893E91B1A49C.quest_desc: [
		"Magnesium is used in &6HV&r to make magnesium diboride, the &bMV&r superconductor, and to reduce titanium tetrachloride to titanium in the electric blast furnace. It also makes magnalium with aluminium."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r as a byproduct of TFC hematite (macerating refined hematite ore) and by electrolyzing magnesia, which centrifuging lava (&bMV&r) gives."
	]
	quest.62A2893E91B1A49C.quest_subtitle: "Element #12"
	quest.62A2893E91B1A49C.title: "Magnesium"
	quest.62D6AFA96EA9FC6F.quest_desc: [
		"Another tier, another energy hatch. You know what to do with this!"
	]
	quest.62D6AFA96EA9FC6F.title: "Q56597d7db5891d31"
	quest.6331043E37C30F01.quest_desc: [
		"Using a Ruby Lens, engrave a Silicon Wafer into an ILC Wafer."
		""
		"This can be processed in a Cutter for Integrated Circuit Chips, which are important components for improving upon your circuit crafting capabilities."
	]
	quest.6331043E37C30F01.quest_subtitle: "I C U"
	quest.6331043E37C30F01.title: "IC Chips"
	quest.63833F5CEF1EE62B.quest_desc: [
		"There's many minerals that can be electrolyzed into aluminium, but most of them are off-limits until &bMV&r. TFC's gems are the exception: electrolyze &aSapphire&r dust in an &7LV&r Electrolyzer, or blast &aRuby&r straight into aluminium nuggets in the EBF. Several ore processing chains also give aluminium dust as a byproduct. TFC's field guide tells you where to find sapphire and ruby."
		""
		"Once you have enough aluminium, we recommend making the Electrolyzer your first &bMV&r machine to unlock all the other options."
	]
	quest.63833F5CEF1EE62B.quest_subtitle: "Time for an adventure"
	quest.63833F5CEF1EE62B.title: "Aluminium Dust"
	quest.63C744822BF87E37.quest_desc: [
		"Hm... didn't we make this joke already?"
		""
		"The &3Basic Extractor&r is your go-to machine for turning solids into liquids. Use it to melt Rubber that you previously solidified, to &dmelt Soldering Alloy&r for your circuits, and to &dmelt Red Alloy&r for the &6best Vacuum Tube recipe&r in the &3Assembler&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Did you notice this machine doubles as both an Extractor and a Fluid Extractor? The two of them were separate machines in previous versions of GregTech."
	]
	quest.63C744822BF87E37.quest_subtitle: "The Extractor extracts..."
	quest.63C744822BF87E37.title: "Basic Liquid Extraction"
	quest.63D06D8B5F321096.quest_desc: [
		"This is a guide on how to automatically route &lall&r your Hot Ingots to a cooler, while keeping everything automated in tip-top shape."
		""
		"The &3Vacuum Freezer&r cools every hot ingot. The &3Chemical Bath&r only cools a few here: &ekanthal&r, &esilicon&r and the &eblack, red and blue steels&r. Everything else needs the freezer."
		""
		"The cheap way would be to use filters, and manually add Hot Ingots one by one... which is so boring! Let's try the fun option."
		""
		"Install an &aItem Tag Filter&r Cover on the side of your &3Vacuum Freezer&r's input bus, open it and set it to &e&l*hot_ingots*&r."
		""
		"From here, you can route with &9any logistics system&r of your choice."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Connect the output of your &3EBF(s)&r to the input of your cooler and to an output dump (Chest or Crate). You can also put a &dRestrictive Pipe&r in front of the output dump so the cooler gets priority."
		""
		"&l&9Note:&r If you wish to know more tags for more automation setups, they will display if you press Shift when hovering over an item. For instance, an item tagged with &e&o#c:plates/copper&r is matched by &e&lc:plates/copper&r, or by a wildcard such as &e&l*plates/copper&r."
		""
		"&9&lOther Note:&r The Item Tag Filter accepts whole expressions: AND, OR and NOT, wildcards and grouping. Hover over the info icon for the syntax."
	]
	quest.63D06D8B5F321096.quest_subtitle: "Stop burning your hands!"
	quest.63D06D8B5F321096.title: "250IQ"
	quest.6407C2830BDE4BDC.quest_desc: [
		"This column shows what you can do with your purified dust."
	]
	quest.6407C2830BDE4BDC.title: "Purified Dust"
	quest.647BCE4EB43D841B.quest_desc: [
		"These are just some of the basic meals you can create. Soups, salads, and sandwiches are your go-tos for easy high saturation combined meals."
	]
	quest.647BCE4EB43D841B.quest_subtitle: "GET IN MAH BELLEH!"
	quest.647BCE4EB43D841B.title: "Meals"
	quest.649ED67652030623.quest_desc: [
		"Carbon is the base of organic chemistry. It is used in &7LV&r+ to make resistors and later carbon fibres."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r by centrifuging coal dust (from TFC bituminous coal or lignite) or rubber logs, or by electrolyzing coke dust."
	]
	quest.649ED67652030623.quest_subtitle: "Element #6"
	quest.649ED67652030623.title: "Carbon"
	quest.64BC39133D40186E.quest_desc: [
		"&aGasoline&r is a really strong combustion fuel that you can make at &6HV&r. A Large Chemical Reactor turns naphtha, refinery gas, methanol and acetone into raw gasoline, and a Chemical Reactor finishes it with &7Toluene&r, distilled from wood tar or heavy oil residue."
		""
		"It's strong, and even better, it can be upgraded into &cHigh Octane Gasoline&r."
	]
	quest.64BC39133D40186E.quest_subtitle: "The middle child"
	quest.64BC39133D40186E.title: "Gasoline"
	quest.64C18F9BF387363D.quest_desc: [
		"Bronze plates, TFC fire bricks and a Create mechanical pump. It burns logs or charcoal. Every steam machine runs on boiler steam, and later the steam turbine turns it into electricity."
		""
		"There are three kinds, all built around a mechanical pump: the &3Solid&r boiler burns solid fuels like coal and charcoal, the &3Liquid&r boiler burns lava or creosote, and the &3Solar&r boiler needs no fuel but only works during the day. If you're unsure, start with the solid one."
		""
		"Steam machines all have a vent which needs to stay unblocked in order for them to work properly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&aWarning:&r Boilers will &bexplode&r if you put water into them while they are dry and hot. It's best to always have water being piped into them, but you can always break and place the block to reset its temperature."
	]
	quest.64C18F9BF387363D.quest_subtitle: "GregTech begins"
	quest.64C18F9BF387363D.title: "Steam Boiler"
	quest.64C485F99244C9F3.quest_desc: [
		"&lOutside of Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Similar to the Centrifuge, this machine does a lot of things - we can't hope to list them all! Fortunately, it's one of the cheapest &7LV&r machines, so grab it as soon as it becomes necessary."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&lFor Ore Processing:&r"
		""
		"Okay, we lied. It's not &oexactly&r used for Ore Processing, it's actually used in the &adecomposition of Dusts&r. However, most of the useful electrolysis recipes are locked at &bMV&r. You can peep at the &emolecular formula&r in a dust's tooltip to see what you can get from electrolysis."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cTake caution!&r Due to how ores work, directly smelting dusts into Ingots can give higher metal yields than electrolysis. However, it means you lose the other products in the dust. You will have to decide whether you want to prioritise direct value, or byproduct count."
	]
	quest.64C485F99244C9F3.quest_subtitle: "It goes bzzz"
	quest.64C485F99244C9F3.title: "Basic Electrolyzer"
	quest.651526D0BA6DA1D1.quest_desc: [
		"You may have noticed that different fuels burn at different temperatures: a fuel's tooltip tells you. Charcoal and lignite burn at 1350 °C and bituminous coal at 1415 °C, well above the melting points of bronze (950 °C) and copper (1080 °C), so keep an eye on your ingots' temperature and take them out once they can be worked or welded."
		""
		"&9Note&r: putting a mold or vessel on the right side of the forge interface will catch any metals that melt."
	]
	quest.651526D0BA6DA1D1.quest_subtitle: "There's more than charcoal!"
	quest.651526D0BA6DA1D1.title: "Fuel Temperatures"
	quest.6534554896BC70F8.quest_desc: [
		"This row is for the very basics of ore processing: Create's millstone and crushing wheels, a hammer in the crafting grid and a cauldron of water. There are no byproducts yet, though Create can already automate the crushing."
		""
		"The millstone gives TFC's own yield; crushing wheels and the macerator give twice that."
	]
	quest.6534554896BC70F8.quest_subtitle: "Before electricity"
	quest.6534554896BC70F8.title: "Early Ore Processing"
	quest.6541E6B876BB04BF.quest_desc: [
		"While javelins are cool, it's hard to beat a bow and arrow. Arrows can be expensive, so setting up a bird farm for feathers isn't a bad idea."
		""
		"Arrows deal &9Piercing&r damage: good against Zombies, useless against Skeletons, which are immune to it."
	]
	quest.6541E6B876BB04BF.quest_subtitle: "Then I took an arrow to the knee..."
	quest.6541E6B876BB04BF.title: "Bow and Arrow"
	quest.65465894A2D8E709.quest_desc: [
		"Titanium requires a slightly more &binvolved&r process than the previous materials. To get started, you'll need &aRutile&r. An &3EBF&r reduces &aIlmenite&r dust with Carbon to Rutile."
		""
		"Ilmenite comes from TFC &aMagnetite&r: run crushed magnetite through a &3Thermal Centrifuge&r, or centrifuge pure magnetite dust, and ilmenite is the &6Byproduct&r."
		""
		"Once you've gotten enough &5Rutile&r, your journey to &6Titanium&r continues in the next quest. There's no need to rush things."
	]
	quest.65465894A2D8E709.quest_subtitle: "...means it WASN'T Titanium!"
	quest.65465894A2D8E709.title: "Almost Titanium"
	quest.657AC34B43F73635.quest_desc: [
		"Three iron plates and a hammer make a vanilla bucket. In this pack iron plates are wrought iron: hammer them by hand (two ingots per plate) or press them one for one in Create's mechanical press."
		""
		"TFC's buckets can't do what this one does: the wooden bucket can't carry lava, and neither it nor the red and blue steel buckets can place source blocks. The vanilla bucket does both, which makes it the way to set up lava for Create's encased fan."
	]
	quest.657AC34B43F73635.quest_subtitle: "Dear God..."
	quest.657AC34B43F73635.title: "This... is a Bucket."
	quest.6591AEB03FC400FF.quest_desc: [
		"Lenses are turned on a &3Lathe&r from an &bExquisite&r gem; an &bMV&r Lathe can also turn a gem plate into one. Exquisite gems come from sifting purified gem ores, so a &aSifter&r is your friend here."
		""
		"Each colour of lens engraves a different wafer: &cRuby&r for ILC, &aEmerald&r for RAM, &9Sapphire&r for ULPIC and &bDiamond&r for CPU."
	]
	quest.6591AEB03FC400FF.quest_subtitle: "So sparkly!"
	quest.6591AEB03FC400FF.title: "Optical Lenses"
	quest.65E8217B302CD07C.quest_desc: [
		"Water is an important resource, not just for staying hydrated! Setting up a base near a fresh lake or river is recommended, so you have easy access to the stuff. Other items can quench your thirst, such as certain types of food or drinks."
		""
		"Water won't always be available when you go exploring, however, so here are some ways to carry drinks around with you. Drinking consumes 100mB from the container."
	]
	quest.65E8217B302CD07C.quest_subtitle: "Yet another bar to keep full..."
	quest.65E8217B302CD07C.title: "Mechanic: Hydration"
	quest.66380B5C035A2419.quest_desc: [
		"Crafting Vacuum Tubes might make you question your existence: a glass tube, two steel bolts and three copper wires each. They're very expensive right now, but they'll get cheaper in a moment - that's the general GregTech philosophy! The assembler makes two to four at a time."
		""
		"Vacuum Tubes are also technically your first Ultra Low Voltage (&8ULV&r) Circuit! Congratulations! From here you can jump right into crafting LV Circuits."
	]
	quest.66380B5C035A2419.quest_subtitle: "The harder component for circuits"
	quest.66380B5C035A2419.title: "Electronics #3: Vacuum Tubes"
	quest.66C581A8872245B1.quest_desc: [
		"Sodium is a subpar &7LV&r to &6HV&r battery electrolyte, and with potassium it makes sodium-potassium, which &6HV&r+ energy hatches are made with."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r by electrolyzing salt dust, which comes from processing TFC halite ore."
	]
	quest.66C581A8872245B1.quest_subtitle: "Element #11"
	quest.66C581A8872245B1.title: "Sodium"
	quest.67328B8754357E78.quest_desc: [
		"Regular &o&dGregTech&r Fluid Pipes can only transport one fluid type at a time."
		""
		"&3Quadruple Fluid Pipes&r can transfer four different types of fluids. &3Nonuple Fluid Pipes&r can transfer nine different types! Useful for compact setups."
		""
		"&3Nonuple Fluid Pipes&r will be useful in &5EV&r for handling the many outputs of the &3Distillation Tower&r."
		""
		"Get &eeither&r to finish this quest."
	]
	quest.67328B8754357E78.quest_subtitle: "Four fluids, one pipe"
	quest.67328B8754357E78.title: "Multiple Channel Pipes"
	quest.674DAF5B8A4BE940.quest_desc: [
		"Thunderstorms can set your thatch and timber alight. To keep lightning away from your base, you can use a &dLightning Rod&r for the cheap price of 3 copper rods."
		""
		"The &dLightning Rod&r redirects lightning that would strike within &3128 blocks&r onto itself, as long as nothing is built above it."
		"Beware: It &oredirects&r lightning and doesn't nullify it, so a strike can still start fires right around it. Place it far away from any flammables."
	]
	quest.674DAF5B8A4BE940.quest_subtitle: "Undesirable voltage"
	quest.674DAF5B8A4BE940.title: "Lightning Rod"
	quest.6774E44AB58F381E.quest_desc: [
		"&aEnergium Crystals&r store a significant amount of &9EU&r. They're also arguably cheaper."
	]
	quest.6774E44AB58F381E.quest_subtitle: "Science-fiction batteries!"
	quest.6774E44AB58F381E.title: "Super Batteries"
	quest.67CB089C79635B9B.quest_desc: [
		"&3Long-Distance Fluid Pipes&r can be used to send fluids across great distances. Place one endpoint at each end, and connect them with pipeline blocks."
		""
		"These pipes instantly transfer from the input side to the output side."
		""
		"They also have a minimum distance between pipe endpoints, so you can't use these for short-range operations."
		""
		"These pipes have a reputation of being &4buggy&r to set up. If they don't seem to work at first, try rotating the endpoints with a &eWrench&r."
	]
	quest.67CB089C79635B9B.quest_subtitle: "Wondering how to move that oil around?"
	quest.67CB089C79635B9B.title: "Long-Distance Fluid Pipes"
	quest.67E8B880BF6FD1D5.quest_desc: [
		"Once you get to IV, you'll gain access to multiblock versions of GregTech's single block machines. They do the exact same recipes as their single block cousins, but are more flexible - you can put lots of huge Input Buses on them, you can overclock them with higher tier &6Energy Hatches&r instead of making new ones every tier, and they even support &6Parallel Hatches&r to do multiple recipes simultaneously!"
		""
		"Their recipes and casings take advanced alloys, so check EMI before you commit."
	]
	quest.67E8B880BF6FD1D5.quest_subtitle: "When size does matter"
	quest.67E8B880BF6FD1D5.title: "Ore processing but bigger"
	quest.67F846139EFC06D9.quest_desc: [
		"&aRandom Access Memory&r is required for many Circuits."
	]
	quest.67F846139EFC06D9.quest_subtitle: "Also a Daft Punk album"
	quest.67F846139EFC06D9.title: "Download more RAM"
	quest.68964210104DDDF9.quest_desc: [
		"Glass tubes come out of the Alloy Smelter: one glass dust with a &aBall Casting Mold&r. Grind glass (made with TFC's glassworking) in the steam macerator for the dust."
	]
	quest.68964210104DDDF9.quest_subtitle: "You'll want a lot of these"
	quest.68964210104DDDF9.title: "Glass Tubes"
	quest.68FFC078004E064D.quest_desc: [
		"To craft &6RTM Alloy&r, you'll need &dRuthenium&r, a product of the infamous &dPlatline&r, &aTungsten&r and a little &aMolybdenum&r, mixed in your &5EV&r Mixer and smelted in the EBF at 3,000K."
		""
		"Before rushing into RTM production, make sure your Platline and Tungsten line are running smoothly."
		""
		"Its main use is the &6RTM Coil&r, a powerful upgrade for your EBF and many of your other coil multiblocks."
	]
	quest.68FFC078004E064D.quest_subtitle: "Ruthenium-Tungsten-Molybdenum Alloy"
	quest.68FFC078004E064D.title: "RTM Alloy"
	quest.692F13DC4C41443D.quest_desc: [
		"Distilling &bLiquid Air&r is a core mechanic in &6GregTech&r to obtain an &oinfinite supply&r of certain rare gases."
		""
		"Liquefy Air in your &3Vacuum Freezer&r, then distill it to get your hands on &bArgon&r, &6Oxygen&r, &eHelium&r, &3Nitrogen&r and &aCarbon Dioxide&r."
	]
	quest.692F13DC4C41443D.quest_subtitle: "So many gases"
	quest.692F13DC4C41443D.title: "Liquid Air"
	quest.6949C06F669C6F94.quest_desc: [
		"With the creation of this machine, many recipes that once required you to use a hammer can instead be made here, and quickly: crushed ore into impure dust, purified ore into purified dust, and gem blocks back into gems."
		""
		"It also makes &aPlates&r at a better ratio than by hand: &6three Ingots for two Plates&r. (Create's press still beats it at one for one.)"
		""
		"It crushes vanilla cobblestone into gravel and gravel into sand, but not TFC rock. Its recipe takes a vanilla anvil, so start saving wrought iron."
	]
	quest.6949C06F669C6F94.quest_subtitle: "The Forge Hammer hammers..."
	quest.6949C06F669C6F94.title: "Steam Forge Hammer"
	quest.69563131D6E8644E.quest_desc: [
		"For now, your only use for Nitrogen will be to make your EBF &6faster&r, which may not sound like that big of a deal, but with how much you'll be using it, it's definitely worth setting up. Faster recipes mean less energy used too!"
	]
	quest.69563131D6E8644E.quest_subtitle: "Your EBF booster"
	quest.69563131D6E8644E.title: "Nitrogen Gas"
	quest.69F6DD182C0C917F.quest_desc: [
		"This quest is here to point out the &9Sea Water&r in &aTerraFirmaCraft&r's oceans. GregTech takes TFC's salt water wherever a recipe asks for Salt Water."
		""
		"Pump it from the sea and &aelectrolyze it&r to get &dChlorine&r, &dHydrogen&r and &dSodium Hydroxide&r."
	]
	quest.69F6DD182C0C917F.quest_subtitle: "As wide as an ocean..."
	quest.69F6DD182C0C917F.title: "Sea Water"
	quest.6A0CD2F7E3907CD7.quest_desc: [
		"&6The Distillation Tower&r (DT) is a direct multiblock upgrade of the &6Distillery&r. You won't have to choose outputs any more as the DT will handle them all automatically, at an increased power cost."
		""
		"This machine will be your future bread and butter for anything involving &ePetrochem&r or &eOrganic distillation."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Like the &6Cleanroom&r, the DT can be made taller, though not wider. Starting from the second layer, each added level requires an &9Output Hatch&r and grants one additional fluid output slot; if a level lacks its output hatch, the corresponding fluid will be voided. Count the number of outputs with &dEMI&r so you know how many layers you need. As always, use the Multiblock Preview tab in &dEMI&r and click the multiblock to see where you can place each part."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&cNote:&r Be careful not to over-overclock the DT when producing fuels! Excessive overclocking can reduce the overall power yield, especially for Diesel. Do the math and double-check your calculations."
	]
	quest.6A0CD2F7E3907CD7.quest_subtitle: "Mr. President, another Distillation Tower has hit the factory floor"
	quest.6A0CD2F7E3907CD7.title: "The Distillation Tower"
	quest.6A5536E072CC2898.quest_desc: [
		"We &lSINCERELY&r hope you didn't make the &7LV&r Extruder, because only the &bMV&r Extruder is actually useful: almost every extruder recipe needs more than &7LV&r power."
		""
		"The Extruder shapes solid materials into (almost!) any form using &aIngots&r. This is a great way to reduce the amount of microcrafting, as well as keeping a high conversion ratio."
		""
		"The Extruder can make &6Bolts&r, &6Small Gears&r, &6Gears&r, and &6Rings&r at the highest efficiency in a single step!"
		""
		"You may also like to use it for &dPipes&r, &dScrews&r, and &dRotors&r."
	]
	quest.6A5536E072CC2898.quest_subtitle: "The biggest upgrade you'll make"
	quest.6A5536E072CC2898.title: "Advanced Extruder"
	quest.6A8199CB44B54E2C.quest_desc: [
		"You can now move your items around! Chutes drop items straight down into whatever is below them (an encased fan can push them up). Funnels pull items out of, or put them into, inventories and belts. Hoppers work too: GregTech makes them from iron plates, TFC from steel sheets."
		""
		"Chutes and hoppers can also push items from containers into GregTech's item pipes."
	]
	quest.6A8199CB44B54E2C.quest_subtitle: "Public infrastructure for your items"
	quest.6A8199CB44B54E2C.title: "Early Logistics"
	quest.6AA37138C25E6BA2.quest_desc: [
		"Another hidden mechanic in GregTech Multiblocks: the &dSubtick&r."
		""
		"What is it? Subtick kicks in when a recipe gets so fast it would take less than one tick. Normally, machines can't go faster than one recipe per tick — but with Subtick, they can!"
		""
		"How does it work? Once a recipe hits 1 tick, more power can't make it any shorter."
		"Instead of wasting that power, the machine &aruns several recipes in parallel internally&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&dNote&r: the &6Large Chemical Reactor&r, an &6HV&r multiblock, combines Subtick with Perfect Overclocking, so extra power is never wasted on it. That makes it the best home for your fast chemistry."
	]
	quest.6AA37138C25E6BA2.quest_subtitle: "Parallel?"
	quest.6AA37138C25E6BA2.title: "Subtick"
	quest.6AF69F9A5D54F09B.title: "Black Steel Age"
	quest.6B241B430FF4A0EB.quest_desc: [
		"Epoxy Circuit Boards are a key component required to craft your &bNano Circuits&r, but they won’t have much use outside of that purpose."
	]
	quest.6B241B430FF4A0EB.quest_subtitle: "A new board, there is more to come"
	quest.6B241B430FF4A0EB.title: "A new board, there is more to come"
	quest.6B5734E2CD596CAB.quest_desc: [
		"These are your basic &61-block Generators&r. Each has a single &9input&r for its fuel — &esteam&r, &agas&r or &6liquid fuel&r — and outputs exactly &e1A&r of power at its tier."
		""
		"They're simple to work with and will be your &ofirst source of power&r in &5GregTech&r until you reach the &dlarge multiblock generators&r later on."
		""
		"&aEMI&r shows what each one burns, and the fuel quests nearby list the best inputs. Here's what &7LV&r offers in this pack:"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e1. Steam Power&r:"
		""
		"The main road here. A Steam Turbine turns the steam from your boilers into EU: &e32 EU/t&r from &e64 mB/t&r of steam. When single boilers can't keep up, build a &6Large Bronze Boiler&r, which burns solid fuels, lava or creosote (check EMI!)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e2. Gas Power&r:"
		""
		"The Gas Turbine burns gases. At &7LV&r that means &eMethane&r: a Centrifuge gets 60 mB from every rubber log, along with sticky resin you need anyway. Not strong, but a rubber tree farm keeps it going."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&e3. Combustion Power&r:"
		""
		"The Combustion Generator burns liquid fuels that pack a lot of energy per mB, easy to carry around in drums or cells. In this pack those fuels (ethanol, methanol, bio diesel, then oil products) arrive at &bMV&r, so this one can wait."
		""
		"It's your choice how you want to grow your energy production."
	]
	quest.6B5734E2CD596CAB.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to LV"
	quest.6B5734E2CD596CAB.title: "Let's make energy"
	quest.6B6F8FE279EE0D2E.quest_desc: [
		"Now these are some real shields. Metal shields are forged on an anvil from a &7double sheet&r of the metal, and better metals last longer."
	]
	quest.6B6F8FE279EE0D2E.quest_subtitle: "Premium protection"
	quest.6B6F8FE279EE0D2E.title: "Metal Shield"
	quest.6BB8F5758A133443.quest_desc: [
		"While distilling &aWood Vinegar&r gives &aAcetone&r, the yield is low and might not meet your needs."
		""
		"You might want to use the direct &3LCR&r recipe from &aAcetic Acid&r to obtain &aAcetone&r."
		""
		"If you want to be fancy, you can also the good old &aAcetic Acid&r -> &dDissolved Calcium Acetate&r -> &aAcetone&r loop, which does not require a &3LCR&r, but still recycles the Calcium compound perfectly."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"We've been talking about Acetic Acid, but we're yet to tell you how to obtain it. Wouldn't that be great?"
		""
		"&aAcetic Acid&r can be synthesized in the &3Chemical Reactor&r. Our favorite recipe is from &dEthylene&r."
	]
	quest.6BB8F5758A133443.title: "Acetone"
	quest.6BD08720DB4FE695.quest_desc: [
		"Put a water wheel in a river. TFC: Real World's rivers follow real rivers."
		""
		"Water wheels need flowing water. If you're far from a river, a windmill is the other way to get going."
	]
	quest.6BD08720DB4FE695.quest_subtitle: "A water wheel"
	quest.6BD08720DB4FE695.title: "Power"
	quest.6BE3F5EC04A9AE2B.quest_desc: [
		"Fire clay is a special clay made of kaolinite, graphite and regular clay that stands up to very high temperatures. It makes the crucible, a better vessel for melting and alloying metal, and fire bricks: GregTech's steam machines are built with them, and TFC's blast furnace, the way to steel, needs them too."
		""
		"You'll likely need to travel far, far away from your base for both graphite and kaolin clay, so preparation is key!"
	]
	quest.6BE3F5EC04A9AE2B.quest_subtitle: "The TerraFirmaCraft Rite of Passage."
	quest.6BE3F5EC04A9AE2B.title: "Fire Clay Ingredients"
	quest.6CDF98F6A3920C34.quest_desc: [
		"Light up your Forge and give it at least 2 Copper Ingots. Keep an eye on their tooltip as they heat up - once they get hot, it'll show \"Can Work\", but we need to wait until they get to \"Can Weld\", which is just before their melting point."
		""
		"Once they reach it, quickly move them from the forge into the Rock Anvil's interface (the two left slots), along with at least one Flux. Then use a hammer on the anvil to weld the two ingots together while they're still hot. A barrel of water cools your new double ingot down quickly."
	]
	quest.6CDF98F6A3920C34.quest_subtitle: "So close to the Copper Anvil"
	quest.6CDF98F6A3920C34.title: "Welding Copper"
	quest.6CE745CFBA9F7B1F.quest_desc: [
		"With IV comes the big huge multiblocks to really ramp up your ore processing speeds."
	]
	quest.6CE745CFBA9F7B1F.title: "&9IV&r Ore Processing"
	quest.6CF83DD6A75997DF.quest_desc: [
		"Covers are placed by right-clicking with Cover in hand on a face of a machine, and removed with a &5Crowbar&r (or by mining the machine, but that's way slower)."
		""
		"Pretty much any GregTech Tile-Entity will accept Covers, even if they wouldn't provide any functionality."
		""
		"Opening a Cover is done by sneak-right-clicking it with an &5empty hand&r. You can also right-click with a &5Screwdriver&r, or sneak-right-click on another face using the grid."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"For Covers that transfer Items/Fluids, you will have a button to enable/disable other forms of transfer through the cover:"
		""
		"&9- &rDisabled: only the cover will be allowed to transfer on this machine side."
		""
		"&9-&r Allow Filtered (only relevant with a filter!): other transfer will be enabled only if it matches the filter"
		""
		"&9-&r Allow Unfiltered: any other transfer is allowed on this machine side."
		""
		"Placing a cover of a lower voltage tier on a machine is &9safe&r."
	]
	quest.6CF83DD6A75997DF.quest_subtitle: "Extra utility without taking up blockspace!"
	quest.6CF83DD6A75997DF.title: "Cover Behaviour"
	quest.6D0A213A7D4A5A81.quest_desc: [
		"Blue steel first starts as high carbon blue steel: weld weak blue steel and black steel together, then work it on the anvil into blue steel."
	]
	quest.6D0A213A7D4A5A81.quest_subtitle: "Lavoisier is rolling in his grave"
	quest.6D0A213A7D4A5A81.title: "Blue Steel Ingredients"
	quest.6D80746D14ED659F.quest_desc: [
		"Obtain &9Hydrochloric Acid&r by mixing &aHydrogen&r and &aChlorine&r."
		""
		"This acid is also obtained as waste from a lot of reactions involving &aChlorine&r. Depending on your setups, you may never need to produce it directly."
	]
	quest.6D80746D14ED659F.quest_subtitle: "You'll need a lot of this!"
	quest.6D80746D14ED659F.title: "Hydrochloric Acid"
	quest.6DF3F3C9B0B5E8DB.quest_desc: [
		"This pack has a plethora of fluids, so you may be looking for a way to store them."
		""
		"Introducing... &aDrums&r! They have large internal buffers, and any &aDrum&r can be broken and picked up and will &dkeep the fluid&r inside. A right-click with a Soft Mallet or Screwdriver lets a Drum drain its contents into a tank placed below it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o These drums are actually ported from GregTech 6."
	]
	quest.6DF3F3C9B0B5E8DB.quest_subtitle: "I don't think a wooden barrel can hold molten steel"
	quest.6DF3F3C9B0B5E8DB.title: "Efficient Fluid Storage"
	quest.6E03414E198D6F06.quest_desc: [
		"Create's &6Copper Diving Helmet&r lets you breathe underwater for as long as the &6Copper Backtank&r on your back has air. Place the backtank and give it rotational power to fill it up."
		""
		"&aCopper Diving Boots&r make you sink and walk along the bottom instead of swimming."
	]
	quest.6E03414E198D6F06.quest_subtitle: "Swimsuit not included"
	quest.6E03414E198D6F06.title: "Diving Gear"
	quest.6E861EE7844116EA.quest_desc: [
		"Bare ridge and arc rock is coated in ferromanganese crust. A pickaxe gives raw pyrolusite, cobaltite and, rarely (one block in 25), pitchblende: the pack's stand-in for the uranium that crusts really do adsorb."
		""
		"Pitchblende goes the usual way (crush, wash, thermal centrifuge) to uraninite, then hydrofluoric acid and fluorine make uranium hexafluoride, and an electrolyzer separates uranium 235 and 238. The fluorine is the slow part: biotite is the pack's source."
	]
	quest.6E861EE7844116EA.quest_subtitle: "Rock with a skin"
	quest.6E861EE7844116EA.title: "Manganese Crust"
	quest.6E9EB0291CCDFE0D.quest_desc: [
		"The only thing separating man from animal is our use of &l&bTools&r&r. &7&oExcept for apes, monkeys, dolphins, crows, otters, octo.......&r&r Use your skills and tools to make the most of this world, and &5save yourself&r some effort."
	]
	quest.6E9EB0291CCDFE0D.quest_subtitle: "It's all a hammer anyways."
	quest.6E9EB0291CCDFE0D.title: "Tools"
	quest.6EB96826C21AC73A.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Vacuum Freezer&r is a multiblock used to cool down &eHot Ingots&r. All ingots made in the EBF with a temperature above &d1750K&r will need it."
		""
		"Most of the time, your &3Electric Blast Furnace&r will be the bottleneck, so you don't need to worry about overclocking your freezer."
		""
		"Since &eHot Ingots&r &churt you&r when held, item routing will be very useful."
	]
	quest.6EB96826C21AC73A.quest_subtitle: "Did you know vacuums actually make things hotter?"
	quest.6EB96826C21AC73A.title: "Ice Cold"
	quest.6F12E7496ECE2F7C.quest_desc: [
		"If you're wanting to dive into &bMV&r, start here."
		""
		"The dusts created in an &3MV Mixer&r have great utility."
	]
	quest.6F12E7496ECE2F7C.quest_subtitle: "Mixing more complex alloys"
	quest.6F12E7496ECE2F7C.title: "Advanced Mixer"
	quest.6F9840D28A7DDD2A.quest_desc: [
		"The final tier of anvil can be made of either red or blue steel. Both are complex alloys of black steel, steel and two more metals: brass and rose gold for red steel, bismuth bronze and sterling silver for blue."
		""
		"Red steel has one more use here: welded onto Create's copper diving gear, red steel armour turns it into netherite diving gear."
	]
	quest.6F9840D28A7DDD2A.quest_subtitle: "Some of the oldest modded Minecraft fantasy steels"
	quest.6F9840D28A7DDD2A.title: "Red and Blue Steel"
	quest.6FA751181FAF7647.quest_desc: [
		"Leather Armor, just like its Minecraft counterpart, is a very basic set of armor, knapped from leather. It doesn't last long, but a full suit gives decent protection against the predators of the early game."
	]
	quest.6FA751181FAF7647.quest_subtitle: "Very basic protection"
	quest.6FA751181FAF7647.title: "Leather Armor"
	quest.7024410B1C9159F0.quest_desc: [
		"The Stonecutter turns blocks into their decorative versions in one step, without chiselling each one in the world."
		""
		"It's the workshop for this pack's building mods: Create's cut and polished stones (TFC andesite, basalt, dacite and rhyolite count as andesite; TFC limestone, chalk and tuff give Create's limestone, calcite and tuff), Create Deco's bricks and catwalks, Steam 'n' Rails' locometal and Copycats+ blocks. Create's mechanical saw does the same job automatically."
	]
	quest.7024410B1C9159F0.quest_subtitle: "Decorate your builds!"
	quest.7024410B1C9159F0.title: "Stonecutters"
	quest.705F6537521D0CED.quest_desc: [
		"LV comes with a ton of machines that can process your ores in many different ways. The most important is probably the Thermal Centrifuge."
	]
	quest.705F6537521D0CED.title: "&7LV&r Ore Processing"
	quest.7096717AEDE99D3C.quest_desc: [
		"Like before, weak blue steel is the first step of blue steel. Alloy it from 4 parts black steel, 2 parts steel, 1 part bismuth bronze and 1 part sterling silver."
		""
		"The exact ranges are 50-55% black steel, 20-25% steel and 10-15% each of bismuth bronze and sterling silver."
	]
	quest.7096717AEDE99D3C.quest_subtitle: "This is getting out of hand."
	quest.7096717AEDE99D3C.title: "Weak Blue Steel Ingredients"
	quest.70AC26E7B17D3A33.quest_desc: [
		"This Jetpack burns combustion fuels to enable a primitive form of flight."
		""
		"Fill it like you would fill a Drum, or with a &3Canning Machine&r. In this pack its fuels arrive at &bMV&r: ethanol, methanol or bio diesel will do."
	]
	quest.70AC26E7B17D3A33.quest_subtitle: "...well, almost Fly"
	quest.70AC26E7B17D3A33.title: "I Believe I Can Fly"
	quest.70D4CDC5438ED00B.quest_desc: [
		"Vacuum tubes, resistors and red alloy cable on a circuit board, with a steel plate. Circuits gate every LV machine."
		""
		"The recipe may look intimidating, but if you've spent some time in the steam age, every part should be easy to make in bulk. You'll be making a lot of these: the assembler makes their parts cheaper, and the circuit assembler makes two circuits at a time."
	]
	quest.70D4CDC5438ED00B.quest_subtitle: "Electronic circuit"
	quest.70D4CDC5438ED00B.title: "Circuits"
	quest.713241BB5FF5A95F.quest_desc: [
		"Pick up loose rocks and sticks from the ground. Knap rocks into tool heads (use two rocks), then craft a head with a stick. A knife and an axe come first: the axe fells whole trees, the knife cuts straw from grass and plants."
		""
		"You've officially entered the Stone Age! Stone tools are enough for basic survival, but eventually you'll want metal tools for much better speed, durability and tool options."
	]
	quest.713241BB5FF5A95F.quest_subtitle: "Knap loose rocks"
	quest.713241BB5FF5A95F.title: "Stone Tools"
	quest.7209557EAD971E75.quest_desc: [
		"GregTech's &aWood Plank&r is a thin wooden plate, the base of your first circuit boards. Grind logs (TFC logs work) into wood pulp in a macerator, then press the pulp into planks in the Steam Compressor, one each."
	]
	quest.7209557EAD971E75.quest_subtitle: "Untreated Plywood...?"
	quest.7209557EAD971E75.title: "Wood Planks"
	quest.7240010A1012782E.quest_desc: [
		"Until you can upgrade, an axe will be your most reliable weapon. Along with high damage, they deal &6Slashing&r damage, which neither Zombies nor Skeletons resist."
		""
		"For more information on &cDamage Types&r consult the &3Field Guide&r."
	]
	quest.7240010A1012782E.quest_subtitle: "Good for more than wood"
	quest.7240010A1012782E.title: "Axes"
	quest.727711AAFEF0B076.quest_desc: [
		"Coat a wood plank in sticky resin: one plank and two resin make a &aResin Circuit Board&r (three planks and six resin make three)."
	]
	quest.727711AAFEF0B076.quest_subtitle: "I guess you could say we're... bored of LaTeX?"
	quest.727711AAFEF0B076.title: "Resin-Coated Boards"
	quest.727A1E0D3CC4D5DC.quest_desc: [
		"&oThis quest's subject is optional, but may still be of interest to you. We've put it here in the name of completeness.&r"
		""
		"The &3Turbo Charger&r charges electric items such as &9Drills&r extremely quickly."
		""
		"It accepts up to 4 Amps for every item it charges, making it &6twice as fast&r as the &3Battery Buffer&r. It cannot discharge, though."
		""
		"&eAny&r Charger will complete this Quest."
	]
	quest.727A1E0D3CC4D5DC.quest_subtitle: "Useful to charge your electric tools faster"
	quest.727A1E0D3CC4D5DC.title: "Turbo Charger"
	quest.72872C829E97A326.quest_desc: [
		"Argon is used to speed up the electric blast furnace for many high-tier alloys."
		""
		"It can be obtained from liquid air in the distillation tower, like helium. The vacuum freezer and the distillation tower both need &5EV&r circuits."
	]
	quest.72872C829E97A326.quest_subtitle: "Element #18"
	quest.72872C829E97A326.title: "Argon"
	quest.72E64E89ED3F2A0A.quest_desc: [
		"The barrel rack can be used to stack barrels on top of each other, allowing you to be more space-efficient!"
		""
		"Consult your field guide for more specific information on how to use them."
	]
	quest.72E64E89ED3F2A0A.quest_subtitle: "Now that's a nice rack!"
	quest.72E64E89ED3F2A0A.title: "Barrel Rack"
	quest.72F250C6D71F9B1B.quest_desc: [
		"Trains are a fantastic option when it comes to any sort of long distance transportation, whether that's players, items, or fluids! They can also safely travel through unloaded chunks. On a real-scale Earth, where Rome to Naples is 9,500 blocks, a rail network pays for itself."
		""
		"Tracks come out of sequenced assembly, so you'll need deployers; stations and controls start from train casing (brass casing with an obsidian plate). Steam 'n' Rails adds more tracks and locometal train parts, and its locometal boilers take GregTech coke."
	]
	quest.72F250C6D71F9B1B.quest_subtitle: "Waypoints wishes it was as cool as these"
	quest.72F250C6D71F9B1B.title: "Trains"
	quest.7329DED320FAFB9B.quest_desc: [
		"Tin is used in the bronze age to make bronze, and in GregTech for soldering alloy and the tin cables of &7LV&r."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC cassiterite."
	]
	quest.7329DED320FAFB9B.quest_subtitle: "Element #50"
	quest.7329DED320FAFB9B.title: "Tin"
	quest.7382E8B12DA03926.quest_desc: [
		"Any Steel you encounter in day-to-day life is most likely &7Stainless Steel&r. It is extremely resilient against corrosion.&r"
		""
		"Stainless Steel is the material for &6HV&r components, like Aluminium for &bMV&r and Steel for &7LV&r. It is also used in large amounts in the &3Distillation Tower&r."
		""
		"It needs &cChromium&r, from &cRuby&r, and &2Manganese&r. In this pack manganese is scarce: it comes from &2Spessartine&r, which you get by centrifuging the &cRed Garnet&r that processing Ruby leaves behind, and then electrolyzing it in an &bMV&r Electrolyzer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Smelting Stainless Steel requires &dHV Power&r, which you likely do not have at this point. Scaling Power Production is crucial."
		""
		"If you &9haven't already&r, it would be a good idea to get a second EBF going. Multiblocks can share blocks, so a second EBF built against the first only needs &a10 Cupronickel Coils&r instead of 16."
		""
		"Have one EBF run off &bMV&r for Aluminium and any other recipes requiring &bMV&r Power, and one running off &6HV&r with &32 MV Energy Hatches&r."
	]
	quest.7382E8B12DA03926.quest_subtitle: "HV is in your grasp"
	quest.7382E8B12DA03926.title: "Stainless Steel"
	quest.73B372D980E0AD59.quest_desc: [
		"Phosphorus is a plant nutrient. It is used to make manganese phosphide, the &7LV&r superconductor, and later phosphorus-doped silicon boules."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r from tricalcium phosphate, a byproduct of processing TFC pyrite: centrifuge it into calcium and phosphate, then electrolyze the phosphate."
	]
	quest.73B372D980E0AD59.quest_subtitle: "Element #15"
	quest.73B372D980E0AD59.title: "Phosphorus"
	quest.73C85F0F7531C720.quest_desc: [
		"You will need the &6HV&r Mixer for several important recipes:"
		""
		"- &5Ender Pearl Dust&r"
		"- &eCetane Boosted Diesel&r"
		"- The valuable &6Ultimet Alloy&r, used for &9Turbine Rotors&r and the &5EV&r Cutter"
		"- &9Lapotron Dust&r for &5EV&r batteries"
	]
	quest.73C85F0F7531C720.quest_subtitle: "Mixing never got so good"
	quest.73C85F0F7531C720.title: "High Voltage Mixer"
	quest.73CB595C671E2AC9.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Nano Saber&r is a powerful weapon you’ll be able to unlock once you reach late &5EV&r. Simply use &dShift + Right-Click&r to activate the &cbzzzzz mode&r."
	]
	quest.73CB595C671E2AC9.quest_subtitle: "26 Attack Damage when active!"
	quest.73CB595C671E2AC9.title: "Nano Saber"
	quest.73D4041F4BBECD24.quest_desc: [
		"To run your &bMV&r machines, you will need to upgrade your power production."
		""
		"If an &7LV&r Generator produces &e32 EU/t&r, the &bMV&r Generator runs at &e128 EU/t&r."
		"It consumes four times more fuel to produce four times more energy."
		""
		"At &bMV&r you also gain access to more options:"
		""
		"- Liquid fuels: ethanol, methanol and bio diesel, later diesel and light oil residue"
		"- Gas fuels: methane, refinery gas, LPG and benzene"
		"- Steam keeps working, though you may need larger pipes (steel, aluminium or potin can handle it)"
		""
		"The &bMV&r chapter has more on power at this tier."
	]
	quest.73D4041F4BBECD24.quest_subtitle: "Basically the same as the LV ones"
	quest.73D4041F4BBECD24.title: "The MV Generators"
	quest.73ED6B0CB4B2014D.quest_desc: [
		"&3TerraFirmaCraft&r is the survival half of this pack. This branch covers some of its handier features, such as &dglassworking&r, &dlamps&r and &bfishing&r."
	]
	quest.73ED6B0CB4B2014D.quest_subtitle: "The ground this pack stands on."
	quest.73ED6B0CB4B2014D.title: "TerraFirmaCraft"
	quest.741C08492572FB66.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you've got a few machines going, it's time to put them to work."
		""
		"The Assembler will make electronic components cheaper, while the Chemical Reactor, Extractor, and Fluid Solidifier will make Rubber cheaper. After that, the rest of &7LV&r is yours to explore!"
	]
	quest.741C08492572FB66.quest_subtitle: "Now the fun begins"
	quest.741C08492572FB66.title: "Even more machines"
	quest.744DCCFC40160583.quest_desc: [
		"Built from TFC's blast furnace, heat-proof invar casings and LV circuits. It needs cupronickel coils and electricity to run."
		""
		"Your &efirst electric multiblock&r: three TFC blast furnaces, three LV circuits, a heat-proof casing and two tin cables make the controller. It processes materials at high temperatures; its main job now is &aAluminium&r (1700K), on the way to &bMV&r."
		""
		"It's a beefy boy: every recipe needs at least &9120 EU/t&r, almost four &7LV&r generators. Two LV energy hatches let it draw up to 128 EU/t. Keep the generators close and use thick cable (2x tin cable or better), or cable loss will make it flicker."
	]
	quest.744DCCFC40160583.quest_subtitle: "The next tier"
	quest.744DCCFC40160583.title: "Electric Blast Furnace"
	quest.7452DA48ECE0BA0C.quest_desc: [
		"Now that you unlocked the &6HV&r Mixer and have access to &eNitric Acid&r, it becomes possible to make &aCetane Boosted Diesel&r, which burns three times as long as plain Diesel in a Combustion Generator."
		""
		"The only tricky part is obtaining &bTetranitromethane&r. We recommend producing it by reacting &9Nitric Acid&r and &dEthenone&r. Ethenone itself isn't hard to make if you combine &9Sulfuric Acid&r - which you should have plenty of by now - and &cAcetic Acid&r, easily produced from &3Oxygen&r and &5Ethylene&r."
		""
		"&cDon't forget&r to set your machine on Circuit 2, or else you'll end up producing &6Polyethylene&r instead!"
	]
	quest.7452DA48ECE0BA0C.quest_subtitle: "This is to go further beyond"
	quest.7452DA48ECE0BA0C.title: "Cetane-boosted Diesel"
	quest.7476B8B81EE7EE9B.quest_desc: [
		"Your second kind of &1IV&r Circuit. It needs NOR Memory Chips and SMD Diodes on top of your Nano Processor Assemblies, so it isn't actually cheaper than the &bMicroprocessor&r Mainframe."
		""
		"However, it will be essential for progressing toward the next tier of technology."
	]
	quest.7476B8B81EE7EE9B.quest_subtitle: "Getting closer to LuV technology"
	quest.7476B8B81EE7EE9B.title: "Getting closer to LuV technology"
	quest.74BF5DED7BA370A4.quest_desc: [
		"&bTungsten Carbide Tools&r clearly belong to the extreme &eSpeed&r category, but they come with relatively low &aDurability&r and the fact that &6Tungsten&r may still be somewhat tedious to produce at this stage. They may even be too fast to comfortably use as a &bWrench&r, but they can feel excellent when crafted as a &bDrill&r or &bWire Cutter&r."
	]
	quest.74BF5DED7BA370A4.quest_subtitle: "As fast as you can expect"
	quest.74BF5DED7BA370A4.title: "Tungsten Carbide Tools"
	quest.74C3FEDFF373113E.quest_desc: [
		"&bMV&r Batteries will appeal to you if you want to buffer Energy, just like &7LV&r."
		""
		"The cost in &aSodium&r, &aLithium&r or &aCadmium&r jumps up to 8 dusts, so you should use whatever you have the most of. The difference in capacity isn't &7THAT&r huge, after all!"
		""
		"Get &eeither&r Battery to complete the Quest."
	]
	quest.74C3FEDFF373113E.quest_subtitle: "Baby Got Battery"
	quest.74C3FEDFF373113E.title: "Better Batteries"
	quest.74D7FEE5F847CDAC.quest_desc: [
		"In theory, Crates are flat upgrades to Chests. A single block space that stores more items - what more could you ask for?"
		""
		"They're more expensive than regular Chests, but they hold items of any size and can &6accept Covers&r, making them perfect candidates for buffers in automation."
	]
	quest.74D7FEE5F847CDAC.quest_subtitle: "Earlygame buffering"
	quest.74D7FEE5F847CDAC.title: "GregTech Storage"
	quest.74D8409DABB44108.quest_desc: [
		"Like before, weak red steel is the first step of red steel. Alloy it from 4 parts black steel, 2 parts steel, 1 part brass and 1 part rose gold."
		""
		"The exact ranges are 50-55% black steel, 20-25% steel and 10-15% each of brass and rose gold."
	]
	quest.74D8409DABB44108.quest_subtitle: "This is getting a little ridiculous"
	quest.74D8409DABB44108.title: "Weak Red Steel Ingredients"
	quest.7574FEF33C293D98.quest_desc: [
		"This Circuit Board is used to create &dMV Circuits&r!"
		""
		"First make a Phenolic Circuit Board in the &3Assembler&r from wood pulp and &aGlue&r. Then etch it: by hand with 8 silver wires, or in the &3Chemical Reactor&r with 4 silver foils and &aIron III Chloride&r or &aSodium Persulfate&r, which takes &6only a quarter of the Silver&r."
		""
		"Given how painful those chemicals may be to obtain &oright now&r, you can simply use more silver from TFC's native silver."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o Back in GTCEu 1.12.2, these circuit boards were called &2Good Circuit Boards&f. Not exactly a fitting name, as they're &4rather evil&f to craft."
	]
	quest.7574FEF33C293D98.quest_subtitle: "They don't make 'em like this any more..."
	quest.7574FEF33C293D98.title: "Phenolic Printed Circuit Board"
	quest.759572A2C5F67BEE.quest_desc: [
		"Get at least 14 ingots of one kind of bronze and weld them in pairs on your copper anvil (with flux) into seven double ingots."
		""
		"The tier-2 anvil can be made from bronze, bismuth bronze or black bronze, but not a mixture of the three."
	]
	quest.759572A2C5F67BEE.quest_subtitle: "I told you to get used to it"
	quest.759572A2C5F67BEE.title: "Welding Bronze"
	quest.75D85202FBB76019.quest_desc: [
		"&3Nichrome Heating Coils&r bring your &3Electric Blast Furnace&r up to &d3,600K&r."
		""
		"Titanium only needs Kanthal coils, but the hotter recipes ahead need these: the &6HV&r Superconductor (3,300K), Tungstensteel (3,000K) and Tungsten (3,600K)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o In the original GregTech 5, there were only three types of coils. This was the last tier."
	]
	quest.75D85202FBB76019.quest_subtitle: "A long way to go before we beat the Sun"
	quest.75D85202FBB76019.title: "Nichrome Coils"
	quest.760B1FBE7A083E6A.quest_desc: [
		"The Wiremill is a good first machine. It draws &6two Wires from one Ingot&r, the same as Create's press and saw, but in one step and on electricity. It also makes &6fine wire&r, four from a single wire, which resistors and diodes eat by the stack."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&9Note:&r Recipes inside &3LV Machines&r go up to a maximum usage of &a32 EU/t (LV)&r. Anything higher than that and you will need a &bMV&r (or better) Machine. Needless to say, we aren't quite there yet."
		""
		"You will need a &dProgrammed Circuit&r for certain recipes. We're sure you don't want to spend a precious Circuit to craft one, so &6read the dedicated quest for important details&r."
		""
		"With this machine safely crafted - welcome to the age of all things electric!"
	]
	quest.760B1FBE7A083E6A.quest_subtitle: "No more painful wires!"
	quest.760B1FBE7A083E6A.title: "Basic Wiremill"
	quest.767876CA6DADE263.quest_desc: [
		"A &7LV&r Battery Buffer and two &7LV&r Energy Hatches likely won't cut it anymore. Let's remedy that!"
		""
		"Upgrade your Electric Blast Furnace with a &3MV Energy Hatch&r. Now, you can run it with &bMV&r Generators without having to mess around with &3Transformers&r."
	]
	quest.767876CA6DADE263.quest_subtitle: "LV is so old-school!"
	quest.767876CA6DADE263.title: "Upgrade your EBF!"
	quest.76EABECEE5D8A053.quest_desc: [
		"EV is the first tier where you'll need to start splitting up your ore processing into different \"lines\"."
	]
	quest.76EABECEE5D8A053.title: "&5EV&r Ore Processing"
	quest.76F737135F3C195A.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Cracker&r is a multiblock built with the sole purpose of cracking fluids. It comes with all the recipes of &3Chemical Reactor&r Cracking, but it is &6lossless&r."
		""
		"This is a great way to save a lot of Fuel in the long term!"
		""
		"Higher Coil tiers provide a small energy discount - up to 70%% with the best Coils available."
	]
	quest.76F737135F3C195A.quest_subtitle: "You Crack Me Up"
	quest.76F737135F3C195A.title: "You Crack Me Up"
	quest.7702DD7793FFE608.quest_desc: [
		"Well, that was quite the experience! Between the &9Rutile Processing&r line, the &5Vacuum Freezer&r, and the &5Cleanroom&r, you've uncovered a lot of new mechanics."
		""
		"If your infrastructure is solid, it's time to enter &5EV&r. This complex chapter will introduce &7even more advanced systems&r and take your factory to the next level."
	]
	quest.7702DD7793FFE608.quest_subtitle: "That's half of the GregTech tiers done"
	quest.7702DD7793FFE608.title: "&5EV&r Machine Hull"
	quest.77421A2EA9C1CE35.quest_desc: [
		"&9Silicon Boules&r are grown in the &3Electric Blast Furnace&r from 32 &aSilicon Dust&r and a small pile of &aGallium Arsenide&r. Their primary purpose is to make &6Wafers&r for circuits."
		""
		"After making the Boule, process it in the &3MV Cutter&r to get 16 Silicon Wafers ready for engraving."
		""
		"&cWarning:&r Each Silicon Boule takes &47.5 minutes&r to make at 120 EU/t, or 1,080,000 EU! If the EBF loses power midway, the recipe will start to &close progress&r."
		""
		"With that being said, Silicon Boules take an absolute age to craft, so consider &3stockpiling&r them."
	]
	quest.77421A2EA9C1CE35.quest_subtitle: "Giant crystals!"
	quest.77421A2EA9C1CE35.title: "Silicon Boules"
	quest.7752CF0B5B7FE022.quest_desc: [
		"Distilling &aOil&r will give you Residue that you will need to desulfurize."
		""
		"&aHydrogen Sulfide&r is perfectly &drecycled&r in an &3Electrolyzer&r."
		""
		"To automate this process, simply place your &3Chemical Reactor&r and your &3Electrolyzer&r next to each other. Be sure to use your &5Screwdriver&r to &4enable input from the output side&r."
		""
		"&aLight Oil Residue&r is a mediocre &9Power&r option, but you can turn it into something much greater... check the &aDiesel&r Quest."
	]
	quest.7752CF0B5B7FE022.quest_subtitle: "Turn up the lights in here, baby"
	quest.7752CF0B5B7FE022.title: "Light Oil Residue"
	quest.77B04582730D0020.quest_desc: [
		"By this point, normal Cables have such insignificant loss that superconductors aren't a requirement. That being said, they're still useful for being able to split and combine cables on the fly, and these ones are half oxygen so they're cheap too!"
		""
		"Superconductors are still required to craft &aField Generators&r."
	]
	quest.77B04582730D0020.title: "HV Superconductors"
	quest.7835AAE60BF01F3D.quest_desc: [
		"A blast furnace's chimney can be five layers tall, each a ring of eight reinforced fire bricks. Every layer holds four more ore, so a full one smelts twenty at a time."
		""
		"It's worth building it up: you'll need a lot of steel."
	]
	quest.7835AAE60BF01F3D.quest_subtitle: "The completed Blast Furnace"
	quest.7835AAE60BF01F3D.title: "Fully Stacked Blast Furnace"
	quest.78ECD5A5FFE1D5DC.quest_desc: [
		"Utilizing some &bThatch&r and a &aLarge Raw Hide&r, you can create a &dThatch Bed.&r It cannot be used to sleep in, but it'll &cset your spawn point.&r"
		""
		"To create a Thatch Bed, place &btwo thatch blocks&r side by side, then interact with the blocks while holding the &aLarge Raw Hide.&r"
	]
	quest.78ECD5A5FFE1D5DC.quest_subtitle: "A place to rest... somewhat"
	quest.78ECD5A5FFE1D5DC.title: "Thatch Bed"
	quest.78F3145CA138CF1F.quest_desc: [
		"&aGasoline&r is an extremely powerful Combustion Fuel. It's over &63 times&r as energy dense as &dDiesel&r!"
		""
		"&9Note:&r This Combustion Fuel exists solely as a &echallenge&r for you to overcome if you desire to take on it."
		""
		"It's completely &doptional&r, so we'll let you figure out how to obtain it, without any further tips."
	]
	quest.78F3145CA138CF1F.title: "Gasoline"
	quest.791962DF1FC6FD5D.quest_desc: [
		"When killed, wild animals drop raw hides. Hide cannot be used as leather directly and instead must be worked and processed first: soak it in limewater, scrape it on a log with a knife, soak it in water, then seal it in a barrel of tannin. The field guide's Leather Making page walks you through it."
		""
		"Leather, just like Clay and Stone, can be Knapped, into Leather Armor, saddles and horse armor. In this pack Create's belts take leather (or burlap) too."
	]
	quest.791962DF1FC6FD5D.quest_subtitle: "Because of course everything has to be more complicated"
	quest.791962DF1FC6FD5D.title: "Leather"
	quest.7932DAB3F7F720DD.quest_desc: [
		"&aRefinery Gas&r, &aLPG&r and &aMethane&r are &9Gas Fuels&r. LPG (Liquid Petroleum Gas) is a mix of hydrocarbons typically used in heating appliances."
		""
		"Refinery Gas is obtained either through &dNatural Gas&r or &dLight Oil&r, the latter yielding more, yet requiring an extra step of distillation."
		""
		"Use of a &3Centrifuge&r to separate into &aLPG&r and &aMethane&r should always be done, as it's practically free."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&a&aLPG&r and &aMethane&r are burned in a &3Gas Turbine&r. Among the other fuel options, they are the easier to set up which makes them excellent to get started. Their drawback is that they cannot be refined further, so upgrading the &3Fluid Drilling Rig&r may be a top priority if you stick to this fuel source."
		""
		"&aMethane&r can also be obtained from a few &anatural sources&r. &eBetween us&r, they're memes, but you can explore them if you wish. Ultimately, your power source is your choice."
	]
	quest.7932DAB3F7F720DD.quest_subtitle: "Whoever smelt it..."
	quest.7932DAB3F7F720DD.title: "The Church of Natural Farts"
	quest.7938C16E0526BF61.quest_desc: [
		"Calcium is used in &6HV&r to make mercury barium calcium cuprate, the &6HV&r superconductor, and in GregTech's fertilizer recipes."
		""
		"It can be obtained in &7LV&r in infinite amounts by electrolyzing bone meal, and as a byproduct of TFC gypsum and hematite."
	]
	quest.7938C16E0526BF61.quest_subtitle: "Element #20"
	quest.7938C16E0526BF61.title: "Calcium"
	quest.79524F90EE972B4B.quest_desc: [
		"The &3HV Autoclave&r - despite being optional - is a machine you'll definitively want to grab."
		""
		"This unlocks unique Batteries that are &6far superior&r to their standard counterparts."
	]
	quest.79524F90EE972B4B.quest_subtitle: "Home-grown batteries"
	quest.79524F90EE972B4B.title: "HV Autoclave"
	quest.79C7E780E467D887.quest_desc: [
		"You may notice that some fluids say they are &aAcidic&r, with &9Sulfuric Acid&r being one of them."
		""
		"This means that many fluid pipes will not be able to transport them safely!"
		""
		"At &bMV&r, the cheapest pipes for acid transportation are probably &aGold&r, with the more expensive &aStainless Steel&r pipes taking second place."
		""
		"&aStainless Steel&r or &aPolytetrafluoroethylene&r (try saying that fast) will be valid options once you are in &6HV&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You have three practical options for acid storage at around this point: &dGlass Vials&r, &dGold Drums&r, or &dSuper Tanks&r. Glass Vials are like &9Fluid Cells&r, and are made to store acids. Gold Drums are self-explanatory. Super Tanks can store any fluid without restriction, but are the most expensive."
		""
		"&cWARNING:&r Acids in the wrong pipes will cause &cvoiding&r, &cpipe burning&r, and high chance of &cdeath&r! Be careful!"
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The acid transportation and storage mechanics originate from GregTech 6."
	]
	quest.79C7E780E467D887.quest_subtitle: "...if you don't read this quest."
	quest.79C7E780E467D887.title: "It will Melt Your Flesh"
	quest.79F30AED6544D26B.quest_desc: [
		"&aUnrefined Paper&r is one step away from becoming real, usable &dPaper.&r There are a lot of ways to go about crafting paper, some could be easier to do while others can be considerably more difficult depending on resource availability. Check the &bPapermaking&r entry on your &2Field Guide!&r"
	]
	quest.79F30AED6544D26B.quest_subtitle: "Time to make some history."
	quest.79F30AED6544D26B.title: "Unrefined Paper"
	quest.7A1B344475D8B5C7.quest_desc: [
		"The Pit Kiln is an early game method of heating items up. We'll use it to both fire our clay items, and most importantly, melt very basic ores and create our first metal tool, a Saw."
		""
		"To create a pit kiln you'll need eight pieces of Straw, eight logs, something you want to heat up, and a Firestarter. Read the Field Guide's Pit Kilns section on how to create it - it's not the same as a Fire Pit!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:tfc:textures/gui/book/tutorial/pit_kiln_2.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:tfc:textures/gui/book/tutorial/pit_kiln_3.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:tfc:textures/gui/book/tutorial/pit_kiln_4.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		""
		"{image:tfc:textures/gui/book/tutorial/pit_kiln_5.png width:100 height:100 align:center}"
	]
	quest.7A1B344475D8B5C7.quest_subtitle: "Things are heating up now"
	quest.7A1B344475D8B5C7.title: "Pit Kiln"
	quest.7A75798DC8627620.quest_desc: [
		"Crushes TFC ore pieces into GregTech crushed ore at twice TFC's yield: 5 small, 10 poor, 2 normal or 10 rich pieces give 1, 3, 1 or 7 crushed ores. Mineral and gem ores give 2 each."
		""
		"That's twice what the millstone gives, so it's worth building even next to one. It also grinds crushed ore into impure dust and logs into wood pulp."
		""
		"EMI shows more output slots than you'll get: the steam macerator has one, and byproducts from macerating wait for an &6HV&r macerator."
	]
	quest.7A75798DC8627620.quest_subtitle: "Twice the ore"
	quest.7A75798DC8627620.title: "Steam Macerator"
	quest.7A9A9812D7E48A40.quest_desc: [
		"These are all the products you can make out of Clay. The Molds are used for metal working, the Vessels are used to hold items, and the others have uses explained in the Field Guide. Think you can knap them all?"
	]
	quest.7A9A9812D7E48A40.quest_subtitle: "I told you Clay was versatile."
	quest.7A9A9812D7E48A40.title: "Clay Products"
	quest.7AA2C30E2C07E368.quest_desc: [
		"The Distillery is kind of like a centrifuge, but mostly for organic/petrochemical fluids: one input, one chosen output, picked with a Programmed Circuit. This will change once you get the Distillation Tower."
		""
		"At &7LV&r its handiest job is turning &7Creosote&r from your coke ovens into &eLubricant&r, which the Cutter and other machines can use. Most of its other recipes, such as phenol and toluene from wood tar, need &bMV&r."
	]
	quest.7AA2C30E2C07E368.quest_subtitle: "The distillery distills..."
	quest.7AA2C30E2C07E368.title: "Basic Distillery"
	quest.7AA9D88BC0C8184C.quest_desc: [
		"Red steel first starts as high carbon red steel: weld weak red steel and black steel together, then work it on the anvil into red steel."
	]
	quest.7AA9D88BC0C8184C.quest_subtitle: "Minecraft is not a physics simulator"
	quest.7AA9D88BC0C8184C.title: "Red Steel Ingredients"
	quest.7AB741431A670F31.quest_desc: [
		"The Rock Crusher is basically a cobblestone generator in a box. With lava and water next to it, it makes more of the vanilla cobblestone or stone in its slot (which isn't used up), at the low cost of just a little steam."
		""
		"It only makes vanilla stone, not TFC rock, so this doesn't help at all for progression; its cobblestone can feed the forge hammer if you need vanilla gravel or sand."
	]
	quest.7AB741431A670F31.quest_subtitle: "The Rock Crusher duplicates blocks... wait what?"
	quest.7AB741431A670F31.title: "Steam Rock Crusher"
	quest.7B2E77C455BB1379.quest_desc: [
		"Graphite forms in metamorphic rock: gneiss, marble, quartzite and schist, below y=60."
		""
		"Its veins leave no loose pieces on the surface, so explore caves in those rocks and bring a prospector's pick. A metal shield and a spyglass can prove very useful too."
	]
	quest.7B2E77C455BB1379.quest_subtitle: "You mean I can't just rely on surface indicators?"
	quest.7B2E77C455BB1379.title: "Graphite Source: Overworld"
	quest.7B9DF2A532CA2BD3.quest_desc: [
		"With the wrought iron anvil (tier III) you can work wrought iron ingots into sheets, tool heads and more."
		""
		"Wrought iron sheets are what this pack's heavy machines are made of: Create's mechanical press (a double sheet), saw, harvester and chute, and TFC's blast furnace with its reinforced fire bricks all need them."
		""
		"Wrought iron tools and armour aren't much of an improvement over bronze, but they last far longer. The next anvil is a big step up in difficulty, so this is a good point to settle down and catch up on the rest of your base."
	]
	quest.7B9DF2A532CA2BD3.quest_subtitle: "Sheets for heavy machines"
	quest.7B9DF2A532CA2BD3.title: "T3 Anvil: Wrought Iron"
	quest.7BE9F40DE554360A.quest_desc: [
		"Sticky resin from GregTech's rubber trees goes into a steam extractor for raw rubber; alloy-smelt three raw rubber with one sulfur dust (crush TFC sulfur or pyrite). Create's press turns rubber into plates."
		""
		"Rubber insulates every cable from here on, so it's well worth automating."
	]
	quest.7BE9F40DE554360A.quest_subtitle: "For cables"
	quest.7BE9F40DE554360A.title: "Rubber"
	quest.7C105A9259BD8E39.quest_desc: [
		"Zinc is used in the bronze age for brass (Create's brass, and with it airships) and bismuth bronze, and later in nickel-zinc ferrite for inductors."
		""
		"It can be obtained from TFC sphalerite."
	]
	quest.7C105A9259BD8E39.quest_subtitle: "Element #30"
	quest.7C105A9259BD8E39.title: "Zinc"
	quest.7CFB25CD3E88510C.quest_desc: [
		"&bMolybdenum&r goes into the Large Centrifugal Unit's coils, RTM alloy and several &6EV&r alloys."
		""
		"TFC &aMalachite&r caps copper deposits that also hold &aMolybdenite&r. Run crushed malachite through a &3Thermal Centrifuge&r, or centrifuge pure malachite dust, and molybdenite comes out as the &6Byproduct&r."
		""
		"An &3Electrolyzer&r splits molybdenite dust into &bMolybdenum&r and sulfur."
	]
	quest.7CFB25CD3E88510C.quest_subtitle: "Moly-b-done yet?"
	quest.7CFB25CD3E88510C.title: "Molybdenum Line"
	quest.7D3CA6CE28AD8FE3.quest_desc: [
		"Not much new equipment is available at &7LV&r, but GregTech's &6power tools&r arrive here, and some of them make fine weapons too."
	]
	quest.7D3CA6CE28AD8FE3.title: "&7LV&r"
	quest.7D5FADCDB5BADB79.quest_desc: [
		"In &7LV&r and &bMV&r, you probably built your first batteries from Sodium or Cadmium."
		""
		"But let's be real — these are the weakest batteries GregTech has to offer."
		""
		"Here are the stronger alternatives: the &acrystal batteries&r. The &aEnergium Crystal&r grows in an &6HV&r Autoclave, the &aLapotron Crystal&r is put together in an &5EV&r Assembler. They store way more energy and can help you push your factory to the next tier."
		""
		"Are they more expensive? Of course. But let's be real..."
		"Power is Power. Who's counting?"
	]
	quest.7D5FADCDB5BADB79.quest_subtitle: "Sci-Fi power storage"
	quest.7D5FADCDB5BADB79.title: "Super Batteries"
	quest.7D8B9890952660C3.quest_desc: [
		"The next &3Circuit Assembler&r. This tier is only required for one Circuit: the &aMicroprocessor Mainframe&r, your first &1IV&r Circuit, whose main use is building the &5EV Circuit Assembler&r."
		""
		"You can put this off until &5EV&r or simply just use it for faster circuit making."
	]
	quest.7D8B9890952660C3.quest_subtitle: "You will need the Cleanroom before you can craft this one"
	quest.7D8B9890952660C3.title: "HV Circuit Assembler"
	quest.7DA6CF1025153359.quest_desc: [
		"&aSMD Diodes&r need fine &aPlatinum&r wire and Gallium Arsenide."
		""
		"Platinum comes from the &dPlatinum Group Sludge&r: react purified Tetrahedrite ore with Nitric Acid in a Chemical Reactor, centrifuge the sludge with Aqua Regia, and electrolyze the raw Platinum dust."
		""
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o The SMD Inductors make an appearance in GTCEu for the first time. It's more consistent and convenient to have all Circuit components receive an SMD counterpart."
	]
	quest.7DA6CF1025153359.title: "More SMD Components"
	quest.7E00252CBF0B6958.quest_desc: [
		"Crushing wheels are a 5x5 recipe, so they're built with mechanical crafters. They crush TFC ores into GregTech crushed ore at the macerator's rate, twice TFC's yield: a rich piece gives a crushed ore 70% of the time."
	]
	quest.7E00252CBF0B6958.quest_subtitle: "Ore at GregTech's rate"
	quest.7E00252CBF0B6958.title: "Crushing Wheels"
	quest.7EE655F20A2E0B25.quest_desc: [
		"The &aPortable Scanner&r, or &aTricorder&r, is GTCEu's debug tool."
		""
		"Using it will show you a block's details, the details of the energy network, its current status and contents, and its impact on performance."
		""
		"It'll also display a percentage of fluid remaining in the fluid vein for the &3Fluid Rigs&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&l&3Lore:&r&o This little useful device comes from GregTech 5. It was extremely useful in the early days, because very little information (basically nothing) was given by GUIs or WAILA."
	]
	quest.7EE655F20A2E0B25.quest_subtitle: "For the nosiest GregTech players"
	quest.7EE655F20A2E0B25.title: "Tricorder"
	quest.7EE6592013115B6A.quest_desc: [
		"&aPolyvinyl Chloride (PVC)&r is the 3rd-most produced plastic in real life. Here it can replace Polyethylene in &aPlastic Circuit Boards&r and other items to increase the yield, and from &5EV&r on its foil is one of the ways to insulate cables that rubber can't."
		""
		"PVC item pipes also have the &6highest throughput&r available for a while, but most of your setups right now won't need such speed. Still, it's good to keep this knowledge in your pocket."
	]
	quest.7EE6592013115B6A.quest_subtitle: "You've already made one polymer, what's two?"
	quest.7EE6592013115B6A.title: "Polyvinyl Chloride"
	quest.7F0FE3C6FE7167A2.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Assembler&r is a staple for every Tier; an important goal to unlock more recipes and progress further into the Age. Many in the community see crafting a voltage tier's Assembler as a sign of &oproperly&r reaching said voltage."
		""
		"That being said, welcome to &bMV&r!"
		""
		"The &bMV &3Assembler&r unlocks &eTransistors&r, &eCapacitors&r and &eInductors&r, used for the next tiers of Circuits."
	]
	quest.7F0FE3C6FE7167A2.quest_subtitle: "Assengers, Avemble"
	quest.7F0FE3C6FE7167A2.title: "Advanced Assembler"
	quest.7F4BA01344B10ECF.quest_desc: [
		"Congrats finishing a major milestone of the &bMV Chapter&r."
		""
		"Better &6HV&r Circuits - much &dcheaper&r and easier to make than before."
		""
		"You should now be &aready to move on&r to the HV Chapter, unless you're yet to scale up your Power Production."
	]
	quest.7F4BA01344B10ECF.quest_subtitle: "On that HV grind"
	quest.7F4BA01344B10ECF.title: "More HV Circuits"
	quest.7FBA6A302D462285.quest_desc: [
		"Cast the blast furnace's molten pig iron into ingots. Pig iron is the only way to steel, whether worked on the anvil or refined in GregTech's primitive blast furnace."
	]
	quest.7FBA6A302D462285.quest_subtitle: "On the way to steel"
	quest.7FBA6A302D462285.title: "Pig Iron"
}
